{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if","id":849576,"title":"What Breaks If......","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-18T19:41:28-07:00","id":849576,"title":"What Breaks If......","content":"I've had a couple of weird and pretty game-rearranging ideas lately, which I don't think really rate their own thread, so I'm putting them here instead. Please, bring your own as well.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>What breaks if Infernals bring in their 2e themes of becoming Primordials, but instead of being Essence-based, they're Attribute-based? Lunars were the other splat defined by being (as opposed to Solars doing), and they were Attribute-based, on the basis that Attributes are what you are but Abilities are what you can do. Besides, the existing Charm trees break down fairly easily if you take each Yozi to cover four Attributes, so Infernals favor two Caste Attributes and two of their own. Most of the Green Sun Flare Nimbus stuff goes in Malfean Strength while the By Pain Reforged stuff goes in Malfean Stamina, as opposed to the Transcendent Desert Creature stuff in Cecilian Stamina. There's definitely a little reshuffling involved, though. Also, Shintai/DBT similarities? I'm just saying.</li> <li>What breaks if Sidereal Resplendent Destinies are more like Vancian magic (the less cool Vancian magic as opposed to Exalted sorcery, that is). I mean, one of the criticisms of DND magic is that it feels like Batman's utility belt, but a James Bond utility belt is exactly the feel Sidereals are going for with their closed Charmset already. Let them requisition/pray for uses of Charms or Resplendencies, even if they don't have them, and the Maidens in the form of the GM approve or even suggest them. I think it would be very in theme for a Sidereal circle in the middle of planning a battle to get approved for Efficient Secretary Technique and take it as a hint that they're missing something. This idea has been brought to you by the comic in MOEP Sidereals where they say they've been &quot;all been granted Terminal Sanction&quot;, which doesn't really make sense otherwise but is in all other respects highly enjoyable.</li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T11:56:09-07:00","id":849820,"title":"","content":"I don't think either of these inherently break the game, at least not mechanically. Giving the Sidereals a way to bureaucratically request a magical effect or remove a charm limiter could be pretty cool.<br /> <br /> As for the Infernals, the whole &quot;using Yozi charms&quot; thing needs to die in a radioactive green fire. But basing them on Attributes doesn't seem too bad. It would further emphasize just how different they are from Solars, but maybe that's what you want?<br /> <br /> Possibly the 2e thing could be modified so that the charms resembled the various demons of a given Yozi, which might give them more story oomph.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T12:35:36-07:00","id":849841,"title":"","content":"I don't see much point to making Infernals Attribute-based. Seems like change for the sake of change. What exactly are you hoping to accomplish there?<br /> <br /> Vancian destinies could be cool, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=849820#post849820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Infernals, the whole &quot;using Yozi charms&quot; thing needs to die in a radioactive green fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it doesn't. It was one of the only good things about Infernals. Most of their book was straight-up terrible, remember. The Yozi Charms were the one good thing about them, and they were deservedly loved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T15:06:14-07:00","id":849889,"title":"","content":"Using Charms that change the Yozis is dangerous. Using Charms from the Yozis is cool. In my opinion, at least.<br /> Attribute-based Infernals mostly just make more sense in categorizing Caste Traits, though the 5-of-8 spread in 3e does help with that. At present, and if they keep exact correspondence between Solar and Infernal Caste Abilities, Fiends don't have Stealth. Slayers, whose patron <i>invented dance</i>, don't have Performance, or even Presence. Cecelyne can't write her laws with Linguistics or enact them with Bureaucracy. Also, I think the Solar/Abyssal contrast is a really good one, and that by comparison the Solar/Infernal theme isn't that strong. The whole &quot;decadent corrupted superpower&quot; works just fine for Deathlords, especially if one of the existing ones has more of an interest on worldly (Underworldly?) pleasures and material (immaterial?) wealth. Looking at you, Bishop. Put those seven wangs to use. Then Bishop's deathknights can enjoy the rockstar thing with ghostly cults and baroque soulsteel violins instead of demon cults and Malfean brass electric guitars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T15:33:27-07:00","id":849901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=849889#post849889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using Charms that change the Yozis is dangerous. Using Charms from the Yozis is cool. In my opinion, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much the rub. The problem wasn't the charms themselves. The 2E Infernal Charms were awesome.<br /> <br /> Presenting them as &quot;These are the powers of the Yozi, who are their Charms, and you can change the nature of the Yozi by altering their Charmset&quot; was a misstep. Honestly, keeping them as-is and simply saying &quot;These are the powers of the Yozi, filtered down through the power of Exaltation and expressed through the power of the Infernals&quot;<br /> <br /> So Windborne Stride is an Infernal channeling some of Adorjan's speed into themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T20:26:30-07:00","id":849993,"title":"","content":"Wasn't &quot;change the Yozis by making charms&quot; Fanon though? I mean, I';m pretty sure some devs outright said that you couldn't actually do that.<br /> <br /> I mean-the charms still have to fit the themes of the Yozi, so you can't make a charm or charms that radically changes a given Yozi's personality because any such charms would by definition be against the themes of the Yozi in question-you can't calm down Malfeas because his rage is part of who he is, and likewise you can't make ED less of an antagonistic assholic douche-bag because being that much of a bastard is literally the only definition he has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T21:27:53-07:00","id":850023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=849993#post849993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't &quot;change the Yozis by making charms&quot; Fanon though? I mean, I';m pretty sure some devs outright said that you couldn't actually do that.<br /> <br /> I mean-the charms still have to fit the themes of the Yozi, so you can't make a charm or charms that radically changes a given Yozi's personality because any such charms would by definition be against the themes of the Yozi in question-you can't calm down Malfeas because his rage is part of who he is, and likewise you can't make ED less of an antagonistic assholic douche-bag because being that much of a bastard is literally the only definition he has.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was kind of a consequence of the whole &quot;The Yozi are their charms&quot; thing. Since you could make new charms and those would instantly be incorporated into the Yozi who were portrayed basically as their charms meaning adding a new charm to Yozi was creating a minor change in the Yozi. The idea that you could cause any significant change to a Yozi through the method was pure fanon, but unfortunately it was also very popular due to the portrayal of the Yozi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T21:33:42-07:00","id":850026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=850023#post850023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was kind of a consequence of the whole &quot;The Yozi are their charms&quot; thing. Since you could make new charms and those would instantly be incorporated into the Yozi who were portrayed basically as their charms meaning adding a new charm to Yozi was creating a minor change in the Yozi. The idea that you could cause any significant change to a Yozi through the method was pure fanon, but unfortunately it was also very popular due to the portrayal of the Yozi.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only change I can see being made is &quot;Yozi slowly evolves into better version of said Yozi.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T22:19:04-07:00","id":850034,"title":"","content":"The Yozi are their charms. The Yozi are also their demon souls. The Yozi are also alien individuals.<br /> <br /> The problem is that fans ignored the last two and interpreted the first as: &quot;The Yozi are computer programs, the charms are lines of code, and by making unique charms I can hack into the Ebon Dragon matrix and change his personality.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's something of a strange read on things.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T02:38:44-07:00","id":850067,"title":"","content":"Being able to change a Yozi by embodying their themes in a different direction is the kind of thing Exalted *should* be about.<br /> <br /> It's protagonising; the player has the power to reshape a major NPC.<br /> <br /> It's actually a good social interaction mechanic; you have to take who the Yozi IS and then sideways edge that into them being who you want them to be, step by painful step. (This is much better than &quot;now you like oranges&quot; &quot;now you like me&quot; &quot;I can give you oranges, so now you REALLY like me&quot; &quot;now you like my pet monkey&quot; &quot;my pet monkey can fetch oranges for you, so now you REALLY like my pet monkey&quot; &quot;if I go away, my monkey comes with me, so now you would DIE for me!&quot;)<br /> <br /> It's mythically resonant; 'As below, so above'. The tale of your Slayer-King who overcomes their anger and grief and becomes great again ripples through the world, changing the way things are.<br /> <br /> It's all about the dangers of no take-back-sies; they made their Champions, and now they have to live with the consequences....<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And, frankly, the combination of being both detailed and narrow made any victories wrung from this more *real*. It's a clear path to change, as opposed to &quot;let the GM tell you when you've won&quot;.<br /> <br /> Could it have been done better? Of course. It was coarse and unrefined and the first iteration of something new, of course it needed work. Creating new Yozi Charms should not have been something you could do in downtime by punching water or something, it should have inherently been an IC philosophical debate as well as an OOC philosophical debate, and possibly one that requires you to win over and/or punch out specific bits of their personality that embody different concepts.<br /> <br /> Yozi's as Charms should probably have been structured differently, too, no doubt. I'd've suggested tying each Charm to a Demon (and noted that the death of demon changes the Charms associated with them) thus providing a clear structure (the soul hierarchy!). (This is to avoid cutting out their souls from the picture)<br /> <br /> Or not, there's a lot of ways to adjust things... but so much potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T08:44:26-07:00","id":850138,"title":"","content":"No, it's something the Exalted *can* be about.<br /> <br /> The idea that Exalted *should* be about changing the Yozi (or defeating the Deathlords; or breaking the Great Curse; or any other huge, Creation altering goals) is a second edition mindset I'm glad to see jettisoned. If those are the things Exalted *should* be about, it excludes about 80% of the stories Exalted can tell as well as puts non-Soloriods in the category of 'not really Exalted.' <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's protagonising; the player has the power to reshape a major NPC.<br /> <br /> It's actually a good social interaction mechanic; you have to take who the Yozi IS and then sideways edge that into them being who you want them to be, step by painful step. (This is much better than &quot;now you like oranges&quot; &quot;now you like me&quot; &quot;I can give you oranges, so now you REALLY like me&quot; &quot;now you like my pet monkey&quot; &quot;my pet monkey can fetch oranges for you, so now you REALLY like my pet monkey&quot; &quot;if I go away, my monkey comes with me, so now you would DIE for me!&quot;) </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm not going to support anything that reduces NPCs to trainable pet monkeys.<br /> <br /> I don't care how 'protagonizing' it is to hack the Yozi, if you want to change them, you have to deal with them as individuals, a collection of demonic souls (each with their own thoughts and personality), and a cluster of thematic powers.<br /> <br /> Erembour, Alveua, and Mara don\u2019t conveniently disappear from the setting while you churn out charms to make the Ebon Dragon like oranges.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T09:53:59-07:00","id":850160,"title":"","content":"You can talk about Infernals resonating back to the source of their Essence and changing it, in a freeform way, without the idea of &quot;Yozis automatically learn the Infernals Charms, and taking on these Charms changes them&quot; and all the literal and mechanistic parts of that. (And incidentally in any case, the idea of Yozi Excellencies which completely provided an immutable, unchangeable base to a Yozi did more to negate the idea of the Yozis being changeable than anything else).<br /> <br /> Of course, if you do that, you have to decide whether the Yozis *should* be beings who can grow to the point of being able to be constructive and interesting influences on the world of the setting. I know some people on here have very strong opinions on this (&quot;The Yozis are losers!&quot;, &quot;The Yozis are *not* protagonists, they are failure NPCs, and it's bad for the line if they ever intrude into that place, or if players ever care about giving them any protagonism&quot;, etc.) I'm happy with that being up to individual groups, as much as they want.<br /> <br /> Re the more general idea of Infernals taking on Yozi Charms, walking into a game about a character becoming a world creating many souled god is very different in focus and scale to one where it's about a myth hero. There's no way that theme could remain self contained in Infernals either. Its not so much the Infernals, themselves, who are a minor splat, but about how the expectations of Solar power rescale in the context of them, and must rescale, for Solars to play the role they play in Exalted's mythos (as the mightiest of the Exalted, with the greatest potential).<br /> <br /> That rescaling assumption is, I think, what gave rise to a lot of conversation about Solars as infinite powered superheroes and world creating gods who trivially blow past all in their path without much reference to the action anime and heroic fantasy genres from which the Solars sprung (and which genre emulation, plus a bit of cleverness and deconstruction, is largely the point of Exalted). Even when the mechanics didn't back them up as infinite powered superheroes (without fairly literal and liberal readings of stuff that was OP for their set, exploitation of paranoia combat, etc.).<br /> <br /> A lot of it comes back to the idea that an upper layer of power for the Exalted as a whole is undefined, purposefully so, in a normal Exalted game, except that the Exalted are at least capable of Essence 5. Having the Infernals able to become the Yozis sort of defines the upper layer in ways you can't get away from, in that you have to say &quot;Well, they can go all the way&quot; or you say &quot;They stop short of the Yozis at this carefully defined level&quot;, and wherever that is defined that that feeds back into the Solars who are supposed to be the Infernals peers, and then back to the Celestials who are supposed to be almost at the level of the Solars (enough that they're basically competitive with them in any broad area of conflict, if the underdog), and so on.<br /> <br /> But that's all old ground, anyway.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> To get back to some new ground, re: the main OP point of a version of Sidereals who request all their Charms, and are granted the use of all their Charms, I don't think anything breaks exactly, but I like my Sidereals to feel like the Charms they have are *their* Charms and are expressions of *their* Abilities and *their* Essence and the fruit of *their* understanding of destiny, as Sidereals. Not things they have on loan from the Bureau or have permission to use, like an Alchemical Charm that's just been slotted into them (and maybe they need the experience to understand and use it, but it's not *them*, and it's the property of an Autochthonian state and the work of thaumaturgical genius that stands outside them).<br /> <br /> Also, I guess from a play perspective, if you take Sidereals as all about applying the weird tools you have in a sandbox way (not something I'm totally fixated on as the point of Sidereals, but hey) then drip feeding them a Charm as something they *hint*hint* just happen to need at that time doesn't totally mesh with that. Also what happens with Ronin here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T12:19:17-07:00","id":850217,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's terribly important whether or not the Charms you invent can change the Yozis. Seems unlikely to affect play much one way or the other.<br /> <br /> Whether or not the Charms you use are actually the Charms of the Yozis isn't often directly relevant in play either, but I suspect that changing it might lead you to change some of the best things about the Infernal Charmset.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=849889#post849889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Attribute-based Infernals mostly just make more sense in categorizing Caste Traits, though the 5-of-8 spread in 3e does help with that. At present, and if they keep exact correspondence between Solar and Infernal Caste Abilities, Fiends don't have Stealth. Slayers, whose patron <i>invented dance</i>, don't have Performance, or even Presence. Cecelyne can't write her laws with Linguistics or enact them with Bureaucracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Infernal Castes are bad. A good solution would be to make Infernal Castes better. Changing the whole Charmset paradigm to fix the Caste Ability spread seems like swatting a fly with a hand grenade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T15:48:57-07:00","id":850288,"title":"","content":"They are, in fact, completly throwing out Infernal Castes and redoing them, and also there's not gonna be a &quot;Caste&quot; Yozi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T02:03:06-07:00","id":850455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=850138#post850138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it's something the Exalted *can* be about.<br /> <br /> The idea that Exalted *should* be about changing the Yozi (or defeating the Deathlords; or breaking the Great Curse; or any other huge, Creation altering goals) is a second edition mindset I'm glad to see jettisoned. If those are the things Exalted *should* be about, it excludes about 80% of the stories Exalted can tell as well as puts non-Soloriods in the category of 'not really Exalted.'</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to run a small-scale game of adventurers wandering about killing monsters for loot, your cup overfloweth for options, you didn't need one more option.<br /> <br /> If you think the game should be a bit larger and more epic in scale than <i>that</i>, then you're closer to me on this than you think, because I don't see &quot;hacking Malfeas into being a better person&quot; as a bigger goal than &quot;finessing my nation into becoming a stable local powerhouse with a shot at expanding further&quot;. Both reshape the setting.<br /> <br /> Malfeas is a demon corporation. Compared to nation containing gods, elementals, other Exalted and not actually least of all - other human beings - he's just another organisation/nation/thing, albeit one with a badass background. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, I'm not going to support anything that reduces NPCs to trainable pet monkeys.<br /> <br /> I don't care how 'protagonizing' it is to hack the Yozi, if you want to change them, you have to deal with them as individuals, a collection of demonic souls (each with their own thoughts and personality), and a cluster of thematic powers.<br /> <br /> Erembour, Alveua, and Mara don\u2019t conveniently disappear from the setting while you churn out charms to make the Ebon Dragon like oranges. </div> </div> </div>The &quot;like oranges&quot; rant is about the 3e social influences system. Seriously, it works on EVERYONE - make them like you, your pet monkey, and oranges, and you're most of the way to making them willing to die for you. Compared to that, &quot;the player must OOC justify how this works within a specific set of things and CANNOT just add to it will-nilly&quot; is greatly constrained. If you don't like NPCs being reduced to trainable pet monkeys, welp, *I* didn't write 3e.<br /> <br /> <br /> And yes, Erembour, Aleveua and Mara *shouldn't* disappear from the setting; they should have been part of the process of rewriting the Ebon Dragon. That doesn't mean it was a terrible idea that needed to be burned out at the root, it means it needed some work; like many 2e things, it had poor mechanics and concepts mixed in among the good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T15:58:39-07:00","id":867886,"title":"","content":"3e What Breaks If: I make global changes to reset conditions<br /> <br /> Note: I have not gone through the rules with a fine tooth comb. I am just in the midst of the charm section now (on an old Kobo so I cannot search or flip through sections easily).<br /> <br /> <b>3 Reset States</b><br /> <br /> <b>Scene</b>: All scene or shorter reset conditions get lumped into this category (I realize this makes many powers one fight only)<br /> <b>Day</b>: Everything between a scene and a day (this is the middle dumping zone)<br /> <b>Story</b>: Everything from day to story reset gets chucked here (not sure how much stuff this would really effect)<br /> <br /> I am hoping nothing really breaks since this would make reset tracking much easier. Gayo's idea of a mortgage side on charm cards is a backup plan but it has been my experience that players do not track past health and willpower; motes, arete, rage, blood, etc., tend to be mostly ignored (people start off diligent but get tired of paying attention).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","name":"Major","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar977_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T16:14:50-07:00","id":867893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Major</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=867886#post867886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3e What Breaks If: I make global changes to reset conditions<br /> <br /> Note: I have not gone through the rules with a fine tooth comb. I am just in the midst of the charm section now (on an old Kobo so I cannot search or flip through sections easily).<br /> <br /> <b>3 Reset States</b><br /> <br /> <b>Scene</b>: All scene or shorter reset conditions get lumped into this category (I realize this makes many powers one fight only)<br /> <b>Day</b>: Everything between a scene and a day (this is the middle dumping zone)<br /> <b>Story</b>: Everything from day to story reset gets chucked here (not sure how much stuff this would really effect)<br /> <br /> I am hoping nothing really breaks since this would make reset tracking much easier. Gayo's idea of a mortgage side on charm cards is a backup plan but it has been my experience that players do not track past health and willpower; motes, arete, rage, blood, etc., tend to be mostly ignored (people start off diligent but get tired of paying attention).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if your group doesn't like the options presented in the book, then this set of reset conditions is probably fine. But what breaks is that it removes strategy options for players that DO keep track of those finer details of the flow of combat and want to make use of them. Your mileage may vary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T20:29:13-07:00","id":868111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=867893#post867893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well if your group doesn't like the options presented in the book, then this set of reset conditions is probably fine. But what breaks is that it removes strategy options for players that DO keep track of those finer details of the flow of combat and want to make use of them. Your mileage may vary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I figured give the option for people which way they'd rather play. I will end up using the more abstracted systems for NPC's, but that likely will not really matter until the DB book comes out anyway since it is not like the characters will be fighting [m]any other Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","name":"Major","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar977_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T20:38:20-07:00","id":868122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=850160#post850160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To get back to some new ground, re: the main OP point of a version of Sidereals who request all their Charms, and are granted the use of all their Charms, I don't think anything breaks exactly, but I like my Sidereals to feel like the Charms they have are *their* Charms and are expressions of *their* Abilities and *their* Essence and the fruit of *their* understanding of destiny, as Sidereals. Not things they have on loan from the Bureau or have permission to use, like an Alchemical Charm that's just been slotted into them (and maybe they need the experience to understand and use it, but it's not *them*, and it's the property of an Autochthonian state and the work of thaumaturgical genius that stands outside them).<br /> <br /> Also, I guess from a play perspective, if you take Sidereals as all about applying the weird tools you have in a sandbox way (not something I'm totally fixated on as the point of Sidereals, but hey) then drip feeding them a Charm as something they *hint*hint* just happen to need at that time doesn't totally mesh with that. Also what happens with Ronin here?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it works fine and could be really fun and cool to have Sidereal Charms explicitly be like tools you requisition. Definitely more like Alchemicals. Which probably means if you make Sidereal Charms slottable it's going to complicate things, because Alchemical Charm slot stuff felt way more complicated than normal Exalted Charms to me.<br /> <br /> I've had no trouble going the other way; opening the Sidereal Charmset and allowing custom Charms all over the place. As long as you keep them sorta weird and stick to the trees' themes, you're golden.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Major</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=867886#post867886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3e What Breaks If: I make global changes to reset conditions<br /> <br /> Note: I have not gone through the rules with a fine tooth comb. I am just in the midst of the charm section now (on an old Kobo so I cannot search or flip through sections easily).<br /> <br /> <b>3 Reset States</b><br /> <br /> <b>Scene</b>: All scene or shorter reset conditions get lumped into this category (I realize this makes many powers one fight only)<br /> <b>Day</b>: Everything between a scene and a day (this is the middle dumping zone)<br /> <b>Story</b>: Everything from day to story reset gets chucked here (not sure how much stuff this would really effect)<br /> <br /> I am hoping nothing really breaks since this would make reset tracking much easier. Gayo's idea of a mortgage side on charm cards is a backup plan but it has been my experience that players do not track past health and willpower; motes, arete, rage, blood, etc., tend to be mostly ignored (people start off diligent but get tired of paying attention).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been playing an investigator with Divine Induction Technique, which is a full free Investigation Excellency with a recent of one scene or if you succeed a diff (Investigation - 1) or higher Investigation roll. And let me tell you, if you removed the extra reset condition, that Charm becomes way worse. Being able to chain difficult Investigation rolls by smashing them down again and again with max-excellency rolls isn't something I'd want to remove.<br /> <br /> Frankly most of the time the reset conditions aren't hard to track at the Essence 1-2 range since you just don't have that many Charms, and few of them probably have reset conditions in the first place. And I think they're optional anyway; most reset on their own at end of scene or whatever besides, so if you don't want to deal with them you don't have to.<br /> <br /> For NPCs I'd totally use that simplified reset system, if I was tracking Charms that closely at all (which I usually don't).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T00:32:50-07:00","id":868247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Major</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=867886#post867886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3e What Breaks If: I make global changes to reset conditions</div> </div> </div> </div> Pretty much everything. Well, not quite everything, but an amazingly large number of things. There's a lot of 1/scene charms that are intended to be used substantially more often than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10881-anasurimbor","name":"Anasurimbor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T02:28:09-07:00","id":868282,"title":"","content":"I read 2e Infernals waaaay back when. I think I must've forgotten most of it back then as most discussions about it passed over my head and no-one I played with was the slightest bit interested in them. I don't think they ever even featured in the campaigns I ran.<br /> <br /> Following the revelations of just how &quot;Ick&quot; the fluff was in places I took to re-reading the 2e Infernals fatsplat (And Malfeas) whilst I was waiting for the E3 backer copy to drop.<br /> <br /> I don't particularly like the charms of the Infernals or how they're arrived at - Every Exalt type has typically quite discrete powers and Charms that escalate. Infernals on the other hand had &quot;thematic&quot; powers that you could use if you could just wrangle the GM to nod and say &quot;OK ... I guess ... that applies?&quot;. They were, to my mind, an abysmal mess of fudges, min-max twink powers. I'd go so far as to say I hate them and hope they die in a green fire.<br /> <br /> But reading them I never once thought &quot;Yay! I can create my own Charms and back-door them into being new aspects/intimacies of the Yozi and thus mess about with the infernal big-wigs!&quot;. I did come up with some specific new Charms that were applicable to certain Yozis and the like but were a lot more specific than the type in the book. But Yozi-hacking via custom Charms? No. It's not protagonizing - it's antagonizing arguably the most potent beings who exist ... the ones who, before being ganked into a side dimension, created Creation. I suspect they'd know if someone suddenly tried making them nice and squishy. I also suspect they'd react, very, very badly and quite painfully to said source of hacking!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/907-jay","name":"Jay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T09:49:49-07:00","id":868506,"title":"","content":"What are your thoughts on Sidereals? It seems to me they've got most of the problems you describe and their drawback of &quot;no custom Charms&quot; isn't a huge drawback for you, so I'm curious if there's anything you feel they have over Infernals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T02:58:41-07:00","id":869197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=868506#post868506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are your thoughts on Sidereals? It seems to me they've got most of the problems you describe and their drawback of &quot;no custom Charms&quot; isn't a huge drawback for you, so I'm curious if there's anything you feel they have over Infernals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm tempted to bring in your signature on the response, provide a nice sultry reply ... but I'll resist!<br /> <br /> Sidereals - Love the type, their setup and fluff, history and style. Somewhat more of a headache than the easy-to-grok Exalt types (Being Solars, Lunars, DBs, Alchies, Abyssals) but not so bad as the GSPs or Raksha (Which in another thread in about 3 replies I suddenly &quot;got&quot; vs re-reading the GWM book numerous times!).<br /> <br /> The implementation of them is something I generally use as a GM fiat/plot device. Again I've never had a player either face-to-face or other the internet in the PBP games express an interest in playing one or even including them in background. I generally bring them in as NPCs to give something (Item/plot/advice) or such things. In terms of their powers/charmsets - I think, IIRC, I liked many of their Charms even if they were a little woolier and free-form compared to the easy-to-grok types. Their powers were, again IIRC, not as defined and discrete as the other types but gave a little wiggle room in how to apply them and, importantly, what they actually did.<br /> <br /> For me - just to explain - I relate things back to an in-setting mindset. If I read &quot;Charm X&quot; my first thought is; what does it actually do? Easier to hit someone? Dodge in flashy strobe-like effect? Summon an essence weapon? Make me understand languages? That sort of thing. Then I think - What does this actually look like to the character and bystanders. Then - How does it actually DO the thing it's doing? Then - probably the last thing - I look at the numbers/rolls/mechanics thing it actually does.<br /> <br /> Which is odd as I'm largely a simulationist type player who loves the numbers side and wants systems/mechanics/support for everything someone does IC! Hence why I'm not a huge fan of things like FATE and SW either - far too fuzzy for me.<br /> <br /> Confused? That's probably why I don't get some things some times. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Take for instance Resplendent Destinies. Took me several reads to get that they're fake identities that everyone believes for a short time. That's it - but the wordyness of their actual explanation when I first read it made me wonder how Sideral X, who's supposedly instantly forgettable due to Curse, can be remembered and function and do things. It's because he's playing at being a Baker and it's just that everyone around him kind of just accepts it whilst he's playing at it. Boom. Instantly got it. <br /> <br /> tl:dr For siddies - Not really read them in a long time, don't recall any massive issues but took a bit to grok at the time, mostly reference splats and inspiration from fluff sort of thing. Really should work on memory and having better recall of the vast amounts of powers and stuff like you other fans. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/907-jay","name":"Jay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T10:58:42-07:00","id":870354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=868122#post868122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been playing an investigator with Divine Induction Technique, which is a full free Investigation Excellency with a recent of one scene or if you succeed a diff (Investigation - 1) or higher Investigation roll. And let me tell you, if you removed the extra reset condition, that Charm becomes way worse. Being able to chain difficult Investigation rolls by smashing them down again and again with max-excellency rolls isn't something I'd want to remove.<br /> Frankly most of the time the reset conditions aren't hard to track at the Essence 1-2 range since you just don't have that many Charms, and few of them probably have reset conditions in the first place. And I think they're optional anyway; most reset on their own at end of scene or whatever besides, so if you don't want to deal with them you don't have to.<br /> For NPCs I'd totally use that simplified reset system, if I was tracking Charms that closely at all (which I usually don't).</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anasurimbor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=868247#post868247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Pretty much everything. Well, not quite everything, but an amazingly large number of things. There's a lot of 1/scene charms that are intended to be used substantially more often than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, good catches. I was mostly afraid of the finicky &quot;when an X has done 10 decisive damage reset this charm&quot; and the like powers. Knowing there are bigger, easier to track, but important scene charms is important.<br /> Maybe what I will do then is make sure anyone with a charm that uses reset rules has a charm card with a mortgage side. That way the player has the onus of tracking the reset condition and if they fail to do so I'll use my reset rules as a backup to make sure everyone's abilities get reset eventually.<br /> This doesn't really help with story charm resetting but that is going to be an issue in either case.<br /> <br /> [conspiritual musings]<br /> I am kinda suspicious that some of these rules were designed as such to make easier flow into a future CRPG product (that's what they seem like to me). If that is the case, chop chop, get it made!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","name":"Major","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar977_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T11:51:31-07:00","id":870411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=868122#post868122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it works fine and could be really fun and cool to have Sidereal Charms explicitly be like tools you requisition. Definitely more like Alchemicals. Which probably means if you make Sidereal Charms slottable it's going to complicate things, because Alchemical Charm slot stuff felt way more complicated than normal Exalted Charms to me.<br /> <br /> I've had no trouble going the other way; opening the Sidereal Charmset and allowing custom Charms all over the place. As long as you keep them sorta weird and stick to the trees' themes, you're golden.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since this is LimitedReagent of LimitedReagent's Sidereals Charms fame, I can't be as negative towards the idea as I was. I think if I think of it as characters who have lots of Astrology (where and Astrology just goes higher than in the existing systems, and is rooted more in your enlightenment than your schmoozing skills), then I feel less negative towards it. <br /> <br /> I think it's the semantics and situational differences from the Alchemicals do it that bugs me about the idea, particularly having to play bureaucracy to use Charms. Compare Alchemicals, and they are generally set up so that they like their states and their states like them, and will give them the tools they need to be the heroes of the state, which they're applauded as being, publicly. The people who build and maintain their Charms *want* the Charms to be used. Sidereals have a more antagonistic and secretive relationship with the bureaucracy and their elders. So there's different feel around that. You could get strong drift to ideas where the elders and gods are deeply mistrustful of PC Sidereals and are very carefully managing what power they have access to, and it seems like a negative experience. (Paperwork simulator, meet mistrustful and micromanaging boss simulator).<br /> <br /> Plus, Alchemical Charms are very physically visceral. Having to request and install them has that analogy to being an fighter pilot, or a mecha ace. For Sidereals, I don't know. More like having to get permission to use your own power, because you're not trusted with it.<br /> <br /> And then you could add to it the kind of invidious comparison to other Exalted (Solar and Lunars, really) that I could see cropping up, contrasting people who earn their own power through skill and effort and &quot;deserve&quot; it against people who are undeservingly given power as a privilege by a corrupt Heaven.<br /> <br /> They wouldn't quite by *my* Sidereals I guess, whose power comes from their own internal enlightenment. I kind of feel like if I did want to build a Sidereal under that system, I'd totally just immediately want to make a b-line for Martial Arts and Sorcery, and not actually want to get most Ability Charms, because they wouldn't be representing the kind of internal skill and learning that I would be looking for out of Sidereals. Only when I had that kind of baseline established that the character was awesome through his own learning and enlightenment would I then want to buy into powers that are granted by Heaven. (Assuming they wouldn't have to weave the ability to use Martial Arts and Sorcery into their destiny, here).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T13:06:01-07:00","id":870513,"title":"","content":"You're right, it very much does change how Sidereals feel. Getting charms would invoke more james bond getting gadgets from Q as well as pull more off of spy thrillers in how distrust amongst allies seems to abound.<br /> <br /> It'd be different, not even my kind of thing really, but still could be cool and fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T13:47:53-07:00","id":870579,"title":"","content":"I mean, you don't need permission to access your own power. Astrology would just let you give permission for someone else to access your Charms, or prepare yourself to use them later, and sometimes as a pretty fringe benefit let you access someone else's Charms.<br /> There definitely is a different feel around internal enlightenment versus that granted by the Maidens, though. Maybe I have different connotations because I'm religious in real life and don't mind getting things from Heaven, as it were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T14:05:50-07:00","id":870605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Major</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=867886#post867886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3e What Breaks If: I make global changes to reset conditions<br /> <br /> Note: I have not gone through the rules with a fine tooth comb. I am just in the midst of the charm section now (on an old Kobo so I cannot search or flip through sections easily).<br /> <br /> <b>3 Reset States</b><br /> <br /> <b>Scene</b>: All scene or shorter reset conditions get lumped into this category (I realize this makes many powers one fight only)<br /> <b>Day</b>: Everything between a scene and a day (this is the middle dumping zone)<br /> <b>Story</b>: Everything from day to story reset gets chucked here (not sure how much stuff this would really effect)<br /> <br /> I am hoping nothing really breaks since this would make reset tracking much easier. Gayo's idea of a mortgage side on charm cards is a backup plan but it has been my experience that players do not track past health and willpower; motes, arete, rage, blood, etc., tend to be mostly ignored (people start off diligent but get tired of paying attention).</div> </div> </div> </div>For everything other than scene-length, it's not going to cause any real mechanical imbalance, even though you do lose out on some of the more flavorful reset conditions. Reset conditions largely exist to prevent powerful effects form being spammed over and over, and it shouldn't be too hard for you to come up with something comparable. <br /> <br /> For things that can be reset within the same scene you use them, this would be a downgrade, with the exact severity depending on how easy that Charm was to reset originally. I'd consider implementing some kind of low-maintenance, universal way for resetting them, like stunts of a certain level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T21:29:43-07:00","id":870917,"title":"","content":"What breaks if you just cut out excellencies, so that nobody gets them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T23:28:02-07:00","id":872156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=870917#post870917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if you just cut out excellencies, so that nobody gets them?</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of versatility, getting the Excellency free in your Caste/Favored does a lot to broaden your starting power. My Dawn doesn't need to buy Ride Charms to cover for the edge cases where he needs to be really good at controlling a horse. <br /> <br /> The basic source of Charm dice and pretty much the brunt of low-Essence Solar power. I can build a kickass swordsman with only a couple of Melee charms, IF one of them is the Excellency. From my read-through, there are very few low-Essence dice adders (if any); mostly dice tricks, which are more effective in a larger pool.Excellent Strike, for example, is much more efficient in a larger pool where 1s are more likely to show up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T23:37:36-07:00","id":872162,"title":"","content":"Dice-adding charms get much, much better, as do Defence-increasing charms.<br /> <br /> For example, Harmonious Presence Meditation becomes a really good dice adder that all social characters will want, rather than just a way to reduce your mote costs in scenes with a lot of social attacks.<br /> <br /> Arguably this is a good thing.<br /> <br /> It also gives MA a big advantage over Melee and Dodge, because Melee and Dodge don't have a lot of charms to boost your Defence (they don't need to, they have excellencies), whereas there are a fair few MA charms that do stuff like give you +2 Evasion or whatever.<br /> <br /> Also, all non-Exalts become more threatening against Exalts.<br /> <br /> Arguably this is also a good thing.<br /> <br /> Basically, it's another thing where I don't think the game breaks as such, but it definitely makes some stuff better and other stuff worse.<br /> <br /> There are a few charms that you'd need to fiddle with since they do stuff relating to excellencies, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T02:06:06-07:00","id":872221,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of a sid being able to temporarily do stuff he normally can't via a prayer request - it makes for a potential fun game of getting dirt on the gods who grant such power, perhaps to get greater temp buffs, or to deny such to a rival sidereal.<br /> <br /> &quot;Sorry, but your request for divine power cannot be granted - because your rival has a recorder of everlasting glories full of holograms with me doing the nasty with a goat that's done up with makeup and lingerie&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T05:43:13-07:00","id":872297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=870917#post870917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if you just cut out excellencies, so that nobody gets them?</div> </div> </div> </div>You lose the baseline ability, as a player, to decide when a roll is important and when it's not; when you really want to succeed, and when you're okay with failure. A WP for success doesn't go far. When you start adding in Charms, they allow you to make that decision again, but it takes a lot more Charm investment to get to that point.<br /> <br /> I don't think it breaks anything besides maybe really high-level combat, since fighting a Solar-equivalent with a persistent Defense of 7 becomes very difficult to even hit without being able to throw an Excellency down every so often.<br /> <br /> Besides that it's fine, but as the Wizard of Oz said, it does vastly change the worth of dice-adder and dice-trick Charms. Especially those &quot;add a full free excellency&quot; once-per scene Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T07:05:36-07:00","id":872328,"title":"","content":"What breaks if I make it so excellencies apply to any Attribute + Ability combo, and not just Caste/Favored abilities or abilities you've bought a charm in?<br /> <br /> What breaks if I give excellencies the Mute keyword?<br /> <br /> What breaks if I combine the above?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T07:26:03-07:00","id":872348,"title":"","content":"1) Very little. It just means that PCs have no real weaknesses, just things they're merely not that great at. I mean, every single Exalt will suddenly become as good at sailing as your avereage sailor. Maybe that's not something you want. But it's not very significant in terms of game balance, it's more of a thematic thing.<br /> Oh, actually, one effect is it no longer encourages PCs to buy charms in lots of abilities.<br /> <br /> 2) You remove one of the main reasons stopping people spamming excellencies outside combat.<br /> <br /> 3) Just the above two effects, there's not really a compound effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T07:29:28-07:00","id":872352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=872328#post872328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I make it so excellencies apply to any Attribute + Ability combo, and not just Caste/Favored abilities or abilities you've bought a charm in?</div> </div> </div> </div>In general, you'll inflate the average success even further (and encourage diversity of abilities) and discourage purchase of non-caste/favored charms for an excellency (and thus discourage the diversity of charms.)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What breaks if I give excellencies the Mute keyword? </div> </div> </div>You remove the single biggest factor <i>towards</i> Anima. Even if you think this is a good thing, you're nerfing any charm that runs on Anima effects as well as the Bonfire anima effects.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What breaks if I combine the above? </div> </div> </div>Mostly the above.<br /> <br /> I know that sounds weird that I think you'll simultaneously encourage and discourage diversity, but keep in mind that different players will react differently to the change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8907-scarecrowj","name":"ScarecrowJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T07:46:41-07:00","id":872357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ScarecrowJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=872352#post872352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, you'll inflate the average success even further (and encourage diversity of abilities) and discourage purchase of non-caste/favored charms for an excellency (and thus discourage the diversity of charms.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. I'm more interested in increasing player options, so i'd consider this a net win.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ScarecrowJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=872352#post872352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You remove the single biggest factor <i>towards</i> Anima. Even if you think this is a good thing, you're nerfing any charm that runs on Anima effects as well as the Bonfire anima effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>This might not be as big of an issue as it seems mostly because of a few other tweaks I was thinking of making, but lets get some feedback on those as well:<br /> <br /> What breaks if I combine personal and peripheral mote pools in to one big pool? In addition, what breaks if I make it so anima flairs only if character do &quot;impossible&quot; actions, such as curing the plague with a touch, or blocking a lightning bolt thrown by a dragon-blooded? Stunting, naturally, can alleviate or exaggerate what counts as &quot;impossible.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 04-23-2016, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T07:55:13-07:00","id":872365,"title":"","content":"So, basically making flaring a lot less common? Essentially, the PCs will throw their full power at far more stuff. So the regular stuff in the game (ie not giant boss battles or such) will be easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T08:06:11-07:00","id":872371,"title":"","content":"More like making it so flaring is something that PCs have more control over. They can either go nuts and stunt all their actions as being impossible, or give me creative descriptions as to why their impossible action doesn't flair their anima.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T08:48:07-07:00","id":872407,"title":"","content":"Ah, okay.<br /> Well, that's basically the same effect. Previously, they wouldn't want to throw their whole power around in most sessions because of the danger of giving themselves away as Anathema. Now they can.<br /> <br /> So, it depends really on how you feel about the PCs doing that. If you're happy for them to be spending more motes in most scenes (and about the same in big dramatic scenes, where they'd likely flare anyway because it's better than being eaten by a demon prince), then it's not a problem. If not, then it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T10:35:29-07:00","id":872483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=872371#post872371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More like making it so flaring is something that PCs have more control over. They can either go nuts and stunt all their actions as being impossible, or give me creative descriptions as to why their impossible action doesn't flair their anima.</div> </div> </div> </div>You end up with a Creation where only Solars who WANT to be noticed by Dragon-Blooded get noticed, unless they're being particularly silly about it. There becomes almost no way for DBs to easily identify Solars and Wyld Hunts either become much less frequent, or much MORE frequent as wild accusation becomes just as valid as proof. &quot;Better safe than sorry!&quot;<br /> <br /> If your story doesn't care about hiding from the Realm, then this isn't really broken for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T12:31:18-07:00","id":872595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=870917#post870917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if you just cut out excellencies, so that nobody gets them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gonna break from the crowd here and say a lot breaks. A bunch of ordinary Charms suddenly become incredibly powerful, Exalts are suddenly no better than mortals a lot of the time, spirits and the like become a lot more threatening, the math on everything that uses extended rolls becomes ridiculous, and one of the major distinguishing features between splats fades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T12:41:37-07:00","id":872598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=870605#post870605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*snip* Reset conditions largely exist to prevent powerful effects form being spammed over and over, and it shouldn't be too hard for you to come up with something comparable.<br /> ...I'd consider implementing some kind of low-maintenance, universal way for resetting them, like stunts of a certain level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I like this. A very straightforward addition with little accounting and works with the mortgage side of charm cards very well. It also encourages players to attempt grander stunts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","name":"Major","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar977_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T10:33:22-07:00","id":873170,"title":"","content":"If I remove non-flurry extra attacks.<br /> <br /> I was happy seeing the baseline extra attack charms of this edition gone. At least I thought they were gone until Irked pointed out (GM manual progression: Charm build combos) that with Melee you could (at Essence 1) have a 15 attack combo.<br /> <br /> I, just, no. <br /> <br /> Celerity was always the one discipline in VtM that made other players groan and I really don't want to have to sit through that again. You may say that it is mote constrained and that is the limiter. True, and that still does not make it fun for the other players to be sitting there waiting for them to finish their 15 attacks whenever they get in the mood to do so.<br /> <br /> Anyone have a way to completely excise non-flurry extra attacks? I'm hoping someone has already thought of ways around the extra attack issue that doesn't horribly break the rest of the games mechanics or the charm trees. The best I can see is to have extra attack charms simply negate the flurry penalty and then have those charms have limiters on use. But I'm terrible with mechanics so that may not be a great idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","name":"Major","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar977_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T19:39:15-07:00","id":873475,"title":"","content":"Since they're pretty much all charms and thus optional, just don't take them, don't let your PCs take them and don't give them to NPCs. That should be fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T19:54:35-07:00","id":873481,"title":"","content":"What breaks if you ignore the Brawl requirement for the Martial Arts Merit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T20:10:21-07:00","id":873487,"title":"","content":"Not much... but.<br /> Most people who are going to buy Martial Arts are people who favour Martial Arts. You get favouring Martial Arts by favouring Brawl. If you favour Brawl, unless you're a Dawn, you need to put a dot in it anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T20:10:41-07:00","id":873488,"title":"","content":"Nothing breaks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T20:39:56-07:00","id":873504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=873487#post873487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not much... but.<br /> Most people who are going to buy Martial Arts are people who favour Martial Arts. You get favouring Martial Arts by favouring Brawl. If you favour Brawl, unless you're a Dawn, you need to put a dot in it anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah! That makes sense to me. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T21:41:37-07:00","id":873527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=873481#post873481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if you ignore the Brawl requirement for the Martial Arts Merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on my experience, players will cheat themselves out of going up to Brawl 3 in order to get Thunderclap Rush Attack. Even nerfed, it's still hella good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T23:12:09-07:00","id":873553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=873527#post873527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on my experience, players will cheat themselves out of going up to Brawl 3 in order to get Thunderclap Rush Attack. Even nerfed, it's still hella good.</div> </div> </div> </div>From my reading, you can use it to basically take your turn early, so... yeah. Crucial!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T00:11:29-07:00","id":873573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=873527#post873527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on my experience, players will cheat themselves out of going up to Brawl 3 in order to get Thunderclap Rush Attack. Even nerfed, it's still hella good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention Iron Battle Focus is also at Brawl 3, one of the most efficient Onslaught negator in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T09:10:54-07:00","id":873809,"title":"","content":"What breaks if you allow for sizes greater than 5 in battle groups?<br /> <br /> One of the issues I'm running into is that battle groups aren't having the staying-power against my players that I was hoping for. Considering playing with higher Size attributes, and changing the mapping between the Size trait and number of people in the Battle Group. This would give large battle groups a bit more punch in terms of bonuses, without needing to narratively justify why this particular group of bandits has the population of a small-ish city. Just can't see if there are any major pitfalls to doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4115-flumpet38","name":"flumpet38","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T09:39:29-07:00","id":873831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=873573#post873573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention Iron Battle Focus is also at Brawl 3, one of the most efficient Onslaught negator in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't work with anything but Brawl Parry.<br /> <br /> Wind and Stones Defense has to specifically say it can be used with (Dodged-based) Evasion, and the compatibility rules still prohibit that one from working with any MA-based Parry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T09:42:25-07:00","id":873832,"title":"","content":"What breaks if I make it easier to get more shaping rituals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T10:10:37-07:00","id":873848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=873832#post873832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I make it easier to get more shaping rituals?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Depends on how many. Effectively, at some point you have people stunting the combination of multiple rituals to blast of Flight of the Brilliant Raptor on round 1 for free, or storing up sorcerous motes until they're ready to unleash hell. So basically, it should remain as expensive as it is now, even if you lower the RP requirement, or at least not substantially cheaper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T10:14:33-07:00","id":873850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=873831#post873831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't work with anything but Brawl Parry.<br /> <br /> Wind and Stones Defense has to specifically say it can be used with (Dodged-based) Evasion, and the compatibility rules still prohibit that one from working with any MA-based Parry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you thinking of a different charm? Iron Battle Focus is a Reflexive charm that makes you immune to onslaught penalties. It doesn't create an action or enhance a static value.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/513-gatts","name":"Gatts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar513_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T11:14:25-07:00","id":873883,"title":"","content":"Onslaught penalties apply to static values.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T11:21:43-07:00","id":873892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=873883#post873883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Onslaught penalties apply to static values.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many things in the system do. However the charm doesn't boost the static value, it prevents you from taking a penalty. Unless there's a quote from the developers that I haven't seen then I'll be using rules as written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/513-gatts","name":"Gatts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar513_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T12:29:58-07:00","id":873953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=873831#post873831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't work with anything but Brawl Parry.<br /> <br /> Wind and Stones Defense has to specifically say it can be used with (Dodged-based) Evasion, and the compatibility rules still prohibit that one from working with any MA-based Parry.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you that the wording is ambiguous, I'll see if I can get t a dev to chime in on this forum and on rpg.net.<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T16:27:40-07:00","id":874981,"title":"","content":"What breaks if you let a player do lethal damage with a specially-crafted shield? (Artifact, razor edges/spikes on the front)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T17:00:57-07:00","id":875008,"title":"","content":"Nothing breaks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T17:45:48-07:00","id":875047,"title":"","content":"Your enemy's skeleton breaks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T22:33:02-07:00","id":875310,"title":"","content":"What breaks if you allow pole-axes with White Reaper Style?<br /> <br /> (Nothing, I think, since they're not mechanically or realistically much different from war scythes.)<br /> <br /> BUT. What breaks if you allow a pole-HAMMER?<br /> <br /> (Nora Valkyrie spinning her melon-on-a-pole around her neck in &quot;Best Day Ever&quot; was TOTALLY Revolving Crescent Defense!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T09:53:48-07:00","id":876749,"title":"","content":"What breaks if I apply the restriction that Flow Like Blood has to Fivefold Bulwark Stance, namely, that for the penalty negation to work your initiative must be higher than your attacker's?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/356-nonamemaddoxx","name":"nonamemaddoxx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar356_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T10:06:19-07:00","id":876763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nonamemaddoxx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=876749#post876749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I apply the restriction that Flow Like Blood has to Fivefold Bulwark Stance, namely, that for the penalty negation to work your initiative must be higher than your attacker's?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your melee player becomes hideously over defensive and tries to find ways of dealing decisive damage without resetting (I forget if Melee has any charms for that, but I know Brawl has one in its clash tree).<br /> <br /> Melee players become even more likely to hoard initiative until they can smash someone to death in a single OHKO. Melee stops being the charmset best equipped to fight multiple enemies at once, or at least loses the biggest reason it was good at fighting multiple enemies. Melee players will probably still use it to boost dipping swallow and bulwark stance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur","name":"Grindavikur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T11:44:34-07:00","id":876831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=875310#post875310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if you allow pole-axes with White Reaper Style?<br /> <br /> (Nothing, I think, since they're not mechanically or realistically much different from war scythes.)<br /> <br /> BUT. What breaks if you allow a pole-HAMMER?<br /> <br /> (Nora Valkyrie spinning her melon-on-a-pole around her neck in &quot;Best Day Ever&quot; was TOTALLY Revolving Crescent Defense!)</div> </div> </div> </div>Since Smashing is scarier than Piercing or Chopping, White Reaper would probably get a little scarier. Ironically, the extra scariness wouldn't help against battle groups.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't call it broken, but I'm not sure it's desirable. I'd probably rather use scythe stats for the hammer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T13:28:51-07:00","id":876917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=876831#post876831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Smashing is scarier than Piercing or Chopping, White Reaper would probably get a little scarier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe White Reaper Charms remain incompatible with Smashing attacks even if they become compatible with pole-hammers?<br /> <br /> Or maybe the solution is just to copy Resolving Crescent Defense into a pole-hammer Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T13:53:56-07:00","id":876935,"title":"","content":"I think Ivory Pestle in 2e is suitable if you're looking for something to convert.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T19:35:17-07:00","id":879850,"title":"","content":"How does combat balance change (or break) if shields allowed you, in some circumstances, to negate onslaught penalties by spending initiative? I'd like some way to make shields useful in a broader array of circumstances.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head, you'd probably want to restrict the circumstances for that combat trick to something like non-flurried Full Defense actions, and require the player to have positive initiative. If you can use shields to negate onslaught while flurried with a Rush or Defend Other action, then shields seem kind of broken in those circumstances. Likewise, if you could keep digging yourself deeper into negative initiative after being crashed, there's little reason not to turtle up behind a shield and continually negate onslaught for the 3 rounds required to reset to base initiative.<br /> <br /> Even then, I have no idea how much that sort of effect should cost. Maybe 1i, plus an additional 1i for each previous attack since the end of your last turn? So the first attack would cost 1i to negate, the second would cost 2i, the third 3i, etc. Basically, I'd like a way for a character (or battlegroup) that realizes s/he's outmatched to hunker down for a non-indefinite period of time, probably while screaming for help from nearby allies or frantically trying to talk their assailants","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4741-greymatterpimp","name":"greymatterpimp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T12:10:11-07:00","id":883961,"title":"","content":"What breaks if I allow ranged weapons to be used with melee to parry, particularly artifact versions of these?<br /> <br /> It feels weird to have a mostly unbreakable piece of metal in your hand that you can't block an incoming attack with, even if it's not well made for that purpose. You'd give it a -1 or -2 Defense adjuster and still have to use your Melee ability score, but what else breaks?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T13:39:54-07:00","id":884034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=883961#post883961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I allow ranged weapons to be used with melee to parry, particularly artifact versions of these?<br /> <br /> It feels weird to have a mostly unbreakable piece of metal in your hand that you can't block an incoming attack with, even if it's not well made for that purpose. You'd give it a -1 or -2 Defense adjuster and still have to use your Melee ability score, but what else breaks?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would probably treat the weapon as an improvised melee weapon for simplicity sake. And yeah make them use their melee rating for the party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1236-loscabadrin","name":"Loscabadrin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T17:44:25-07:00","id":884184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=883961#post883961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I allow ranged weapons to be used with melee to parry, particularly artifact versions of these?<br /> <br /> It feels weird to have a mostly unbreakable piece of metal in your hand that you can't block an incoming attack with, even if it's not well made for that purpose. You'd give it a -1 or -2 Defense adjuster and still have to use your Melee ability score, but what else breaks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing breaks, especially if you still have to use Melee or Brawl to block with it. There's no penalty or anything to using an improvised Melee weapon on Defense as far as I remember. Just a 1 initiative cost to attacking with it. In fact, I relied on this for a Brawl-based character; she'd rip branches off trees or planks out of docks as improvised clubs to get that sweet +1 Defense.<br /> <br /> If you really want it to have some penalty to using it for Parry and it's really not made for it, I'd just extend that initiative cost to parrying as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T19:09:25-07:00","id":884249,"title":"","content":"Hmm in a similar vein.<br /> What breaks if I allow players to have a specialty without the base ability?<br /> e.g. Knowing how to use a firewand without general archery.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","name":"Major","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar977_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T19:16:05-07:00","id":884254,"title":"","content":"Nothing. They're still going to pretty poor at hitting anything, as specialties are only 1 dice.<br /> (I didn't actually know you couldn't do that)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T16:01:30-07:00","id":886704,"title":"","content":"What breaks if you allow posion arrows?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T19:11:07-07:00","id":886858,"title":"","content":"Are those not allowed anyway? Because poison arrows is, well, a thing that happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T19:14:23-07:00","id":886861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=886858#post886858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are those not allowed anyway? Because poison arrows is, well, a thing that happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>It came up in crumplepunch's Clutch of Dragon's thread; only thrown weapons have the 'Poisonable' tag which, by inference, means you can't (RAW) have poison daggers, poison arrows or... poison anything other than ninja stars, basically.<br /> <br /> Which seems... very strange.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T19:47:14-07:00","id":886896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=886704#post886704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if you allow posion arrows?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can implicitly poison most cutting or piercing weapons, if you have poison suitable for applying to a weapon. Certainly nothing breaks. This is about the &quot;poisonable&quot; tag, right? Thrown weapons have that tag to indicate that most such weapons aren't suited to it because they don't cut deeply if at all, but you can assume that non-thrown weapons are poisonable if it makes sense (including, probably, the knife, even though it also has the thrown tag). To be honest, I'm pretty sure that &quot;Poisonable&quot; tag is a way of trying to make light thrown weapons attractive, and they just neglected to specify it with non-thrown weapons because that wasn't a consideration there (archery weight refers to the bow, not the arrow). But you can probably assume that anything that tends to cut or pierce deeply into flesh can be poisoned. I'd allow it on light throwable melee weapons of that type, too, like the knife.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T02:50:40-07:00","id":887056,"title":"","content":"I'd note that the Mounted tag also doesn't feature on most melee weapons, despite the fact that they can clearly be used on horseback. I'd wager this is a similar thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T14:59:56-07:00","id":889378,"title":"","content":"What breaks if I make part of my Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes first Evocation ability to switch Perception+Occult rolls for damage spells (Death of Obsidian Butterflies, Flight of Brilliant Raptor and future spells) to Wits or Intelligence + Occult?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T15:35:23-07:00","id":889396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daerian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=889378#post889378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I make part of my Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes first Evocation ability to switch Perception+Occult rolls for damage spells (Death of Obsidian Butterflies, Flight of Brilliant Raptor and future spells) to Wits or Intelligence + Occult?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perception becomes even more of a dump stat. Wits becomes even more of a god stat. Intelligence becomes even more valuable for sorcerers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-12-2016, 06:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T19:24:27-07:00","id":889566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daerian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=889378#post889378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I make part of my Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes first Evocation ability to switch Perception+Occult rolls for damage spells (Death of Obsidian Butterflies, Flight of Brilliant Raptor and future spells) to Wits or Intelligence + Occult?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's kind of a weird idea for an Evocation -- you'd have to really pitch me on it if I were running -- but if you can get your ST to sign off on it, I can't see it causing any issues. It feels build-optimizey, but it isn't going to mess anything up as a one-off game-specific power. You might want to refluff the Talisman a bit at that point, though, because as written it feels a bit off-theme for it to help an imperceptive character avoid using Perception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T22:30:37-07:00","id":890431,"title":"","content":"What breaks if the Shield tag, in addition to its current effects, adds 1 Defence to the weapon so tagged, making bucklers and tower shields actually worth using (as well as main-gauche, sai, and similar)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T22:37:08-07:00","id":890432,"title":"","content":"Anybody who's even the remotest bit interested in fighting from that point afterward will have at least one shield, possibly even have a second and third as backups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T23:51:25-07:00","id":890463,"title":"","content":"And combat tilts significantly in favour of nothing much happening (especially when it comes to decisive attacks) since everyone now has +1 defence all the time. Any two-handed combat style (heavy weapons and archery) gets badly screwed over because it can't be used in conjunction with shields, especially heavy melee weapons since their low accuracy is even more punishing than before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T00:19:12-07:00","id":890473,"title":"","content":"Not to mention the baseline for mortals to hit Exalts will be that much harder, where Exalts can just spend two more motes on offense.<br /> <br /> One of the big assumptions of Ex3 combat is that characters can and do hit one another, and passively raising everyone's Defense by one throws a monkey wrench right into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-14-2016, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T12:32:08-07:00","id":890712,"title":"","content":"Yeah. As much as the existing Shield tag is somewhere between worthless and worse-than-useless, the margin on Defense ratings is razor thin. It's a discussion that's been coming up periodically, and there hasn't really been a satisfactory answer worked out yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T12:37:17-07:00","id":890716,"title":"","content":"Subtler, then: What breaks if you allow shield-users to flurry full defense with an attack, so long as the attack isn't with the shield? It's effectively +1 defense, -3 to hit rolls for a cost of 1 Initiative per turn, which seems better, but it's hard to gauge if it's too strong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T12:50:56-07:00","id":890726,"title":"","content":"You could have shields add 1 to the pool used to calculate Parry. Meaningless when people are optimizing because 5+5+1 is so cheap and easy to get, but potentially significant for non-optimizers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T19:52:04-07:00","id":890933,"title":"","content":"After SO MANY threads hashing out dice probabilities, got a couple of very mechanical ones: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>What if the &quot;1-point Stunt&quot; were no more? +1/+2 Successes for exceptional description, but no &quot;unwritten&quot; +2 dice to every action ever.</li> <li>What if a Specialty becomes +2 dice/+1 level of a static value? Of note, I tend to favor specialties which only come up sometimes (so, &quot;Dueling&quot; or &quot;When outnumbered&quot; for Melee, not &quot;with my weapon of choice, which I never fight without&quot;).</li> </ol><br /> Off the top of my head, both are hard on Solar PCs (in that the former is hard on PCs in general, and the latter helps DBs out a smidge), but not overwhelmingly. Anything else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":2168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","user":"Chejop Kejak","date":". 05-14-2016, 11:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T20:27:12-07:00","id":890945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=890933#post890933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the &quot;1-point Excellency&quot; were no more? +1/+2 Successes for exceptional description, but no &quot;unwritten&quot; +2 dice to every action ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming you mean 1-point stunt, it would be a big blow to any effect that factors in stunt ratings, such as Immortal Blade Triumphant, although you could fix that by having them assume that you got at least a 1-point stunt even though 1-point stunts no longer actually exist. You also make it <i>much</i> harder for anyone to accomplish anything they haven't invested into, since +2 dice is very often going to be the difference between success and failure if you only had 2-3 to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T20:28:45-07:00","id":890946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=890933#post890933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After SO MANY threads hashing out dice probabilities, got a couple of very mechanical ones:<br /> 1. What if the &quot;1-point Excellency&quot; were no more? +1/+2 Successes for exceptional description, but no &quot;unwritten&quot; +2 dice to every action ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>The big thing is that people will be much less likely to do the things stunting is meant to incentivize, and when they do go out of their way to engage with the stunt mechanics stunt they'll expect an &quot;exceptional description&quot; bonus.<br /> <br /> There are also various little things. You need higher dicepools to be viable -- stunting is partly designed to allow you to do impressive things with smaller pools. Dice tricks are generally less effective. The various zany system-pushing extended roll systems, like crafting and Wyld-shaping, run into issues since they're calibrated for stunts. I'd just resign yourself to giving the +2 to these rather than trying to recalibrate them without breaking anything else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=890933#post890933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. What if a Specialty becomes +2 dice/+1 success? Of note, I tend to favor specialties which only come up sometimes (so, &quot;Dueling&quot; or &quot;When outnumbered&quot; for Melee, not &quot;with my weapon of choice, which I never fight without&quot;).<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head, both are hard on Solar PCs (in that the former is hard on PCs in general, and the latter helps DBs out a smidge), but not overwhelmingly. Anything else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Specialty optimization becomes much higher-stakes. That's the level of modifier that makes people sit up and take notice, so you can expect more people to go out of their way to game their specialties hard under this paradigm (you <i>really</i> want that bonus on your clashes, for instance). On the upside, you get rid of the thing where people take specialties to bump their static value pools from even to odd values to exploit sweet, sweet rounding.<br /> <br /> An autosuccess means you can't ever fail difficulty 1 tasks and can't ever botch a specialty roll; it makes charms that give automatic successes less valuable, since the first one is worth far more than the rest. This might be a bit much, given how high the bar is for difficulty 1 in Ex3. +2 dice benefits dice gimmicks like double 9s, obviously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T21:08:55-07:00","id":892251,"title":"","content":"What breaks if you apply the +5 motes per turn to social combat scenes?* I've noticed that the few times I've been in a social-heavy scene, I'm rapidly running out of motes to draw upon as I'm usually limited to my personal pool.<br /> <br /> *yeah yeah it's not called social combat anymore, sue me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T21:43:30-07:00","id":892267,"title":"","content":"Considering that social scenes are far lower-risk than combat scenes, players would be much more likely to game the system by selling candy bars in-character after a particularly mote-intensive combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T22:02:09-07:00","id":892279,"title":"","content":"Hm, that seems like more of a player/GM thing than a system concern. I feel like most GMs would let you get away with it only a handful of times before putting a stop to it. So long as nothing breaks mechanically I don't see an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T22:28:22-07:00","id":892295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=892279#post892279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, that seems like more of a player/GM thing than a system concern. I feel like most GMs would let you get away with it only a handful of times before putting a stop to it. So long as nothing breaks mechanically I don't see an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to agree here. Selling candy bars seems fairly equivalent to arguments of what constitutes a &quot;real fight&quot;, or white-room arguments on withering attack batteries. If the social scene is dramatically important, especially if there are other essence powered parties involved, I'd expect to respire essence the same way as combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","name":"Major","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar977_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T23:01:09-07:00","id":892314,"title":"","content":"The real issue is that social scenes move in David Lynch time. When there's a real tactical benefit to taking a ton of actions in a row, the lack of rules about what order things may happen in could cause some hurt feelings when different people feel different things &quot;just make sense&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T23:08:24-07:00","id":892319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=892251#post892251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if you apply the +5 motes per turn to social combat scenes?* I've noticed that the few times I've been in a social-heavy scene, I'm rapidly running out of motes to draw upon as I'm usually limited to my personal pool.<br /> <br /> *yeah yeah it's not called social combat anymore, sue me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget that spending 4 motes of peripheral a round isn't going to give you any anima flare, even a caste mark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T23:11:15-07:00","id":892322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=892314#post892314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The real issue is that social scenes move in David Lynch time. When there's a real tactical benefit to taking a ton of actions in a row, the lack of rules about what order things may happen in could cause some hurt feelings when different people feel different things &quot;just make sense&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Edit: I realise I misunderstood what you said.<br /> <br /> Yeah, social scenes just follow people talking, they don't really have turns. So, when do you get the 5 motes? Every time you roll maybe? It could work, but it might be a bit odd, with people trying to make a lot more rolls than they ought to to get more motes back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-17-2016, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T23:23:20-07:00","id":892330,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm not here to defend 2E. I hate 2E.<br /> <br /> I'm talking about potential issues from a discussed house rule in 3E. And I see &quot;talking faster/over others = better mote economy&quot; to be a real potential problem.<br /> <br /> For a less extreme example, consider the case of two advisors, both trying to persuade their rules of something. Under these rules, the advisors keep regaining motes, but the ruler - who never &quot;acts,&quot; exactly - doesn't. This could matter if one of them is, say, a secret Lunar infiltrator trying to work insidious Charms upon the queen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T07:17:32-07:00","id":892482,"title":"","content":"Considering that all you need for many social scenes (in my experience) is just one successful roll with no extra successes, I don't think you really need a ton of extra mote regen. It makes more sense in combat where those extra successes make a difference, and you need many successful rolls to win.<br /> <br /> If you really want fast mote regen out of combat, the best you can really do, since there are no rounds, is arbitrarily pick times when everyone gets those 5 motes.<br /> <br /> (In extended rolls, you could get the motes back at the end if every interval, but that doesn't work in social conflicts.)<br /> <br /> Nothing breaks, I think, but social influence becomes a ton easier if you've got more motes to throw around. It might break specific games or characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T09:04:26-07:00","id":892563,"title":"","content":"<b><i>What breaks if:</i> You can use a Move action <i>after </i>a successful Rush action?</b><br /> <br /> Right now, the rules explicitly <i>but specifically</i> allow you to use a Rush action action <i>after </i>using a Move action in your turn. Which means you can Move into short range, and then Rush, or you can Move into close range, and then Rush.<br /> <br /> But it also means that you cannot Rush while at short range <i>and then</i> Move into close range. Which is not a terribly huge deal, since you could Move while at short range and then Rush when you are in close range. But it does mean that you need to commit to advancing on an opponent before you know whether or not the Rush will succeed, whereas if you could try Rushing before you decide to Move, you could at least cut your losses and perhaps Move towards a different target or change to a tactic which requires you to stay put.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Possible answer to my own question:</b><br /> <br /> The inability to Move after Rushing also means this: If someone successfully Disengaged from you and moved out to short range on their turn, you must first Move before you can attempt to Rush, and your Move action will trigger their reflexive Disengage movement. Whereas, if you could attempt Rushing first, your following Move action (into close range) would trigger their reflexive retreat (back into/maintaining short range), which would then trigger your reflexive pursuit (back into/maintaining close range).<br /> <br /> Right now, you must choose to gamble on a Rush action directed at an enemy at close range, against the possibility of your opponent attempting to flee. If they do not flee, any attack you make that turn suffers flurry penalties for nothing. If they do flee and you were not prepared, they can escape from you even as you chase after them.<br /> <br /> If you <i>could</i> use a Move action after a successful Rush action, the stakes of that gamble are fundamentally reduced. You can always concentrate on fighting an opponent at close range without fear that they can escape. You don't even need to flurry your attempts to chase them with an attack on the same turn, if you are patient -- in catching up to the target at close range, they once again need to beat you on an opposed roll with their Disengage action, or else you can spend all of your next turn concentrating on attacking them.<br /> <br /> This is a systematic change to tactical possibilities beyond simply allowing an assaulting player the ability to wait and see if a Rush succeeds before taking a Move action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-17-2016, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T09:16:50-07:00","id":892569,"title":"","content":"I think you did a pretty good job of breaking down the implications yourself?<br /> <br /> I will say that I initially didn't object, but your breakdown convinced me it's not a rule I'd want. Just from the very basic level, not actually moving towards someone until you know that's you've beaten them in the chase <i>feels</i> wrong. That's not how running after someone works. Playing a lot of SMITE has driven home to me the diciness of running all-out after someone in a combat situation, even if you are objectively faster. Things can go wrong!<br /> <br /> Add to that the way it tends to moot the reflexive Disengage move, and I see this as a change which creates problems without adding anything desirable. Why do you want it? Do you think it's too easy to escape melee as-is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T10:52:26-07:00","id":892626,"title":"","content":"No, I was just going to ask if the implicit limitation was intentional. Then, after I worked out the problem, I wanted to share my logic so that others would understand that this was NOT an error, but rather an important limitation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T22:34:06-07:00","id":893042,"title":"","content":"<b><i>What breaks if</i> Battle Groups added their Size modifier to their opposed rolls against Disengage actions?</b><br /> <br /> The bigger the group, the more easily they ought to be able to surround you and cut off your escape routes, right? The rules explicitly state that trying to move THROUGH a range band occupied by a Battle Group counts as trying to pass through difficult terrain.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Possible answer: </b>Difficult terrain rules automatically apply a -3 penalty to movement actions such as Disengage, so anything more is unnecessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-18-2016, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T11:10:21-07:00","id":893458,"title":"","content":"What breaks if I decide not to have a different Craft ability for each, err, craft, and just opt for specialties? You'd start with a free Craft specialty once you start putting points in it, and all kinds of craft would have the same rating: Woodworking, Artifacts, Armors, etc...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T11:19:26-07:00","id":893466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChairKicker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=893458#post893458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I decide not to have a different Craft ability for each, err, craft, and just opt for specialties? You'd start with a free Craft specialty once you start putting points in it, and all kinds of craft would have the same rating: Woodworking, Artifacts, Armors, etc...</div> </div> </div> </div>Craft makes more sense. Also: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...how-i-fixed-it</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T11:53:54-07:00","id":893502,"title":"","content":"Some craft charms stop working, but those are relatively easy to ignore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T07:05:37-07:00","id":895460,"title":"","content":"What breaks if you allow characters to choose their Supernal from any of their caste or favored abilities?<br /> <br /> I'm on an Assassin's Creed kick and trying to figure out ways to create the omni-tactical battle hydra in 3e while still being a stealth-focused character. Short of waiting for Lunars to come out the best option looks like dumping a ton of investment into Ebon Shadow, Righteous Devil, Snake, and possibly Steel Devil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T07:09:14-07:00","id":895464,"title":"","content":"I don't think anything breaks, per-se, there's just the danger of having tons of characters with entirely inappropriate supernals for the power of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T07:20:09-07:00","id":895470,"title":"","content":"Caste choice goes back to being cosmetic or done just for the anima power(s).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T07:49:29-07:00","id":895480,"title":"","content":"I don't think it was purely cosmetic before... I'd say 80% of people chose the caste that fit their character. But then, 20% of people chose the caste with the best anima power, you're right.<br /> I did that for my first Solar character, and 3 years later I regretted it a lot. Bad, bad idea.<br /> Anyway, Supernal as caste-only does help with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T15:02:33-07:00","id":903795,"title":"","content":"What breaks if a Solar can use a normal Defend Other action to protect one character while using War Lion Stance to reflexively protect a third character?<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I wish Defend Other had been named &quot;Protect&quot; or &quot;Protection&quot;, so that I could use short and natural language like &quot;using War Lion Stance to Protect a third character&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T15:25:55-07:00","id":903803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=903795#post903795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if a Solar can use a normal Defend Other action to protect one character while using War Lion Stance to reflexively protect a third character?<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I wish Defend Other had been named &amp;quot;Protect&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;Protection&amp;quot;, so that I could use short and natural language like &amp;quot;using War Lion Stance to Protect a third character&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's 2m less per attack being drained from them. In the instance of a single opponent that means practically nothing, but it means increasingly more with additional opponents thus attacks being thrown around. I would't say it breaks anything, but Melee always felt deliberately mote intensive to keep up all its versatility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T17:19:07-07:00","id":903864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=903795#post903795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if a Solar can use a normal Defend Other action to protect one character while using War Lion Stance to reflexively protect a third character?<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I wish Defend Other had been named &quot;Protect&quot; or &quot;Protection&quot;, so that I could use short and natural language like &quot;using War Lion Stance to Protect a third character&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>War Lion Stance is already a very good Charm. Cranking up the power level is probably not a great idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T17:55:39-07:00","id":903875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=903864#post903864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">War Lion Stance is already a very good Charm. Cranking up the power level is probably not a great idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just found the language unclear about whether WLS counted against the number of Defend Other actions a Solar could perform.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T18:07:10-07:00","id":903880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=903795#post903795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if a Solar can use a normal Defend Other action to protect one character while using War Lion Stance to reflexively protect a third character?</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually read the charm as allowing you to do this. It seemed to me that the limitation was that you could only take reflexive defend other actions to protect the original ward, not that you couldn't even use the result of a previous Defend Other action.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10881-anasurimbor","name":"Anasurimbor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T18:30:34-07:00","id":903886,"title":"","content":"RAW, if you use Defend Other on a character who is not the subject of your War Lion Stance, you must drop commitment to War Lion Stance, because the last line does not say &quot;...to defend another character <i>with this Charm</i>&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now, if you activate War Lion Stance during a turn where you are already using a Defend Other action, I really have no idea what happens.<br /> <br /> As for what breaks if you allow a Solar to use WLS and their action to defend two characters at the same time? Well, as far as I can tell, nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11878-realbrickwall","name":"realbrickwall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T20:04:08-07:00","id":903919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=903795#post903795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if a Solar can use a normal Defend Other action to protect one character while using War Lion Stance to reflexively protect a third character?<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I wish Defend Other had been named &quot;Protect&quot; or &quot;Protection&quot;, so that I could use short and natural language like &quot;using War Lion Stance to Protect a third character&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Couldn't you just say &quot;defend&quot;? That's pretty short.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>realbrickwall</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, if you activate War Lion Stance during a turn where you are already using a Defend Other action, I really have no idea what happens.</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe you stop defending the first person?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>realbrickwall</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for what breaks if you allow a Solar to use WLS and their action to defend two characters at the same time? Well, as far as I can tell, nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say anything breaks per-se, but it does make Dawn bodyguards much, much better, and thus it's very difficult for opponents to damage the other PCs.<br /> I already find War Lion Stance to be one of the best combat charms in the game!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T09:53:52-07:00","id":904231,"title":"","content":"What breaks if a Zenith absorbs all of the intimacies of the dead, rather than just their Defining one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T10:09:29-07:00","id":904236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=904231#post904231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if a Zenith absorbs all of the intimacies of the dead, rather than just their Defining one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Their sanity, mostly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10881-anasurimbor","name":"Anasurimbor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T10:23:16-07:00","id":904250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anasurimbor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=904236#post904236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their sanity, mostly</div> </div> </div> </div>Have a Like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T10:49:13-07:00","id":904270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anasurimbor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=904236#post904236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their sanity, mostly</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh right, good. I'm playing him correctly then <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T12:03:48-07:00","id":905834,"title":"","content":"What breaks if you allow people struck by a decisive attack to spend initiative to reduce the raw damage of the incoming strike? Not *neccesarily* at 1:1, although that would be the place to start with tinkering.<br /> <br /> (I'm thinking of the somewhat unintuitive examples of two characters both get very high join battle results, and both are incentivized to making immediate decisive attacks)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T12:11:17-07:00","id":905842,"title":"","content":"It becomes impossible to ever end fights without Crashing people/strong Decisive Charms, basically. Since I know some people think that's too hard already, this won't be for everybody.<br /> <br /> Conversely, it becomes harder to kill someone with an ambush, or otherwise snipe them out early through good luck/big burst damage. Some people hate when that happens, so they'd be happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T16:13:08-07:00","id":906036,"title":"","content":"I don't think that's a good idea. Heavenly Guardian Defense shouldn't be free and universal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T16:14:53-07:00","id":906038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=906036#post906036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that's a good idea. Heavenly Guardian Defense shouldn't be free and universal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention without the 4m surcharge (if a bit less efficient).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10881-anasurimbor","name":"Anasurimbor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T16:22:05-07:00","id":906042,"title":"","content":"They're not suggesting free Heavenly Guardian Defense. HGD reduces decisive damage by 1 success per initiative spent. They're suggesting at best 1 raw damage die per initiative, about three time worse than HGD's efficiency. Make it 2i or 3i for each die, and it's incredibly worse than HGD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T09:12:23-07:00","id":907128,"title":"","content":"Anything break if I allow PC's and important NPC's to gain +1 defence from a weapon with the reaching tag when fighting enemies without a reaching tag weapon? (unmounted combat)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","name":"Major","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar977_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T09:19:31-07:00","id":907131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Major</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=907128#post907128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything break if I allow PC's and important NPC's to gain +1 defence from a weapon with the reaching tag when fighting enemies without a reaching tag weapon? (unmounted combat)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Spears become *way* awesome. Like, only suckers would want a sword unless they are mounted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T09:42:20-07:00","id":907138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=907131#post907131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Spears become *way* awesome. Like, only suckers would want a sword unless they are mounted.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That seems entirely realistic.<br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> What breaks if you allow mortals to regain 1 wp per day by playing with a pet for half an hour? This can only be done if they have spent a willpower that day and can't take you above your permanent willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T09:51:10-07:00","id":907142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=907131#post907131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Spears become *way* awesome. Like, only suckers would want a sword unless they are mounted.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's easy to fix. Just give axes a bonus against spears. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10881-anasurimbor","name":"Anasurimbor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T10:21:53-07:00","id":907162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Major</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=907128#post907128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything break if I allow PC's and important NPC's to gain +1 defence from a weapon with the reaching tag when fighting enemies without a reaching tag weapon? (unmounted combat)</div> </div> </div> </div>You've arbitrarily powered up one weapon tag but no others, so every optimal build now needs to use that tag.<br /> <br /> You should also apply Reaching to EVERY Daiklave - they basically only lack it for flavor reasons, since a five-foot sword clearly has the reach of a short spear. Making Daiklaves a poor choice against pointy sticks would leave this rule even sillier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T11:15:23-07:00","id":907197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anasurimbor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=907142#post907142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's easy to fix. Just give axes a bonus against spears. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Contrary to &quot;common knowledge&quot;, it is actually rather difficult to chop straight through a spear-shaft. They are around 1 1/2 inches thick, of hardwood, and sometimes reinforced with metal. Granted, smacking a spearshaft with a weapon <u>will</u> knock the head out of the way, but it probably won't chop through it. <br /> <br /> I just give axes and other &quot;hooked&quot; weapons a bonus die whenever my characters stunt a disarm or trip Gambit. (clarification: they just get the standard +1 die for stunting) In &quot;real life&quot;, it is almost trivially easy to disarm or trip an enemy when you use the heel of a war-axe to hook around a weapon, a shield, or an arm or a leg. The players have to describe using the heel of the axe to do so, however. If they describe the Gambit as &quot;I knock away the weapon with my own&quot;, they don't get the bonus.<br /> <br /> I am interested in giving spear-users some Defense bonus against non-spear users (it is really easy to keep someone at bay using a spear), but I would balance it by also giving spears and other Reaching weapons an Accuracy penalty vs adjacent opponents, to represent the difficulty of using a 7-foot-long weapon with 3 feet of the shaft swinging around behind your head, but the arbitrary ranges of 3E make it difficult. In D&amp;D it was easy, as distances in combat were concrete and penalties were easy to add.<br /> <br /> Again, in real life, spears weren't used in close quarters. If an enemy got within the reach of the spearhead, you would usually drop the spear and draw a backup weapon. Of course, you could always choke up on the spear, but doing so made fighting with it difficult.<br /> <br /> Take the above with a grain of salt, as I run mortal campaigns were even a +1/-1 bonus to rolls are important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T11:50:23-07:00","id":907213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=907197#post907197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take the above with a grain of salt, as I run mortal campaigns were even a +1/-1 bonus to rolls are important.</div> </div> </div> </div>+1/-1 bonuses to rolls are important in Solar games. Arguably more important, since dice tricks mean it can translate to more than .5 successes for them.<br /> <br /> That's why I am DEEPLY hesitant to give such a bonus to anything. I'm also deeply hesitant to take a combat system built around being cinematic and unrealistic and start assigning granular bonuses/penalties based on real-world traits of weapons. My honest advice (especially if you're not using Charms) would be to find a system designed to support that style of play.<br /> <br /> But clearly you know what you and your group are enjoying. It's just sufficiently far-removed from what I see Exalted 3 as equipped to handle that I can no longer predict what will &quot;break&quot; - the status quo represents a massive break from my expectations already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T17:31:42-07:00","id":907338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=907138#post907138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That seems entirely realistic.<br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> What breaks if you allow mortals to regain 1 wp per day by playing with a pet for half an hour? This can only be done if they have spent a willpower that day and can't take you above your permanent willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing breaks, it's just silly. That's not how pets or Willpower works. Willpower isn't &quot;I'm less tired and in a better mood&quot;. It's a powerful resource, spending a willpower is a very tiring thing that gives you a pretty decent boost. 'Playing with a pet' isn't 'I slept really well last night' or 'I killed the six-fingered man and avenged my father' or 'I stopped the plague ravaging my nation' in terms of sudden boosts of renewed purpose and energy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":800,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","user":"Fenrir666","date":". 06-04-2016, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T18:43:33-07:00","id":907371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=907338#post907338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing breaks, it's just silly. That's not how pets or Willpower works. Willpower isn't &quot;I'm less tired and in a better mood&quot;. It's a powerful resource, spending a willpower is a very tiring thing that gives you a pretty decent boost. 'Playing with a pet' isn't 'I slept really well last night' or 'I killed the six-fingered man and avenged my father' or 'I stopped the plague ravaging my nation' in terms of sudden boosts of renewed purpose and energy.</div> </div> </div> </div>It actually has a significant real world effect. Cancer patients with pets who play with them live significantly longer than cancer patients that don't have pets/play with them. And when I don't sleep well, spending time playing with my cat really does help a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T19:08:28-07:00","id":907381,"title":"","content":"You still probably oughtta limit it. Maybe to once a week?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T19:27:12-07:00","id":907386,"title":"","content":"Yeah, without a limit, people are regaining 6 WP a day by just saying &quot;I preen my eagle between scenes&quot; every time there's a slow moment. That's... moderately game-breaking.<br /> <br /> As a cat owner myself, I'd be hesitant to say that playing with them is more personally restoring than extended meditation in a setting where that ties directly into demonstrable magical forces (see: attuning a demesne). Since regaining WP via meditation requires the same 6-8 hours as doing so by sleep, I wouldn't make an exception for <i>any</i> faster action. People will probably not be spending six hours currying their horse multiple times per day, so that's really abuse-proof.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T19:43:31-07:00","id":907391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=907386#post907386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, without a limit, people are regaining 6 WP a day by just saying &quot;I preen my eagle between scenes&quot; every time there's a slow moment. That's... moderately game-breaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did limit it to once a day. And only if you had already spent WP that day.<br /> <br /> Edit: Maybe I'm just underestimating how hard WP is to come by in 3e? Most of my interaction with Exalted by time is 2e, where sleep generally restored more than 1 wp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11917,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","user":"Aranfan","date":". 06-04-2016, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T22:08:41-07:00","id":907451,"title":"","content":"In EX3, a night's sleep (or multiple hours of meditation) restores 1wp (p. 169). Also, two-point Stunts are meant to be harder to get.<br /> <br /> So, yes, an extra WP per day is a non-trivial bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T13:50:10-07:00","id":909444,"title":"","content":"<b>Essence of Blaster: </b><br /> Cost: 6m, 1wp ; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Uniform<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> Knowing the power of Elements lying in her weapon, young Twilight learned to target her weapon not by eye, but with elements of Creation. As she struck the air, her weapon blow moved upon Essence to hit enemies. This attacks emanate as powerful Essence blasts, hitting her enemies and stopping them in their tracks.<br /> The Solar is capable of making Melee attacks up to Short range by hitting her enemies with blast of Essence instead of weapon itself. She can also attack enemies at medium range if she takes Aim action first. Attacks made further than close range do not add Solar Strength to damage. This effect cannot be used for counterattacks if they are done from further than close range. When combined with Iron Raptor Technique this Evocation allows attacking enemies at long range without Aim action.<br /> <b>Special activation rules:</b> This Evocation awakens at no cost when wielder of the Elemental Heart attunes to her weapon.<br /> <br /> Sorry to post homebrew here, but I really want to have some opinions if you think it will break the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T14:09:56-07:00","id":909468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daerian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=909444#post909444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Essence of Blaster: </b><br /> Cost: 6m, 1wp ; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Uniform<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> Knowing the power of Elements lying in her weapon, young Twilight learned to target her weapon not by eye, but with elements of Creation. As she struck the air, her weapon blow moved upon Essence to hit enemies. This attacks emanate as powerful Essence blasts, hitting her enemies and stopping them in their tracks.<br /> The Solar is capable of making Melee attacks up to Short range by hitting her enemies with blast of Essence instead of weapon itself. She can also attack enemies at medium range if she takes Aim action first. Attacks made further than close range do not add Solar Strength to damage. This effect cannot be used for counterattacks if they are done from further than close range. When combined with Iron Raptor Technique this Evocation allows attacking enemies at long range without Aim action.<br /> <b>Special activation rules:</b> This Evocation awakens at no cost when wielder of the Elemental Heart attunes to her weapon.<br /> <br /> Sorry to post homebrew here, but I really want to have some opinions if you think it will break the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a LOT of missing context here, since we don't know what the weapon is. I <b>assume</b> that you're using weapon stats even though you're hitting with a beam of essence. So it's a scene-long effect that gives your (I presume) melee weapon ranged abilities. It's WAY too strong for Essence 1 (and kind of outside the scope of that Essence level) imo, but mechanically in general I'd say it's very strong anyways. But I don't think it's game-breaking, no. Taking away strength helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T16:24:32-07:00","id":909568,"title":"","content":"Thanks a lot. It's Wreckstaff - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907201#post907201\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...201#post907201</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T06:27:39-07:00","id":912211,"title":"","content":"Blantly stolen from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/912160-social-actions-in-combat\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ions-in-combat</a> - <br /> <br /> What breaks if you can make withering attacks with Presence / Performance against the victim's resolve, as you prey upon their mental and emotional weaknesses.<br /> <br /> Assuming that you still have to exploit some kind of intimacy to do so, anyways.<br /> <br /> (I'm certain you could make a reasonable charm to do so; I'm wondering about it as a general system conceit)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T06:46:14-07:00","id":912218,"title":"","content":"What breaks if I merge the Personal and Peripheral Essence tracks together, and decide to opt for the rules concerning Peripheral motes spending (so that whatever's the source of your motes, your anima will grow if enough if spent at once)? Besides the Charms making explicit references to those tracks, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T06:55:46-07:00","id":912221,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar169_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"169\" data-vbnamecard=\"169\">wastevens</a> as a guess, it probably would be something close or similar to a Sidereal Martial Arts. Mortals and people who can't generally boost their resolve will have a hard time keeping up but beside that, it's not too bad.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar519_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"519\" data-vbnamecard=\"519\">ChairKicker</a> It would technically only have a story effect, as in it would become easier to track your Solars. Now if your ST play it straight that every time that you glow, some citizens of the realm report you and your activities, the Wyld Hunt, quite possibly led by some young bronze faction sid will come for you and worst come to worst, the inner circle of the immaculate order or if you prefer Chejop buddies who were responsible for the Usurpation will come for you. Now if your ST is soft and barely ever involves the immaculate order, wyld hunt etc...it won't change anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T06:58:30-07:00","id":912222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChairKicker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=912218#post912218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I merge the Personal and Peripheral Essence tracks together, and decide to opt for the rules concerning Peripheral motes spending (so that whatever's the source of your motes, your anima will grow if enough if spent at once)? Besides the Charms making explicit references to those tracks, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>It becomes a lot harder to keep your anima from glowing, of course. Normally if you've got a Charm that has a 5m+ cost, you can opt to use it from your personal, at least once or twice. With your change, you can't do that. Anything with a 5m+ cost makes your anima glow. The Night anima power gets a lot better.<br /> <br /> I was actually thinking about how to do a single mote pool the other day, and one idea you might want to consider is also having so many uses of free Mutes. That is, maybe so many times a day, or so many times a scene, you can use a Mute to have all your expenditures in an instant not count toward anima flaring. Sort of a way to emulate the personal pool without actually having it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T08:10:25-07:00","id":912238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=912222#post912222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was actually thinking about how to do a single mote pool the other day, and one idea you might want to consider is also having so many uses of free Mutes. That is, maybe so many times a day, or so many times a scene, you can use a Mute to have all your expenditures in an instant not count toward anima flaring. Sort of a way to emulate the personal pool without actually having it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooooh, that sounds like a good compromise!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T08:21:34-07:00","id":912246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChairKicker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=912218#post912218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I merge the Personal and Peripheral Essence tracks together, and decide to opt for the rules concerning Peripheral motes spending (so that whatever's the source of your motes, your anima will grow if enough if spent at once)? Besides the Charms making explicit references to those tracks, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Getimian Exalted (from what little we know) make explicitly different use of personal vs peripheral essence in some of their charms. Dunno how important that might be to you tho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T08:28:57-07:00","id":912250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=912246#post912246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getimian Exalted (from what little we know) make explicitly different use of personal vs peripheral essence in some of their charms. Dunno how important that might be to you tho.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably be easy enough to just let the getimians specifically have that personal/peripheral split, as a special thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T08:38:58-07:00","id":912256,"title":"","content":"Plus, they're not out for years, so it's not important.<br /> <br /> I think what breaks is that any charm more than 4m (including fat excellencies) can't be used in public unless you're in a place that's very tolerant of Anathema. And less combos of charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T14:06:58-07:00","id":912987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=912256#post912256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what breaks is that any charm more than 4m (including fat excellencies) can't be used in public unless you're in a place that's very tolerant of Anathema. And less combos of charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the issue, yes. I would recommend a higher threshold for Anima growth (8 motes, say), and/or greater proliferation of Mute Charms.<br /> <br /> Note that these fixes create a new issue - it gets harder to deliberately power up your Anima to trigger Charms which need it. I don't see that as a problem (I don't really think intended of use of those Charms is to nova like a psycho and get them on round one), but others might.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T17:30:20-07:00","id":913106,"title":"","content":"What breaks if I add a Celestial Circle Spell to allow someone to summon ess 4 elementals [aka, Garda Birds] along the lines of Demon of the Second Circle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T19:06:57-07:00","id":913153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=913106#post913106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I add a Celestial Circle Spell to allow someone to summon ess 4 elementals [aka, Garda Birds] along the lines of Demon of the Second Circle?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not much. From the examples we have, 2CDs are scarier than E4 Elementals. There might be some story impact, but a competent ST can easily handle that if/when it comes up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T11:05:14-07:00","id":918133,"title":"","content":"I've either seen this question floating around and forgotten the answer, or seen things tangentially related otherwise.<br /> <br /> <b>What breaks if:</b> As a first-level sorcerous artifact evocation, I permit the situational use of Perception (replacing Intelligence) for Shape Sorcery?<br /> <br /> Context: The sorcery initiation and shaping rituals are tied into converting light itself into power through blessed (or cursed) eyes. For the purposes of the question, the &quot;situational&quot; conditions are being in clear (or partly cloudy, I suppose) daylight or other significantly brightly lit area, such that there's enough light to actually convert into sorcerous motes to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T11:31:20-07:00","id":918149,"title":"","content":"Folks will dump Intelligence and then either fight in brightly lit areas or use their animas to light it up enough to use Perception in virtually every spellcasting situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T12:34:20-07:00","id":918182,"title":"","content":"I suppose for a Terrestrial Circle combat sorcerer, that's true, if they wanted to limit their useful spells to DoOB and FotBR. But Intelligence is still needed for a vast number of the spells, and it seems like more of a penalty if they seriously wanted to churn out the motes to get themselves to Burning anima or higher...<br /> <br /> Hrm. It's only really for my personal use, and I know I don't plan to use it that way, but I'll chew on it a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T12:51:48-07:00","id":918199,"title":"","content":"Actually, you can brighten an area as much as you want for a single mote, so it's not like a minmaxing player is dumping 15m into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T13:01:03-07:00","id":918205,"title":"","content":"Oh, huh. Well then I might have to include a condition that the user cannot draw power from their own light, seeing as that would be so self-sustaining. Thanks for the head's up!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T13:14:00-07:00","id":918212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=918199#post918199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, you can brighten an area as much as you want for a single mote, so it's not like a minmaxing player is dumping 15m into it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Can they? I thought the only two &quot;one mote&quot; effects of the anima banner were telling the exact time of day and displaying their caste mark (not saying anything about creating a light source). Maybe I missed something and that effect isn't listed under the Anima Banner section in the core?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My (mostly) German Exalted blog: <a href=\"http://ryokiseck.de/\" target=\"_blank\">Praise the Spiral!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11185-ryoki","name":"Ryoki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T13:20:30-07:00","id":918215,"title":"","content":"Misremembered - I thought the Solar could make the caste mark shine as <i>bright</i> as he desires, when it's in fact for as <i>long</i> as he desires. <i>Mea culpa</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T13:35:57-07:00","id":918221,"title":"","content":"Ah, alright and you got my hopes up. I always found it to be somewhat strange that the Chosen of the Sun can't effortlessly create light... But well I think that makes the idea of replacing Intelligence with Perception fine. Personally I would think about adding in a limitation for &quot;pure&quot; and &quot;corrupted&quot; light depending on what kind of artifact it is. If you are using &quot;blessed&quot; eyes you would only be able to convert from light sources that are born in creation and not from the light of the green sun (and vice-versa for cursed eyes). <br /> The effect itself is not overpowered or breaking the system in my eyes, but it enables certain character types a whole new playstyle and that's why I like to some interesting conditions. But that is only me and if the above stated conditions are interesting is up to debate. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My (mostly) German Exalted blog: <a href=\"http://ryokiseck.de/\" target=\"_blank\">Praise the Spiral!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11185-ryoki","name":"Ryoki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T17:01:36-07:00","id":931692,"title":"","content":"What breaks if:<br /> <br /> <b>Savaging or throw/slam actions/attacks in a clinch apply onslaught penalties against the victim for the purposes of other character's attacks?</b><br /> <br /> Savaging and slam/throwing actions are resolved just like attacks, save that they need a clinch and treat the target's Defense as 0. The victim does not treat his Defense as 0 against other opponents (though he takes a Defense penalty for being clinched). It makes sense that being savaged would penalize the victim's Defense against outside attacks, and that the victim would suffer onslaught for being thrown into a hard surface, at least.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Savaging or throw/slam actions/attacks in a clinch can be treated like attacks for Charms that do not explicitly forbid use within grapples?</b><br /> <br /> Savaging and slam/throwing actions are resolved just like attacks, save that they need a clinch and treat the target's Defense as 0. The list of non-grappling-specific Brawl Charms that could thus supplement these attacks include:<br /> <br /> <br /> Fists of Iron Technique (gets you Lethal grappling damage earlier than Dragon Coil Technique, and even after DCT, still adds damage)<br /> <br /> Ferocious Jab (someone outside of the grapple could attack your victim, and even if their Defense cannot become a negative number, without a penalty-negator, the penalty is still there for Ferocious Jab to exploit)<br /> <br /> Thunderclap Rush Attack (you might need to act outside of your Initiative order to get in one last squeeze before the opponent breaks free, and you can even Crash your opponent before you even apply a savaging or slam/throwing attack!)<br /> <br /> Falling Hammer Strike (if savaging and slam/throwing actions/attacks really do apply onslaught penalties that the Solar grappler's allies might exploit... or the Solar himself with Ferocious Jab)<br /> <br /> Solar Cross-Counter (unless you Restrain a victim, he can still attack you; any Brawl-based attack or counter-attack you make against the victim, including from this Charm, should treat his Defense as 0)<br /> <br /> Ox-Stunning Blow<br /> <br /> Burning Burial Fist<br /> <br /> Force-Rending Strike (again, the victim can still attack you; since their attack is definitely NOT their Defense, your clash would not treat their attack pool as 0)<br /> <br /> Blade-Rebuking Wrath (disarm your victim of that knife he keeps trying to stab you with)<br /> <br /> Hammer On Iron (like Titan-Strengthening Method, but Decisive instead of Withering-only, and you don't expend your rounds of control for it!)<br /> <br /> One With Violence<br /> <br /> Cancel the Apocalypse<br /> <br /> Adamantine Fists of Battle (the victim can still soak, so more Overwhelming damage is useful)<br /> <br /> Intercepting Fury Smite<br /> <br /> Fire-Eating Fist<br /> <br /> Striving Aftershock Method<br /> <br /> Incarnated Fury Attack (the unblockable and undodgeable aspects are wasted, but there's more to this Charm than that)<br /> <br /> Orichalcum Fists of Battle<br /> <br /> Rampage-Berserker Attack (again, like Titan-Straightening Method, but Decisive instead of Withering-only, and you don't expend your rounds of control for it!)<br /> <br /> Apocalypse Flare Attack (the range aspect of this attack is wasted, but you can spend your anima banner to add to the damage you'd inflict with Fire-Eating Fist)<br /> <br /> Heaven Fury Smite (especially nasty with Cancel the Apocalypse, Striving Aftershock Method, Raging Wrath Repeated, Incarnated Fury Attack, and Ferocious Jab; Orichalcum Fists of Battle also increases base Initiative by 1)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T05:26:33-07:00","id":936039,"title":"","content":"What breaks if I permit combos between Martial Arts and Brawl/Melee Charms (depending on the form weapons, as usual)?<br /> <br /> My rationale for considering it: my game has a no-PC-death system, that also sort of applies to important NPC's too (plot kills them, not fighting), so one-hit-kills are less of a pain. I do very much enjoy the flavor that Exalts are naturally better at everything, including martial arts. I would apply it to all Exalts, if I did it.<br /> <br /> Thanks for indulging my curiosity!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12120-bitterwalnut","name":"bitterWalnut","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T06:43:03-07:00","id":936062,"title":"","content":"Even if you don't let anyone important die, there's still a lot of plot-wrecking potential to be had in beating somebody at combat. Or even just coming close.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T15:05:16-07:00","id":936260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bitterWalnut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=936039#post936039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My rationale for considering it: my game has a no-PC-death system, that also sort of applies to important NPC's too (plot kills them, not fighting), so one-hit-kills are less of a pain. I do very much enjoy the flavor that Exalts are naturally better at everything, including martial arts. I would apply it to all Exalts, if I did it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalts ARE better at combat. Normal people don't get Martial Arts Charms at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T18:48:43-07:00","id":936354,"title":"","content":"What breaks if: I allow <b>Flawless Diagnosis Technique</b> to work with injury as well as illness?<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">eg. Post-battle the party medic discovers one of their generals incoherent, shaking with feverish symptoms. It is not actually an illness but a reaction caused by the pain of a ruptured/broken whatever.</div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":977,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","user":"Major","date":"part 07-24-2016, 01:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","name":"Major","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar977_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T21:01:38-07:00","id":936402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bitterWalnut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=936039#post936039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I permit combos between Martial Arts and Brawl/Melee Charms (depending on the form weapons, as usual)?<br /> <br /> My rationale for considering it: my game has a no-PC-death system, that also sort of applies to important NPC's too (plot kills them, not fighting), so one-hit-kills are less of a pain. I do very much enjoy the flavor that Exalts are naturally better at everything, including martial arts. I would apply it to all Exalts, if I did it.<br /> <br /> Thanks for indulging my curiosity!</div> </div> </div> </div>Martial Arts combined with Solar Charms become ridiculous, balls-to-the-walls powerful. If you allow this, I'd recommend at the least removing Mastery benefits, because those got added in when we made the styles incompatible with Solar Charms to compensate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T21:37:19-07:00","id":936411,"title":"","content":"Iron Whirlwind Attack + Fatal Stroke Flash looks pretty good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T22:18:16-07:00","id":936424,"title":"","content":"Any response to my grappling related questions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T00:56:20-07:00","id":936449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=931692#post931692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if:<br /> <br /> <b>Savaging or throw/slam actions/attacks in a clinch apply onslaught penalties against the victim for the purposes of other character's attacks?</b><br /> <br /> Savaging and slam/throwing actions are resolved just like attacks, save that they need a clinch and treat the target's Defense as 0. The victim does not treat his Defense as 0 against other opponents (though he takes a Defense penalty for being clinched). It makes sense that being savaged would penalize the victim's Defense against outside attacks, and that the victim would suffer onslaught for being thrown into a hard surface, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no issue with this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=931692#post931692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Savaging or throw/slam actions/attacks in a clinch can be treated like attacks for Charms that do not explicitly forbid use within grapples?</b><br /> <br /> Savaging and slam/throwing actions are resolved just like attacks, save that they need a clinch and treat the target's Defense as 0. The list of non-grappling-specific Brawl Charms that could thus supplement these attacks include:<br /> <br /> <br /> Fists of Iron Technique (gets you Lethal grappling damage earlier than Dragon Coil Technique, and even after DCT, still adds damage)<br /> <br /> Ferocious Jab (someone outside of the grapple could attack your victim, and even if their Defense cannot become a negative number, without a penalty-negator, the penalty is still there for Ferocious Jab to exploit)<br /> <br /> Thunderclap Rush Attack (you might need to act outside of your Initiative order to get in one last squeeze before the opponent breaks free, and you can even Crash your opponent before you even apply a savaging or slam/throwing attack!)<br /> <br /> Falling Hammer Strike (if savaging and slam/throwing actions/attacks really do apply onslaught penalties that the Solar grappler's allies might exploit... or the Solar himself with Ferocious Jab)<br /> <br /> Solar Cross-Counter (unless you Restrain a victim, he can still attack you; any Brawl-based attack or counter-attack you make against the victim, including from this Charm, should treat his Defense as 0)<br /> <br /> Ox-Stunning Blow<br /> <br /> Burning Burial Fist<br /> <br /> Force-Rending Strike (again, the victim can still attack you; since their attack is definitely NOT their Defense, your clash would not treat their attack pool as 0)<br /> <br /> Blade-Rebuking Wrath (disarm your victim of that knife he keeps trying to stab you with)<br /> <br /> Hammer On Iron (like Titan-Strengthening Method, but Decisive instead of Withering-only, and you don't expend your rounds of control for it!)<br /> <br /> One With Violence<br /> <br /> Cancel the Apocalypse<br /> <br /> Adamantine Fists of Battle (the victim can still soak, so more Overwhelming damage is useful)<br /> <br /> Intercepting Fury Smite<br /> <br /> Fire-Eating Fist<br /> <br /> Striving Aftershock Method<br /> <br /> Incarnated Fury Attack (the unblockable and undodgeable aspects are wasted, but there's more to this Charm than that)<br /> <br /> Orichalcum Fists of Battle<br /> <br /> Rampage-Berserker Attack (again, like Titan-Straightening Method, but Decisive instead of Withering-only, and you don't expend your rounds of control for it!)<br /> <br /> Apocalypse Flare Attack (the range aspect of this attack is wasted, but you can spend your anima banner to add to the damage you'd inflict with Fire-Eating Fist)<br /> <br /> Heaven Fury Smite (especially nasty with Cancel the Apocalypse, Striving Aftershock Method, Raging Wrath Repeated, Incarnated Fury Attack, and Ferocious Jab; Orichalcum Fists of Battle also increases base Initiative by 1)</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of these aren't too bad, but most of them, I'd hesitate to allow while grappling, especially the ones that allow you to reduce or ignore Control costs. And TCRA is too good to expand this way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T08:01:06-07:00","id":936544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=936449#post936449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of these aren't too bad, but most of them, I'd hesitate to allow while grappling, especially the ones that allow you to reduce or ignore Control costs.</div> </div> </div> </div>If so, we need some official rulings. Nothing in the Charms themselves forbids any of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And TCRA is too good to expand this way. </div> </div> </div>How does being viable against your grappling victim make it any more powerful than it already is? If anything, using it in a grapple limits it, since you can ONLY target the person you are grappling. And then, only once without resetting the Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T20:33:23-07:00","id":937904,"title":"","content":"What breaks if I allow read intention actions to be rolled with (Perception + Investigation) as well as Socialize?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T00:33:18-07:00","id":937979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=937904#post937904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I allow read intention actions to be rolled with (Perception + Investigation) as well as Socialize?</div> </div> </div> </div>Twilight Caste Sherlock Holmes characters will become more efficient to build. Unfortunately, the charms that exist wouldn't do much to actuate that sort of rule change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T17:30:49-07:00","id":938447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=937979#post937979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Twilight Caste Sherlock Holmes characters will become more efficient to build. Unfortunately, the charms that exist wouldn't do much to actuate that sort of rule change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda, but that opens up to homebrewing charms for that niche, which I always find an interesting oportunity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T11:32:27-07:00","id":957738,"title":"","content":"What breaks if you let mortal MAists deal lethal damage unarmed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T13:32:19-07:00","id":957813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=957738#post957738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if you let mortal MAists deal lethal damage unarmed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anything breaks. Mortals are allowed to use style armour and form weapons. Granted the text usually specifies &quot;with a charm&quot; for unarmed as lethal so that is a possible warning sign against it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","name":"Major","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar977_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T13:59:41-07:00","id":957832,"title":"","content":"It'd be a teensy bit odd if mortals can stunt for lethal damage on a non-charm-enhanced attack when Exalts can't, but it's a very minor thing and there aren't any balance issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T12:26:47-07:00","id":961164,"title":"","content":"What breaks if you're allowed to use supplemental/reflexive combat charms on spells? It's mostly the Occult stuff I'm thinking, but would there be anything else to be worried about? Combat sorcery could use a boost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11077-thanatos","name":"Thanatos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T12:36:29-07:00","id":961173,"title":"","content":"Well, since most attack spells are Occult rolls, you can use Occult combat charms. And I'm not sure what other combat spells will be appropriate. I mean, it wouldn't make sense to use Brawl charms to enhance Flight of the Brilliant Raptor.<br /> It would make sense to use Brawl charms to enhance attacks with Wood Dragon's Claw... but you can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T12:44:05-07:00","id":961176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thanatos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=961164#post961164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if you're allowed to use supplemental/reflexive combat charms on spells? It's mostly the Occult stuff I'm thinking, but would there be anything else to be worried about? Combat sorcery could use a boost.</div> </div> </div> </div>If by &quot;the Occult stuff&quot; you mean, like, Spirit-Cutting Attack and Ghost-Eating Technique, those already work with attack spells. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T13:25:50-07:00","id":961204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=961176#post961176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If by &quot;the Occult stuff&quot; you mean, like, Spirit-Cutting Attack and Ghost-Eating Technique, those already work with attack spells.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Would any of the charms that explicitly function with other abilities also function with spells?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T14:40:56-07:00","id":961246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=961176#post961176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If by &quot;the Occult stuff&quot; you mean, like, Spirit-Cutting Attack and Ghost-Eating Technique, those already work with attack spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there someplace where that is spelled out explicitly (like, page number)? I definitely could see that being the case, but could also see the opposite being the case. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11077-thanatos","name":"Thanatos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T14:47:23-07:00","id":961252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thanatos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=961246#post961246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there someplace where that is spelled out explicitly (like, page number)? I definitely could see that being the case, but could also see the opposite being the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not spelled out explicitly. Spirit-Cutting Attack/Ghost-Eating Technique can supplement any attack; Death of Obsidian Butterfies is an attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T18:14:37-07:00","id":961318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=961252#post961252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not spelled out explicitly. Spirit-Cutting Attack/Ghost-Eating Technique can supplement any attack; Death of Obsidian Butterfies is an attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind = Blown. I would not have imagined that possible in the previous editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T19:28:53-07:00","id":961356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=961252#post961252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not spelled out explicitly. Spirit-Cutting Attack/Ghost-Eating Technique can supplement any attack; Death of Obsidian Butterfies is an attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are your feelings on combining Death of Obsidian Butterfiles and Thunderclap Rush Attack?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/91-wandering","name":"Wandering","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar91_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T20:29:19-07:00","id":961385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wandering</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=961356#post961356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What are your feelings on combining Death of Obsidian Butterfiles and Thunderclap Rush Attack?</div> </div> </div> </div>*Rereads*<br /> <br /> Thunderclap Rush Attack is pretty specific that it allows you to make one attack in place of your turn that round, instead of instead of letting you take the shape sorcery action required to complete a Death of Obsidian Butterflies. Based on a strict reading, I don't think they'd be compatible (but if it came up in my game, I'd probably give it a Storyteller thumbs up).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T20:45:37-07:00","id":961394,"title":"","content":"Thanks! That was sort of how it looked to me too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/91-wandering","name":"Wandering","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar91_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T10:30:40-07:00","id":964375,"title":"","content":"What breaks if I give Craft the Lore treatment and use different crafts as specialities instead of now skills?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11395-shaddar","name":"Shaddar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"338"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T10:44:05-07:00","id":964387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shaddar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=964375#post964375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I give Craft the Lore treatment and use different crafts as specialities instead of now skills?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a relatively old one around here. I think consensus was &quot;A few Charms that give you free dots in Craft don't work properly anymore&quot; which is generally met with an &quot;Oh well, working as intended.&quot; So nothing serious. Just cut those Charms from the game and you're good to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T10:47:19-07:00","id":964393,"title":"","content":"Becoming the omnicrafter who has no theme to their crafting and simply makes anything they feel like becomes infinitely easier. Certain Solar charms intended to highlight their phenomenal capabilities in contrast to others without those capabilities become unimpressive or useless. There arises massively less narrative value in having more than one person with Craft ability. But, since it's mostly just a savings of Solar XP, it probably doesn't break the game in and of itself;. Works out to a 16xp savings per area of Craft. You might consider requiring Artifacts as a standalone purchase to make it less of a gimme default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T10:54:29-07:00","id":964397,"title":"","content":"What breaks if I reduce the initiative crash bonus from 5 to 2 or 3? I feel like right now, combat is basically &quot;race to the crash&quot;, with one happening in the first round or second round of combat, and then combat is over because the other side gets oneshot. Would reducing the initiative crash bonus help this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat","name":"PraxisCat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12025_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T10:56:29-07:00","id":964398,"title":"","content":"I have the feeling it would mostly result in beating on a crashed opponent an extra round or two when they can't use any Perilous defenses, then decisive attacking anyway.<br /> <br /> I mean, &quot;push your opponent into crash and then finish them&quot; is kind of the core component of the 3e combat engine, at least vs any enemy who isn't adequately protected against such (ridiculous soak or DVs, massive initiative start from join battle)<br /> <br /> To put it another way; players in general, I think, prefer a decisive blow over a death of a thousand cuts. Give me the option of landing one attack for seven levels of damage vs seven attacks for one level apiece, and the former feels better. On the other hand, they prefer being subjected to the latter; dying in one hit sucks and feels like arbitrary dice luck no matter how foregone a conclusion it was, but having had the option to escape, deciding not to, and dying to a dozen attacks, generally people can go &quot;yeah, that was my fault, I own that death&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which is why I suggest to STs on this site, generally save up a couple dice from one or two withering, and deliver a decisive. Nick and scratch your players and they'll feel like the battle was hard fought and won, where they won't feel that if the enemy died while stockpiling the 21 initiative expected to one shot them. <br /> <br /> May I ask the specific reason you want them to not save and strike?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 09-06-2016, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T11:16:53-07:00","id":964410,"title":"","content":"It's not that I don't want them to not save and strike (as a mechanic), it's more that I feel that there should be a back-and-forth initiative exchange which eventually pushes someone back. At that point, I don't care if there's a single decisive attack or not. The problem is that from the very start, from join battle, there's a death spiral, where a bad JB is basically a death sentence, because the first mover will initiative crash them, and then likely one-shot them the next round. I don't feel like it's particularly cinematic and players don't get the opportunity to do cool things, because they're either incapped immediately, or win immediately. An example given is Luke vs Vader as a good emulation of what Exalted 3e's combat should be. Instead, even against tough enemies, it always feels like &quot;Anime Protag vs Mook.&quot; It's just that sometimes the PC is the mook.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of cool stuff in the combat system: weapon tags, gambits, specific-use evocations, certain charms -- that will possibly never be realized because you never need them, because combat is basically a 1 to 2 round affair that is not really that strategic.<br /> <br /> Likewise, initiative shift never happens because the +5 from the crash bonus is such a complete buffer that in 1v1 or paired off scenarios, that once you're crashed, it feels to me like combat becomes a foregone conclusion instead of &quot;I'm on my back foot.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12025,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat","user":"PraxisCat","date":". 09-06-2016, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat","name":"PraxisCat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12025_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T11:20:00-07:00","id":964414,"title":"","content":"Generally, &quot;getting crashed&quot; and one-shot is how most hand-to-hand combat went in real life, so I don't really see the problem with it. <br /> <br /> Sitting there and trading scratch damage seems ..... I dunno, boring. Both for me as ST and for my players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T11:21:41-07:00","id":964415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=964414#post964414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally, &quot;getting crashed&quot; and one-shot is how most hand-to-hand combat went in real life, so I don't really see the problem with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Respectfully; you don't run games with Exalted as PCs, and this system is a cinematic experience, not a simulationalist one. Whether or not it's how combat went in real life is unimportant to me, because I want to focus more on a &quot;wuxia movie&quot; style.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat","name":"PraxisCat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12025_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T11:30:15-07:00","id":964423,"title":"","content":"I've yet to see a bad-JB early-decisive actually kill an important enemy. Don't get me wrong, that +5 makes an early Crash pretty punishing, but not insurmountably so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T11:33:40-07:00","id":964425,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's mostly something you'll need non-Perilous defensive charms and the like (plus good soak) on the part of the defender to avoid. 3e is definitely intended to reward use of armor or other soak charms.<br /> <br /> While generally &quot;this is my only scene&quot; treatment of NPC resources is bad, I think it's okay to let someone who is meant to be a significant opponent go all out with motes and willpower to stay alive.<br /> <br /> 5v1 is a very losing prospect no matter who you are though, so plans to prevent the circle from ganging up are a good idea. Battle groups complicating engagement, secondary opponents, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T11:33:54-07:00","id":964426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PraxisCat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=964415#post964415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Respectfully; you don't run games with Exalted as PCs, and this system is a cinematic experience, not a simulationalist one. Whether or not it's how combat went in real life is unimportant to me, because I want to focus more on a &quot;wuxia movie&quot; style.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And, respectfully, your question was already pretty much answered, both by yourself and by other posters.<br /> <br /> My post was just my $0.02 cents, giving my experiences from both sides of the table. Sitting there, trading blows over multiple rounds is, well, <i>kinda boring</i>. At least crashing the opponent is something to look forward to, a goal of sorts.<br /> <br /> Depending on how you build your opponents, combat could drag out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T11:37:17-07:00","id":964429,"title":"","content":"To be fair, when they said &quot;cinematic,&quot; they only meant <i>some</i> movies. ESB is a good one. The 45-minute lightsaber duel in RotS, is not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T11:48:14-07:00","id":964442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=964425#post964425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's mostly something you'll need non-Perilous defensive charms and the like (plus good soak) on the part of the defender to avoid. 3e is definitely intended to reward use of armor or other soak charms.<br /> <br /> While generally &quot;this is my only scene&quot; treatment of NPC resources is bad, I think it's okay to let someone who is meant to be a significant opponent go all out with motes and willpower to stay alive.<br /> <br /> 5v1 is a very losing prospect no matter who you are though, so plans to prevent the circle from ganging up are a good idea. Battle groups complicating engagement, secondary opponents, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more than even in 3v3, I don't think that our combat has ever lasted past 3 rounds. I don't have a problem with secondary / trivial opponents, it just seems like that +5 can be really very swingy; I've never had an NPC with ~12 or so ini to make a decisive. They usually sit at either 20, or at -2, and battlegroups usually get merc'd after one or two attacks. Then again, this could be the problem with telling human stories with exalted PCs; nothing is really going to challenge them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, respectfully, your question was already pretty much answered, both by yourself and by other posters.<br /> <br /> My post was just my $0.02 cents, giving my experiences from both sides of the table. Sitting there, trading blows over multiple rounds is, well, <i>kinda boring</i>. At least crashing the opponent is something to look forward to, a goal of sorts.<br /> <br /> Depending on how you build your opponents, combat could drag out.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I was merely stating that we have different goals and that the PCs have different capabilities, not attacking you personally.. Just sitting there, trading shots and watching numbers go up and down isn't very exciting. But with stunting, using the environment, trying to stop the fighting with social rolls, establishing stealth, using gambits and charms and evocations, you can get a much more varied combat experience. If my player who has a sorcerer who messes around with fire, wants to stunt fire tricks like burning houses down to have importance in combat outside of the overall narrative. The athletics characters have no reason to do cool athletics things like drawing people away, because combat's going to be over in the next round anyway. Right now, both of those things would just be a wasted turn, because they're going to either<br /> A: get crashed and then get killed next round<br /> B: wasting a chance to crash someone and just kill them in the next round<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> <br /> Yeah, I was specifically thinking about ESB<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat","name":"PraxisCat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12025_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T20:45:43-07:00","id":966564,"title":"","content":"What breaks if you can carry your allies with you when you cross range bands, especially with Athletics Charms like Mountain-Crossing Leap Technique?<br /> <br /> That wouldn't render Strength-Hying Heave <i>totally</i> useless, since you don't always want to enter the same range band that you're tossing an ally into, but it would seem to make SHH's restriction against moving a little odd.<br /> <br /> Wings Spread To Sky explicitly allows a Crane Stylist to drag an ally around (if the martial artist is Defending them), but that may be explicitly stated because the Charm allows the martial artist to FLY.<br /> <br /> So. Where does &quot;dragging an ally around with you&quot; fall? Can you do it without a Charm, or should it require an Athletics Charm building off of Strength-Hying Heave?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, what the heck, SHH requires you to use Strength-Increasing Exercise to the max? That raises the cost of accessing SHH as you raise your Essence and/or Strength!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 09-09-2016, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T01:53:06-07:00","id":966680,"title":"","content":"I assumed you can carry them if you're strong enough, just like you can carry anything else. I don't see why you couldn't.<br /> However, it should probably count as their move action, like when you ride a horse, so you don't have some shenanigans where you carry a guy carrying a guy and string out your move actions in one turn to send one person loads of range bands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T07:58:09-07:00","id":966754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=966680#post966680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assumed you can carry them if you're strong enough, just like you can carry anything else. I don't see why you couldn't.<br /> However, it should probably count as their move action, like when you ride a horse, so you don't have some shenanigans where you carry a guy carrying a guy and string out your move actions in one turn to send one person loads of range bands.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Carrying a guy who is carrying a guy&quot; wouldn't normally be possible without Charms <i>anyway</i>. The middleman has to be strong enough to carry the other guy despite the rough ride, and the bottom guy has to be strong enough to carry two guys while running at full speed.<br /> <br /> When I read &quot;shenanigans&quot;, I thought you were going to broach the idea of a number of allies passing someone forward like a relay baton, with the &quot;baton&quot; ally only using his own movement action to reach the first &quot;relayer&quot; or to keep moving after being released by the last relayer.<br /> <br /> Anyway, &quot;carrying one guy with you without it counting as his movement action for the turn&quot; should probably be an Athletics 4, Essence 3 Charm following Strength-Hying Heave, making it analogous to Wings Spread To Sky.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>But what breaks if you remove SHH's restriction of &quot;first you must use Increasing-Strength Exercise to the maximum&quot;?</b><br /> <br /> The more dots of Essence or Strength you have, the more you have to pay for Increasing-Strength Exercise before you can use Strength-Hying Heave. It's not even proportional to the target you're lifting! A Solar with Strength 2, Essence 1 can pay for one bonus Strength dot and throw the same guy that a Strength 5, Essence 5 Solar needs to pay FIVE dots to throw. That's crazy.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't understand the point of having such a restriction at all. You don't need to use Increasing-Strength Exercise before you use Monkey Leap Technique or Mountain-Crossing Leap Technique, no matter how big or heavily-armored you are. You likewise don't need to use Increasing-Strength Exercise before you use Crashing Wave Throw or Heaven-Thunder Hammer -- not for man-sized targets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T11:13:01-07:00","id":966836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=966680#post966680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assumed you can carry them if you're strong enough, just like you can carry anything else. I don't see why you couldn't.<br /> However, it should probably count as their move action, like when you ride a horse, so you don't have some shenanigans where you carry a guy carrying a guy and string out your move actions in one turn to send one person loads of range bands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Peasant Railgun II: Motonic Boogaloo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T10:29:19-07:00","id":971998,"title":"","content":"I don't know about an Evocation (resembling the DB's Earth theme of stability) that can retroactively prevent a botch. The basic mechanic would go something like this: <br /> <br /> Reflexive Charm (5m): The wielder can pay 1wp per 1 rolled on the botch to fully prevent the consequences. If aware the one that got helped may develop a Minor Intimacy of gratitude for his guardian. <br /> Only once per story. No reset condition.<br /> <br /> I'd personally think this is pretty darn strong and may not even be a good idea to do even with further balancing. But I'm someone that manages to botch with everything under 19 dice quite regulary. Just recently lost a character to a 18 dice roll with 6 1s and no success and just the other session I had 16 dice with 4 1s... <br /> But yeah I botch at least 2 to 3 times per story. So I may be a bit biased. <br /> <br /> What do you think? <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My (mostly) German Exalted blog: <a href=\"http://ryokiseck.de/\" target=\"_blank\">Praise the Spiral!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11185-ryoki","name":"Ryoki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T09:11:59-07:00","id":975966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryoki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=971998#post971998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about an Evocation (resembling the DB's Earth theme of stability) that can retroactively prevent a botch. The basic mechanic would go something like this:<br /> <br /> Reflexive Charm (5m): The wielder can pay 1wp per 1 rolled on the botch to fully prevent the consequences. If aware the one that got helped may develop a Minor Intimacy of gratitude for his guardian.<br /> Only once per story. No reset condition.<br /> <br /> I'd personally think this is pretty darn strong and may not even be a good idea to do even with further balancing. But I'm someone that manages to botch with everything under 19 dice quite regulary. Just recently lost a character to a 18 dice roll with 6 1s and no success and just the other session I had 16 dice with 4 1s...<br /> But yeah I botch at least 2 to 3 times per story. So I may be a bit biased.<br /> <br /> What do you think?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think you need a Good Luck charm, they prevent 1 botch per story. (P580 under talismans)<br /> <br /> Given that talismans are noted as costing resources 1-4 (i.e. they're available with <i>mortal</i> resources, *if* you can find a thaumaturge who's able to make them) I'd say that your suggested power's cost is very steep; I'd be tempted to make it a flat cost of 1WP (maybe 2WP?) but I guess that depends on the WP economy in your game. *shrug*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3890-nsfw","user":"NSFW","date":". 09-25-2016, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3890-nsfw","name":"NSFW","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T17:20:47-07:00","id":976182,"title":"","content":"People have complained about BP/XP split for time immemorial. What happens if you make the XP costs for Attributes/Abilities a flat cost? Something like...<ul><li>Attributes - 10xp per dot</li> <li>Favored/Caste Abilities - 4xp per dot, including the first dot</li> <li>Non-Favored/Caste Abilities - 5xp per dot, including the first dot</li> </ul><br /> All other XP costs remain the same, as do all BP costs.<br /> <br /> For Attributes, that cost means that someone that does 5/5/1 from the start will need 40xp to raise that 1 to a 5, while someone that does 4/4/3 will also need 40xp to raise all three to 5s.<br /> <br /> Abilities would cost 20/25xp to raise from 0 to 5, whereas normally it would be 19/23, depending on Caste/NonFavored.<br /> <br /> Does this break anything, or is the BP/XP split still too large even with this modification?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T00:09:59-07:00","id":976399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=976182#post976182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People have complained about BP/XP split for time immemorial. What happens if you make the XP costs for Attributes/Abilities a flat cost? Something like...<ul><li>Attributes - 10xp per dot</li> <li>Favored/Caste Abilities - 4xp per dot, including the first dot</li> <li>Non-Favored/Caste Abilities - 5xp per dot, including the first dot</li> </ul><br /> <br /> All other XP costs remain the same, as do all BP costs.<br /> <br /> For Attributes, that cost means that someone that does 5/5/1 from the start will need 40xp to raise that 1 to a 5, while someone that does 4/4/3 will also need 40xp to raise all three to 5s.<br /> <br /> Abilities would cost 20/25xp to raise from 0 to 5, whereas normally it would be 19/23, depending on Caste/NonFavored.<br /> <br /> Does this break anything, or is the BP/XP split still too large even with this modification?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is pretty close to what I do, but I add a few extra changes. First, Merits are 3 XP per point, doesn't matter if it has a fixed or variable rating. More importantly, I have completely eliminated BP, trading those initial 15 BP for 50 XP to spend on those new fixed XP costs. The XP needed to reach a new Essence rating is, accordingly, increased by 50 XP.<br /> <br /> Has worked pretty well for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T01:13:33-07:00","id":976417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=976182#post976182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People have complained about BP/XP split for time immemorial. What happens if you make the XP costs for Attributes/Abilities a flat cost? Something like...<ul><li>Attributes - 10xp per dot</li> <li>Favored/Caste Abilities - 4xp per dot, including the first dot</li> <li>Non-Favored/Caste Abilities - 5xp per dot, including the first dot</li> </ul><br /> <br /> All other XP costs remain the same, as do all BP costs.<br /> <br /> For Attributes, that cost means that someone that does 5/5/1 from the start will need 40xp to raise that 1 to a 5, while someone that does 4/4/3 will also need 40xp to raise all three to 5s.<br /> <br /> Abilities would cost 20/25xp to raise from 0 to 5, whereas normally it would be 19/23, depending on Caste/NonFavored.<br /> <br /> Does this break anything, or is the BP/XP split still too large even with this modification?</div> </div> </div> </div>It'll encourage people to min-max with their xp more, and with their bp less.<br /> <br /> I'd rather do it the other way, and fix starting dots and bp rather than xp (I think XP is fine, it's the interaction between it and bp that's the problem), but tbh, doing the xp is much, much easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T01:17:25-07:00","id":976418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=976399#post976399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is pretty close to what I do, but I add a few extra changes. First, Merits are 3 XP per point, doesn't matter if it has a fixed or variable rating. More importantly, I have completely eliminated BP, trading those initial 15 BP for 50 XP to spend on those new fixed XP costs. The XP needed to reach a new Essence rating is, accordingly, increased by 50 XP.<br /> <br /> Has worked pretty well for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just swapped the 15 freebies for 50xp and kept the normal xp costs. That seemed to work sort-of-okay.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T10:03:54-07:00","id":976593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=976418#post976418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just swapped the 15 freebies for 50xp and kept the normal xp costs. That seemed to work sort-of-okay.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even taking away the BP/XP disparity, XP costs alone were already an issue for me. You know, the whole &quot;5/5/1 reaches 5/5/5 easier than the 4/4/3&quot; kind of situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T10:23:59-07:00","id":976600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=976593#post976593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even taking away the BP/XP disparity, XP costs alone were already an issue for me. You know, the whole &quot;5/5/1 reaches 5/5/5 easier than the 4/4/3&quot; kind of situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming 5/5/1 guy survives his bout of crippling weakness long enough to improve it, yes. Incidentally, this edition's a lot less forgiving of having a shitty soak, so consider carefully when allocating those Attribute dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T10:30:37-07:00","id":976603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=976600#post976600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming 5/5/1 guy survives his bout of crippling weakness long enough to improve it, yes. Incidentally, this edition's a lot less forgiving of having a shitty soak, so consider carefully when allocating those Attribute dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who said the 1 is Stamina?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T11:45:35-07:00","id":976638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NSFW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=975966#post975966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you need a Good Luck charm, they prevent 1 botch per story. (P580 under talismans)<br /> <br /> Given that talismans are noted as costing resources 1-4 (i.e. they're available with <i>mortal</i> resources, *if* you can find a thaumaturge who's able to make them) I'd say that your suggested power's cost is very steep; I'd be tempted to make it a flat cost of 1WP (maybe 2WP?) but I guess that depends on the WP economy in your game. *shrug*</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, right! There were Good Luck charms, I forgot about those... That makes it way easier. I just need to convince my ST that I get the chance to make a thaumaturge teach me the ritual. Being an exalted sorcerer that unlocks the thaumaturge merit for free helps with that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> I also asked John over Twitter and he said that even with the steep cost the Evocation would be op if it would apply to every botch. But that was without the &quot;once per story&quot; addition. Just for the record.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My (mostly) German Exalted blog: <a href=\"http://ryokiseck.de/\" target=\"_blank\">Praise the Spiral!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11185-ryoki","name":"Ryoki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T12:19:53-07:00","id":976656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=976593#post976593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even taking away the BP/XP disparity, XP costs alone were already an issue for me. You know, the whole &quot;5/5/1 reaches 5/5/5 easier than the 4/4/3&quot; kind of situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's partly why it was sort-of-okay and not perfect.<br /> At least this way the players can just spend the XP to boost attributes now anyway.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T06:54:59-07:00","id":977155,"title":"","content":"What breaks if i change the twilight anima to give 2*essence spirit familiars?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T10:30:38-07:00","id":977244,"title":"","content":"What breaks if I let my Supernal Brawl player have his bare fists have the stat line of a light artefact weapon? He pays for them with the artefact background and commits motes as if they were an artefact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T10:38:23-07:00","id":977249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=977244#post977244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I let my Supernal Brawl player have his bare fists have the stat line of a light artefact weapon? He pays for them with the artefact background and commits motes as if they were an artefact.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Brawl, nothing. It's just like smashfists. <br /> <br /> The potential for imbalance would be letting a martial artist use artifact-grade fists to combine multiple unarmed styles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T10:46:42-07:00","id":977255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=977244#post977244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I let my Supernal Brawl player have his bare fists have the stat line of a light artefact weapon? He pays for them with the artefact background and commits motes as if they were an artefact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd make them tattoos or something. Or, hell, even a pair of rings that emit an essence field when powered up via attunement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T10:53:28-07:00","id":977258,"title":"","content":"There is a particular brawl charm that's only useable with your bare hands, not artefact weapons. I guess it'd be awkward with that one, but you could just say that charm doesn't work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T12:14:02-07:00","id":977288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=977258#post977258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a particular brawl charm that's only useable with your bare hands, not artefact weapons. I guess it'd be awkward with that one, but you could just say that charm doesn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're talking about Adamantine Fists of Battle, it doesn't do much for you if you have artifact brawl weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T16:27:54-07:00","id":977465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=977155#post977155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if i change the twilight anima to give 2*essence spirit familiars?</div> </div> </div> </div>That will become a lot of familiars pretty fast.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Empyreal Puissance (Greater)</b></span><br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Manse-born<br /> This translucent, diamond-shaped gem has a mote of glowing energy at its center, as if a miniature sun is entrapped within it. Empyreal Puissance allows a character to treat their Essence score as +1 higher for the purposes of Anima Banner effects when it is socketed in an attuned artifact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T10:24:50-07:00","id":979140,"title":"","content":"What breaks if i change deadly predator method to make any familiar gigantic regardless of initial size? (legendary size mouse, king kong blood ape)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11395-shaddar","name":"Shaddar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"338"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:02:44-07:00","id":979899,"title":"","content":"I love the idea of Foe Vaulting Method, but it's...not good in 3e. Spend 3i and successfully roll ATH + DEX vs your opponent's Evasion to lower their Defense by 2? Oh and it's once per combat. And you have to have high Init to use it in the first place! And it's only useable at Close range! <br /> <br /> Just how much more powerful is it for benefit of charm to make an Ambush mid combat instead of just a surprise attack? Maybe make it an Essence 3 upgrade?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11476-tk421","name":"TK421","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T17:39:00-07:00","id":979957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TK421</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=979899#post979899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the idea of Foe Vaulting Method, but it's...not good in 3e. Spend 3i and successfully roll ATH + DEX vs your opponent's Evasion to lower their Defense by 2? Oh and it's once per combat. And you have to have high Init to use it in the first place! And it's only useable at Close range!<br /> <br /> Just how much more powerful is it for benefit of charm to make an Ambush mid combat instead of just a surprise attack? Maybe make it an Essence 3 upgrade?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a number of Charms that key off of unexpected attacks, which is fulfilled by Foe-Vaulting Method's surprise attack.<br /> <br /> Like Throat-Slitting Shadow Atemi from the Ebon Shadow MA. Every extra success on a decisive attack roll converts one damage die into a success. And speaking of Ebon Shadow... it's form Charm would automatically fulfill Foe-Vaulting Method's reset condition if you had Stealth at 5.<br /> <br /> Charms work best in combos, not as single powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:26:59-07:00","id":980103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=979957#post979957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a number of Charms that key off of unexpected attacks, which is fulfilled by Foe-Vaulting Method's surprise attack.<br /> <br /> Like Throat-Slitting Shadow Atemi from the Ebon Shadow MA. Every extra success on a decisive attack roll converts one damage die into a success. And speaking of Ebon Shadow... it's form Charm would automatically fulfill Foe-Vaulting Method's reset condition if you had Stealth at 5.<br /> <br /> Charms work best in combos, not as single powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a beautiful combo, but further inspection raises a question. How does Umbra Noose Execution react with unexpected attacks that aren't created by Stealth? Winging it, I'd say that the &quot;The umbra noose adds a number of dice equal to the total successes she received on her Stealth roll to the raw damage of the attack (to a maximum of [Essence x 2])&quot; clause would simply work with the number of successes on Foe-Vaulting Method's Athletics roll. I wonder if anyone knows of an official ruling?<br /> <br /> Foe-Vaulting Method + Throat-Slitting Shadow Atemi + Umbra Noose Execution is a very deadly trick that only costs 6 motes. The 2 willpower and 3 initiative are more of an investment, but it's still remarkable, especially given Umbra Noose Execution's mote refund! Throwing in Shadow-Stepping Motion seems somewhat optional, but it helps you land every stage of the attack, including the initial Athletics roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T23:50:57-07:00","id":980137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ketrus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=980103#post980103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a beautiful combo, but further inspection raises a question. How does Umbra Noose Execution react with unexpected attacks that aren't created by Stealth? Winging it, I'd say that the &quot;The umbra noose adds a number of dice equal to the total successes she received on her Stealth roll to the raw damage of the attack (to a maximum of [Essence x 2])&quot; clause would simply work with the number of successes on Foe-Vaulting Method's Athletics roll. I wonder if anyone knows of an official ruling?<br /> <br /> Foe-Vaulting Method + Throat-Slitting Shadow Atemi + Umbra Noose Execution is a very deadly trick that only costs 6 motes. The 2 willpower and 3 initiative are more of an investment, but it's still remarkable, especially given Umbra Noose Execution's mote refund! Throwing in Shadow-Stepping Motion seems somewhat optional, but it helps you land every stage of the attack, including the initial Athletics roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say Umbra Noose gets no extra raw damage, because Stealth wasn't rolled if you use Foe-Vaulting Method.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T20:14:21-07:00","id":983110,"title":"","content":"What breaks if the rollover of extra successes on an attack roll to extra damage dice is capped by some multiple of strength?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking x1 for light weapons, x2 for medium weapons, and x3 for heavy weapons.<br /> <br /> I know Flame Pieces need a new rule. Probably attach a (assume strength 2) clause to the flame tag. Something like rapier might include a finesse tag that gives it a higher multiplier as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1067-primefactorx01","name":"Primefactorx01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1067_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T21:35:33-07:00","id":983142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primefactorx01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=983110#post983110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if the rollover of extra successes on an attack roll to extra damage dice is capped by some multiple of strength?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking x1 for light weapons, x2 for medium weapons, and x3 for heavy weapons.<br /> <br /> I know Flame Pieces need a new rule. Probably attach a (assume strength 2) clause to the flame tag. Something like rapier might include a finesse tag that gives it a higher multiplier as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prepare to see an increase in the use of heavy weapons, and nobody using light weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T03:41:05-07:00","id":983236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=983142#post983142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Prepare to see an increase in the use of heavy weapons, and nobody using light weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still don't think that's enough to make heavy weapons not suck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T09:38:53-07:00","id":983370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=983236#post983236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I still don't think that's enough to make heavy weapons not suck.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall someone did the math and concluded that Heavy weapons end up doing the most damage of the 3 types against high-soak foes, so it has a niche. Medium weapons are likely still the best overall, though (superior defense is a big deal). Also, that was probably before Charms enter into the picture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T09:45:43-07:00","id":983375,"title":"","content":"Also, if you're going for a Dodge build anyway, Heavy Weapons don't suck so much. (Kind of weird conceptually; I mean, you can see how dagger fighters go with Dodge, and longsword-wielders go with Parry, but it seems odd to have guys leaping around wielding giant clubs or something.)<br /> There's also the thing that Heavy Weapons get better the worse your opponent is at defending, so against, say, a Battlegroup (whose primary defence is soak and tons of health levels), they're good, but against a Solar melee-ist they're a bit rubbish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T11:23:55-07:00","id":983420,"title":"","content":"What breaks if i makeFlawless Impenetrable Disguise or Perfect Mirror be indefinite duration instead of ending when i sleep?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T11:36:36-07:00","id":983430,"title":"","content":"I don't think anything breaks, it just makes them much better, as you can now hold a disguise for years with no-one having the chance to be the wiser.<br /> I guess one could argue that devalues Lunar's ability to steal someone's identity long-term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T16:24:49-07:00","id":983588,"title":"","content":"Maybe use another widget to extend their duration? Like an Evocation or a Hearthstone? I probably wouldn't make it indefinite, but give it some kind of cost that is tough to sustain long term, like 2wp to extend it by another day and through your sleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T10:06:15-07:00","id":984474,"title":"","content":"What breaks if:<br /> I replace(this charm counts as a pre-req in place of) all dicetrick charms with the following:<br /> Solar (Ability) Supremacy (1 ability, 1 ess): 2m, reflexive: 10's rolled count for 3 successes each. In addition, you may pick one of the following to apply to the roll:<br /> 1) The solar gains +1 natural success to the roll.<br /> 2) The solar regains 2 motes per 10 rolled.<br /> You may the pick the bonus feature each activation and not just at charm purchase.<br /> For an additional +1 wp you may apply both, but doing so causes your action to be noticeably supernatural in some appropriate manner.<br /> <br /> This seems like a useful and at least mechanically fun replacement.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4352-krellian","name":"Krellian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4352_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T10:12:41-07:00","id":984479,"title":"","content":"Everything.<br /> <br /> Basically, there would be no reason not to use it in all actions, getting triple 10's basically for free.<br /> <br /> With a 10 dice pool, it cost 0 in average; With 20, it gives back 2 motes.<br /> <br /> This takes all the underliying math a kills it with a club.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12278,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12278-broken25","user":"Broken25","date":". 10-09-2016, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12278-broken25","name":"Broken25","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T11:57:00-07:00","id":984537,"title":"","content":"Too good? This charm is a bit of an amalgamation between a good bit of other charms. And its good that it clubs the underlying math because the underlying math was unnecessarily complex and not useful outside specific scenarios. Without excellency on a max pool, this is still a useful charm to add (unlike the others), and yes there is a nice combination use with a maxed out excellency. The mote return might push it to being a little too good, but compared to charms that actually do something other than just add dice, this actually ranks as being useful to own in its own right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4352-krellian","name":"Krellian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4352_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T14:29:31-07:00","id":984598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krellian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=984474#post984474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if:<br /> I replace(this charm counts as a pre-req in place of) all dicetrick charms with the following:<br /> Solar (Ability) Supremacy (1 ability, 1 ess): 2m, reflexive: 10's rolled count for 3 successes each. In addition, you may pick one of the following to apply to the roll:<br /> 1) The solar gains +1 natural success to the roll.<br /> 2) The solar regains 2 motes per 10 rolled.<br /> You may the pick the bonus feature each activation and not just at charm purchase.<br /> For an additional +1 wp you may apply both, but doing so causes your action to be noticeably supernatural in some appropriate manner.<br /> <br /> This seems like a useful and at least mechanically fun replacement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that it can actually reliably hit with it's horrific bad touch attacks, Brawl murders everything forever.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10881-anasurimbor","name":"Anasurimbor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T17:12:08-07:00","id":984661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krellian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=984537#post984537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Too good? This charm is a bit of an amalgamation between a good bit of other charms. And its good that it clubs the underlying math because the underlying math was unnecessarily complex and not useful outside specific scenarios. Without excellency on a max pool, this is still a useful charm to add (unlike the others), and yes there is a nice combination use with a maxed out excellency. The mote return might push it to being a little too good, but compared to charms that actually do something other than just add dice, this actually ranks as being useful to own in its own right.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is way too freaking overpowered, for the cost, for the requisites, for the way the game engine works. It is gonna be a complete must buy <b>and </b>wreck the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T17:17:39-07:00","id":984662,"title":"","content":"Natural success isn't defined. I assume you mean non-charm success.<br /> <br /> Also, &quot;10s are 3 successes&quot; is not actually the same as &quot;double 9s&quot; because of Fate-Shifting Solar Arete, First Movement of the Demiurge, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3353-rca","name":"RCa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T10:43:49-07:00","id":984943,"title":"","content":"It takes all expectad probability curves and torpedoes them with a soulbreaker orb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T11:18:27-07:00","id":984961,"title":"","content":"The devs intentionally made dice tricks very hard to get for combat Abilities. Adding them back in is at best problematic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T19:30:40-07:00","id":986519,"title":"","content":"I did mean non charm successes.<br /> <br /> As for cost, in light of all the chatter about it being overpowered I can see it moving to at least 3m and the optional return to only 1m per 10.<br /> <br /> As far as probability curves, on average it adds a single succ for 2m or 2 succs for 3m on 10 dice. That is hardly game breaking. Scales effectively with a higher pool.<br /> <br /> As for hard to get with combat, combat abilities are <i>littered </i>with them. Melee has several, as does brawl, Archery has at least one as does thrown. Now, they tend to be a little more specialized, but that also tends to make them weak/boring/overly complicated.<br /> <br /> As far as charms that exploit 10's, that might actually make them worth a purchase now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4352-krellian","name":"Krellian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4352_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T06:56:30-07:00","id":986733,"title":"","content":"Martial Arts ability went away, attacks with martial arts melee weapons were resolved with melee, unarmed with brawl, archery/firewand with Archer, and any thrown attacks with thrown (attacks with their own unique pools replaced it with a regular attack pool or a complementary skill pool instead. Then Each MA is now based off an ability and the minimums for MA were replaced with that ability such as (just an example):<br /> <br /> Shinning Point being Melee based along with Steel Devil, Ebon Shadow based off stealth, Tiger, Snake, and Crane all brawl, Silver Voiced NG based off performance, Dreaming Pearl based off dodge, RDS based off Archery, Black Claw based on socialize, and White Reaper based on war. There no longer is a supernal MA option, but when you choose supernal in an ability with a MA associated with iy, you gain the ability to apply it to that MA. MA charms are still not compatible with other combat abilities charms unless explicitly stated in the charm description.<br /> <br /> The 4 point Merit is now a 2 point Merit one for each ability with the 1 dot prerequisite (not necessarily brawl anymore) being in that ability. <br /> <br /> What breaks if the above is how it's ran?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T08:06:21-07:00","id":986768,"title":"","content":"What break if i put Thousand Courtesan Ways and Celestial Bliss Trick in the presence charm after Awakened Carnal Demiurge, and expand the purview of Thousand Courtesan Ways to other positive emotions like friendship or respect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11395,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11395-shaddar","user":"Shaddar","date":". 10-13-2016, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11395-shaddar","name":"Shaddar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"338"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T08:46:12-07:00","id":986784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shaddar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=986768#post986768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What break if i put Thousand Courtesan Ways and Celestial Bliss Trick in the presence charm after Awakened Carnal Demiurge, and expand the purview of Thousand Courtesan Ways to other positive emotions like friendship or respect?</div> </div> </div> </div>You give social characters access to an appearance cap-breaker that doesn't necessarily force them to be nymphomaniacs or make some people at the table uncomfortable. Which is a very good thing, at least in my book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T13:03:57-07:00","id":986904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maudova</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=986733#post986733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">MA charms are still not compatible with other combat abilities charms unless explicitly stated in the charm description.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as this is kept, it should be fine as long as you are okay with non-combat Abilities becoming combat-Abilities on top of their normal usefulness for so cheap. 2 merit points seems fine to use an MA for, say, melee (heck, I'd allow it for one under your rules). To add parrying and attacking to Stealth or Socialize, on the other hand, is a tremendous bargain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T11:19:07-07:00","id":988942,"title":"","content":"Deleted 10c","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":12102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","user":"Maudova","date":". 01-15-2018, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T22:54:42-08:00","id":1176193,"title":"","content":"Thinking of porting putting the down and dirty combat rule in my campaign.* Figured it would apply to instances of trivial opponents in areas where they might be obstacles. Any issues that might come up from it that you all can think of?<br /> <br /> <br /> *The rule for those not familiar (Pg 87 of the Chronicles of Darkness corebook for those who want it explained more thoroughly.)<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Usually used if the combat isn't the most important thing, or the players severally outclass the enemy or something like that. Player makes a roll of their combat pool (str+brawl, dex+thrown, etc). This is contested by the enemy either making their own combat roll or an escape roll. If the player wins then whatever the player was hoping to happens, the target is dead, or unconscious, etc. If they lose then the enemy deals damage and potentially comes out with an advantage in the event of a dramatic failure.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T08:10:47-08:00","id":1176287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1176193#post1176193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking of porting putting the down and dirty combat rule in my campaign.* Figured it would apply to instances of trivial opponents in areas where they might be obstacles. Any issues that might come up from it that you all can think of?<br /> <br /> <br /> *The rule for those not familiar (Pg 87 of the Chronicles of Darkness corebook for those who want it explained more thoroughly.)<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Usually used if the combat isn't the most important thing, or the players severally outclass the enemy or something like that. Player makes a roll of their combat pool (str+brawl, dex+thrown, etc). This is contested by the enemy either making their own combat roll or an escape roll. If the player wins then whatever the player was hoping to happens, the target is dead, or unconscious, etc. If they lose then the enemy deals damage and potentially comes out with an advantage in the event of a dramatic failure.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I think the core book explicitly gives an example of this in regards to trivial opponents, so I don't think it breaks anything.<br /> <br /> Also I'm sad this thread fell away, I think it's super useful as a topic. So while others might feel otherwise, I thank you for necroing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T15:50:32-08:00","id":1176400,"title":"","content":"What breaks if Rainmaker is compatible with Crane Style?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T08:31:32-08:00","id":1176521,"title":"","content":"What breaks if you use the organization management system from Masters of Jade as is with 3e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13447-quolise","name":"Quolise","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T08:44:10-08:00","id":1176526,"title":"","content":"If I allow a evocation enhancing sound and scent banishment technique to banish another sense that is not sight? If I allow a upgrade/evocation that that can extend the duration of said charm to indefinite?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T19:23:54-08:00","id":1176667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quolise</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1176521#post1176521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if you use the organization management system from Masters of Jade as is with 3e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Said system wasn't really designed to work with any charms other than the excellency, I think. So, not much really...but you still can't really use the Bureaucracy charms in the Core book.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T00:25:34-08:00","id":1176711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maudova</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1176400#post1176400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if Rainmaker is compatible with Crane Style?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you allow a practitioner of a style focussed on elegant defence to use it with a concealable shield possessing evocations focussed on defence and resisting weather. (Blue jade but also resonant with Lunars as a specific exception.)<br /> <br /> So: <i>maybe not much</i>, but you would set a precedent for also making it compatible with other war-fan friendly styles, such as <i>Dreaming Pearl Courtesan</i>.<br /> <br /> PS: \u200bThe <b>Mournful Crane's Cry </b>charm may need tweaking, or allow Rainmaker to be used with it as though it were a war-fan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T08:26:58-08:00","id":1176777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1176711#post1176711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you allow a practitioner of a style focussed on elegant defence to use it with a concealable shield possessing evocations focussed on defence and resisting weather. (Blue jade but also resonant with Lunars as a specific exception.)<br /> <br /> So: <i>maybe not much</i>, but you would set a precedent for also making it compatible with other war-fan friendly styles, such as <i>Dreaming Pearl Courtesan</i>.<br /> <br /> PS: \u200bThe <b>Mournful Crane's Cry </b>charm may need tweaking, or allow Rainmaker to be used with it as though it were a war-fan.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I just actually turned it into a Tessen and gave it the shield tag. So it didn't set a precedent that other weapons are allowed. I was thinking does it break the game if you can go Full Defense, Defend other, and reflexive counter attacks with a light artifact weapon? I'm just trying to figure out if those evocations stacked with a War Fan combined with Crane and Dream Pearl are broken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T01:55:49-08:00","id":1177540,"title":"","content":"I asked this in 2nd. I ask now again for 3rd ed.<br /> What Breaks if I take away the need for prequistes when choosing charms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T02:41:40-08:00","id":1177544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>light-hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1177540#post1177540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I asked this in 2nd. I ask now again for 3rd ed.<br /> What Breaks if I take away the need for prequistes when choosing charms?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Abilities/Attributes: Charms no longer reflect the capabilities of the character writ epic<br /> <br /> Charms: The entire scaling dynamic in many charmsets stops making any coherent sense<br /> <br /> Essence: Easiest to chose to ignore (hence Supernal Abilities), you just end up with substantially more powerful starting PCs then the games power scaling assumes. If you're fine with that, then you do you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T02:48:23-08:00","id":1177547,"title":"","content":"Does anything break if I let Solar PCs learn Martial Arts styles and Charms without buying the Merit at character creation, if without they Merit they can't spend Solar XP on MA Charms or combo charms from different styles (effectively they have to treat charms from different styles like they're from different Abilities), and purchasing the Merit makes Martial Arts work like in canon?<br /> <br /> The intended effect here is that players who want their character to wield a specific style that fits their theme do not need to make an extra investment and treat it like they do any other combat ability - but someone who has being a Martial Artist as a central part of their concept, and thus is going to want all the advantages inherent in building up a diverse repetoire of synchronized techniques (all the extra advantages that make the buy-in cost necessary) are going to want to make the investment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T06:59:59-08:00","id":1177578,"title":"","content":"That sounds fine, glamourweaver; my understanding is that the reason for gating is so you can't just get Solar Charm-like competence out of your Solar XP without having made an investment (otherwise everyone just picks up a MA Charm or three and the thesis becomes incoherent), but you're handling that in a different way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T20:24:07-08:00","id":1178322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChairKicker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=893458#post893458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I decide not to have a different Craft ability for each, err, craft, and just opt for specialties? You'd start with a free Craft specialty once you start putting points in it, and all kinds of craft would have the same rating: Woodworking, Artifacts, Armors, etc...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=893502#post893502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some craft charms stop working, but those are relatively easy to ignore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a thought on that...<br /> <br /> Arete-Shifting Prana works pretty much the same: 4m, 1sxp, 1wp to switch one specialty to a different related specialty for the duration of one project.<br /> <br /> Supreme Celestial Focus should just let you buy new specialties with Goldxp, but I'm unsure what the exchange rate should be.<br /> <br /> Supreme Perfection of Craft gives you your number of Specialties in Goldxp.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Right now I'm leaning toward just dropping Supreme Celestial Focus and making Arete-Shifting Prana and Peerless Paragon of Craft the prerequisites for Supreme Perfection of Craft. Specialties being cheaper than Ability dots, I'm worried any economy of exchange that would make Supreme Celestial Focus worth the purchase would also overpower Supreme Perfection of Craft and create a massive Goldxp/Specialties feedback loop.<br /> <br /> (any others I'm missing?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-22-2018, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T22:04:08-08:00","id":1179109,"title":"","content":"What breaks if you allow massive strengh differences to penalize Parry?<br /> <br /> I always come back to Dex being god stat for to hit, and then <i>also</i> contributing to damage via threshold successes (for withering at least). Combine that with the fact that in fiction big strong heavy hits are harder to block, and I thought of a houserule. When parrying, compare strength and damage values, and if the attacker has 4+ more damage potential, then the defender is at -1 penalty. Granted this is one more step in an already complicated system, but this way, Strength 5 Heavy Weapon negates the +1 Parry of Strength 3 Medium.<br /> <br /> Phrase it as &quot;If the attacker's strength damage total is 4+ greater than the defender's, then treat the defender's Onslaught as 1 greater for this attack&quot;, that way this would fall under an existing penalty, and any powers that negate it.<br /> <br /> The only part I haven't worked out is how charm damage should affect this, or if it even should. As it stands, it squares up neatly for you have to have 2 orders of magnitude in your favor for this to apply. 2 strength, weapon category, or artifact. Forex- 5 strength and an artifact medium levies a penalty against 3 strength and a mundane medium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T23:16:33-08:00","id":1179120,"title":"","content":"Fighters with more base withering damage being harder to block against is already one of the things withering damage represents, i.e.- you technically succeed in putting your weapon in the way of theirs but the momentum being transferred to you is still enough to send you reeling, thereby giving them the upper hand for the next few moments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T08:28:25-08:00","id":1179208,"title":"","content":"I can see that as being part of the abstraction, but it doesn't actually translate to actually getting in hits. Being able to actually inflict the withering damage it's supposed to represent depends on a successful attack roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":1542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","user":"MoroseMorgan","date":". 01-25-2018, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T09:01:17-08:00","id":1179218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1179208#post1179208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see that as being part of the abstraction, but it doesn't actually translate to actually getting in hits. Being able to actually inflict the withering damage it's supposed to represent depends on a successful attack roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but being super strong doesn't actually translate as being more accurate either. Parrying is often more about redirecting the strength of an attack than to actually block it and stop it cold. This is true of shields as well. Very rarely would you use a sword to straight up stop an enemy's attack since swords can have a lot of momentum and strength behind them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T10:14:41-08:00","id":1179242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1179218#post1179218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but being super strong doesn't actually translate as being more accurate either. Parrying is often more about redirecting the strength of an attack than to actually block it and stop it cold. This is true of shields as well. Very rarely would you use a sword to straight up stop an enemy's attack since swords can have a lot of momentum and strength behind them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, that's why I went with a penalty instead of adding dice or something, as it would still be harder to Parry a stronk attack, and more strength takes more effort to redirect.<br /> <br /> Verisimilitude was only part of the intent on this though. The main point was chipping away at Dex as god stat and Strength as dump stat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T17:42:13-08:00","id":1179373,"title":"","content":"Either way there's not much point in getting weapon damage involved, in fact that might even be counterproductive once artifact weapons enter the picture. Just key it to a Strength difference of, say, 2 or more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T16:21:14-08:00","id":1179650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1179109#post1179109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if you allow massive strengh differences to penalize Parry?<br /> <br /> I always come back to Dex being god stat for to hit, and then <i>also</i> contributing to damage via threshold successes (for withering at least). Combine that with the fact that in fiction big strong heavy hits are harder to block, and I thought of a houserule. When parrying, compare strength and damage values, and if the attacker has 4+ more damage potential, then the defender is at -1 penalty. Granted this is one more step in an already complicated system, but this way, Strength 5 Heavy Weapon negates the +1 Parry of Strength 3 Medium.<br /> <br /> Phrase it as &quot;If the attacker's strength damage total is 4+ greater than the defender's, then treat the defender's Onslaught as 1 greater for this attack&quot;, that way this would fall under an existing penalty, and any powers that negate it.<br /> <br /> The only part I haven't worked out is how charm damage should affect this, or if it even should. As it stands, it squares up neatly for you have to have 2 orders of magnitude in your favor for this to apply. 2 strength, weapon category, or artifact. Forex- 5 strength and an artifact medium levies a penalty against 3 strength and a mundane medium.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dodge becomes absolutely necessary for any combat build that doesn't focus on a heavy weapon. Certain combat abilities, especially brawl and martial arts styles that focus on lighter weapons, are significantly penalized. Non-combat focused PCs with the most affected combat abilities are even further penalized, as they're forced to move away from their non-combat focuses of choice and pick up enough Dodge Charms to remain combat viable. The biggest advantage of medium weapons (their defense value) is often negated, leaving the category decidedly unappealing. Play slows down as every potentially parried blow needs to compare the relevant damage values to determine what the parry penalty should be.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Dex remains the most important combat attribute, it just requires a much higher dodge, since it isn't impacted by the house rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","user":"HighPriest","date":". 01-26-2018, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T12:55:41-08:00","id":1179911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1179650#post1179650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dodge becomes absolutely necessary for any combat build that doesn't focus on a heavy weapon. Certain combat abilities, especially brawl and martial arts styles that focus on lighter weapons, are significantly penalized. Non-combat focused PCs with the most affected combat abilities are even further penalized, as they're forced to move away from their non-combat focuses of choice and pick up enough Dodge Charms to remain combat viable. The biggest advantage of medium weapons (their defense value) is often negated, leaving the category decidedly unappealing. Play slows down as every potentially parried blow needs to compare the relevant damage values to determine what the parry penalty should be.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Dex remains the most important combat attribute, it just requires a much higher dodge, since it isn't impacted by the house rule.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good points, thanks.<br /> <br /> Although, Dodge is penalized by armor mobility penalty, so it isn't quite as black and white, especially with armor being so advantageous in 3e. \u200bAlso, I think Dodge could use the gimme, because until charms into effect in 3e it is pretty inferior to Parry, since it has to deal with mobility penalties.<br /> <br /> I disagree that medium weapons losing their defense bonus makes them less appealing, to hit is already more advantageous than damage, the +1 is just gravy. There was a fairly expansive thread like a year ago where the exact mathematical breakdown of Light V Medium V Hard was worked out.<br /> <br /> DO you really think a 1 point defense penalty would have such a cascading effect on the meta? It didn't seem to be the make or break for &quot;combat viable&quot; to me.<br /> <br /> Also, I already conceded it is one more check in an already check heavy system, but you could ostensibly check it just once and remember.<br /> <br /> I worked out when light weapons would be impacted, and with equal strength is is only if they are wielding a heavy weapon. The wrinkle comes with artifact weapons, and fists. <br /> <br /> Again, thanks for feedback. Just wanted to see &quot;What Breaks&quot; just for theorycrafting, and also because dex god str dump has always been a pet peeve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T00:30:53-08:00","id":1180090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1179911#post1179911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DO you really think a 1 point defense penalty would have such a cascading effect on the meta? It didn't seem to be the make or break for &quot;combat viable&quot; to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could be totally off base, maybe other people would be fine with it, but I wouldn't want to play a part time brawler or martial artist under this house rule. The Medium Infantry QC has 4 higher base damage than a strength 3 brawler or martial artist who has to rely on light weapons. It just wouldn't be fun to worry that my DV is going to drop by half every time I'm attacked by &quot;average guy with spear&quot;, even if my concept wasn't necessarily built around the character's combat prowess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","user":"HighPriest","date":". 01-28-2018, 03:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T09:58:50-08:00","id":1180192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1180090#post1180090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could be totally off base, maybe other people would be fine with it, but I wouldn't want to play a part time brawler or martial artist under this house rule. The Medium Infantry QC has 4 higher base damage than a strength 3 brawler or martial artist who has to rely on light weapons. It just wouldn't be fun to worry that my DV is going to drop by half every time I'm attacked by &quot;average guy with spear&quot;, even if my concept wasn't necessarily built around the character's combat prowess.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good point. Kinda surprising that medium infantry is Strength 3, although you run into the same issue if you wanted to use Dodge and Medium Armor.<br /> <br /> Hypothetical dabble brawler Dex 2 Brawl 2, or 3/1?<br /> <br /> Conversely, would this make you more interested in dabbling with a spear? Would you have ever dabbled in a spear before?<br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":1542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","user":"MoroseMorgan","date":". 01-28-2018, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T20:40:05-08:00","id":1180332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1180192#post1180192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good point. Kinda surprising that medium infantry is Strength 3, although you run into the same issue if you wanted to use Dodge and Medium Armor.<br /> <br /> Hypothetical dabble brawler Dex 2 Brawl 2, or 3/1?<br /> <br /> Conversely, would this make you more interested in dabbling with a spear? Would you have ever dabbled in a spear before?<br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this obviously isn't the discussion for it, but my personal belief is that the QCs are terribly written, and probably not even a good idea in theory. Reverse engineering them indicates that the average stat for a mortal is apparently a 3 or so, not the 1-2 that the book claims in the attributes section. But that's beside the point.<br /> <br /> I'd give my hypothetical dabbler a straight 3 build - 3 in each physical attribute, 3 in Brawl. A base parry of 3 is as low as I'm comfortable with in this system, and even that is pretty low in my mind. Especially since raising that brawl to 5 is so much cheaper in Character Creation than it is once play begins.<br /> <br /> No, I wouldn't be interested in dabbling with a spear, at least not based solely off of this house rule. A dabbler with strength 3 would end up with a damage of +14. Even the QC Conscript with a short sword is at +11 (SUPER CONSCRIPT STRENGTH 4 ACTIVATE), so you wouldn't be getting the benefit of the double onslaught unless you went up to str 4, and even then only on the least worthwhile of opponents. You'd need to hit +16 to affect most mortal level foes, which is str 5 and a mundane heavy weapon, or strength 2 and an artifact heavy weapon. But an artifact is definitely not something I'd think of as a &quot;dabbler's&quot; equipment. Considering how busted the QCs are (hate to harp on this), the only characters regularly being negatively affected by this rule are going to be PCs on the lighter end of the combat spectrum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","user":"HighPriest","date":". 01-29-2018, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T21:20:39-08:00","id":1180339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1180332#post1180332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, this obviously isn't the discussion for it, but my personal belief is that the QCs are terribly written, and probably not even a good idea in theory. Reverse engineering them indicates that the average stat for a mortal is apparently a 3 or so, not the 1-2 that the book claims in the attributes section. But that's beside the point.<br /> <br /> I'd give my hypothetical dabbler a straight 3 build - 3 in each physical attribute, 3 in Brawl. A base parry of 3 is as low as I'm comfortable with in this system, and even that is pretty low in my mind. Especially since raising that brawl to 5 is so much cheaper in Character Creation than it is once play begins.<br /> <br /> No, I wouldn't be interested in dabbling with a spear, at least not based solely off of this house rule. A dabbler with strength 3 would end up with a damage of +14. Even the QC Conscript with a short sword is at +11 (SUPER CONSCRIPT STRENGTH 4 ACTIVATE), so you wouldn't be getting the benefit of the double onslaught unless you went up to str 4, and even then only on the least worthwhile of opponents. You'd need to hit +16 to affect most mortal level foes, which is str 5 and a mundane heavy weapon, or strength 2 and an artifact heavy weapon. But an artifact is definitely not something I'd think of as a &quot;dabbler's&quot; equipment. Considering how busted the QCs are (hate to harp on this), the only characters regularly being negatively affected by this rule are going to be PCs on the lighter end of the combat spectrum.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good points all around. QCs killed my houserule.<br /> <br /> Thanks for this. I'll keep chasing the dream of one day finding the right rules tweak that will make strong a slow types not require low key having Dex 4 to stay competitive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T00:51:22-08:00","id":1180365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1180339#post1180339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for this. I'll keep chasing the dream of one day finding the right rules tweak that will make strong a slow types not require low key having Dex 4 to stay competitive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good luck. For what it's worth, I do agree with the point that Dexterity is too important, I just don't think that this is the way to try to correct it.<br /> <br /> The best solution I've seen is still the 2E merit that lets a character make attack rolls with their strength instead of dexterity. Admittedly, it just shifts the &quot;combat god stat&quot; title to strength, but dexterity still being tied to defense keeps it a bit more viable, especially since 3E only uses strength to generate initiative, not to actually deal damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T14:27:03-08:00","id":1180505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1180365#post1180365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good luck. For what it's worth, I do agree with the point that Dexterity is too important, I just don't think that this is the way to try to correct it.<br /> <br /> The best solution I've seen is still the 2E merit that lets a character make attack rolls with their strength instead of dexterity. Admittedly, it just shifts the &quot;combat god stat&quot; title to strength, but dexterity still being tied to defense keeps it a bit more viable, especially since 3E only uses strength to generate initiative, not to actually deal damage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How about to achieve the goals of making Strength more worthwhile, and Dexterity less all consuming, we increase the amount of accuracy you get from equipment, decrease the amount of damage you get from equipment, and a Decisive attack uses Dex or Str to hit, whichever is greater.<br /> <br /> While having lower damage totals overall could slow down initiative movement, it probably averages out, as there are less potential misses, which can bring initiative movement to a standstill.<br /> <br /> I had also realized that my previous approaches only addressed Withering attacks. It hadn't jumped out at me that Dex is the only attribute included in the Decisive Attack process at all.<br /> <br /> Would need to have a special rider for Increasing Strength Exercise that it doesn't apply to Decisive Attack rolls with Strength. Any other charms like that? That'd probably be the only cascading issue in the Solar charmset, but Lunars will probably be all kinds of screwy with this change.<br /> <br /> I considered that inflating Acc pools would also require a defense boost, but then I have to think about how that would affect decisives, and then consider removing equipment from decisive parry which is just one more stat difference to track yadda yadda yadda. More withering attacks hitting is a good thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T17:07:31-07:00","id":1236209,"title":"","content":"Doing some obsidian circle necromancy to bring this thread back<br /> <b>What breaks if I allow Elemental Bolt to be used with martial arts that use archery/thrown weapons.</b><br /> <br /> I've been thinking of doing this at my table to allow people to take Air Dragon or Wood Dragon and still use their Elemental Bolts, these are the factors I've been considering so far:<br /> -For both you'd need to consider the MA excellency, which gives rerolling 6s on damage rolls, this(in my opinion) is a bit stronger than the archery and thrown excellecies, which ignore one point of visual penalty to the attack and one point of defence from cover respectively.<br /> -The only MA style that has charms that enhance ranged attacks is Air Dragon, and even then only a few.<br /> -There may be other charms that can intervene reflexively without necessarily enhancing the attack, but I haven't found any in these two styles after a quick check, still I'll write this point down since some of you are bound to know the books better than me and may be able to come up with an example.<br /> <br /> As it is, I don't think anything breaks outright, so I'm throwing over to you guys to see what you think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12778-rustedair","name":"RustedAir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12778_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T18:50:10-07:00","id":1236252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RustedAir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1236209#post1236209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doing some obsidian circle necromancy to bring this thread back<br /> <b>What breaks if I allow Elemental Bolt to be used with martial arts that use archery/thrown weapons.</b><br /> <br /> I've been thinking of doing this at my table to allow people to take Air Dragon or Wood Dragon and still use their Elemental Bolts, these are the factors I've been considering so far:<br /> -For both you'd need to consider the MA excellency, which gives rerolling 6s on damage rolls, this(in my opinion) is a bit stronger than the archery and thrown excellecies, which ignore one point of visual penalty to the attack and one point of defence from cover respectively.<br /> -The only MA style that has charms that enhance ranged attacks is Air Dragon, and even then only a few.<br /> -There may be other charms that can intervene reflexively without necessarily enhancing the attack, but I haven't found any in these two styles after a quick check, still I'll write this point down since some of you are bound to know the books better than me and may be able to come up with an example.<br /> <br /> As it is, I don't think anything breaks outright, so I'm throwing over to you guys to see what you think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think wood dragon currently allows you to make ranged attacks - it let's you use a bow as a staff, but to make Wood Dragon attacks you need to be using it as a staff (ie. in melee).<br /> I can't think of any reasons that this would be especially OP. Maybe something that combos to make smashing attacks force an enemy to never reach close range? Or something that behaves poorly with the AoE upgrades. I'd find it odd to make non-air-aspected attacks with Air Dragon Style, but it wouldn't break anything.<br /> Would you allow use with Righteous Devil Style? Nearly all of it's charms supplement ranged attacks. Only things I would worry about are redundancy (I think both have an effect to to double 10s on decisive damage) and range (Firewands tend to be shorter-range than the bows Elemental Bolt more typically replaces)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T19:51:16-07:00","id":1236268,"title":"","content":"You're right on wood dragon not allowing ranged attacks, silly me.<br /> As for Righteous devil style, I guess it could get pretty strong(I get flashbacks on when our solar hit someone with something like 32 dice of lethal damage after 2 turns), but those guys already throw around a bunch of non-strength dependent damage out to medium range(and if you have an artifact, more than your bolt will tend to do), although in a pinch the Bolt could be used when you need to finish someone off (or get out of crash) and haven't reloaded your guns.<br /> Also I was convinced Elemental Bolt doubled 10s as a matter of course but it's actually only for the Fire version.(the RD version cheaper though).<br /> The benefit of attacking with unloaded guns also gets nullified once you get the form and can reflexively aim(and therefore reload) at any enemy you managed to intimidate.<br /> <br /> Overall I guess it's a decent synergy, but nothing seems overpowered so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12778-rustedair","name":"RustedAir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12778_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T10:59:43-07:00","id":1236480,"title":"","content":"I haven't considered RD, but I did allow my player to use Elemental Bolt with Air Dragon. I don't remember the specifics, but even the AoE upgrade was just an expensive way of doing something the style already did IIRC. I reconciled the different elemental enhancements by realizing that the player would be able to do the same thing with an artifact, but this is more expensive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-31T09:43:21-07:00","id":1315710,"title":"","content":"I want to even out the power levels between exalts a bit more for mixed group play. I want to reduce the distance between the two poles of the exalted spectrum while also maintaining relative positions in the 'tier list'<br /> <br /> The first, lightest touch, approach I am considering is capping excellencies at 5-6 dice (attribute/ability/essence + specialty) the idea being that the 'raw' magical power of the exalted is roughly equal between splats so the differences imposed by splat-themes, charms, MA keywords, and artifacts matter much more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-31T09:57:19-07:00","id":1315715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1315710#post1315710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first, lightest touch, approach I am considering is capping excellencies at 5-6 dice (attribute/ability/essence + specialty) the idea being that the 'raw' magical power of the exalted is roughly equal between splats so the differences imposed by splat-themes, charms, MA keywords, and artifacts matter much more.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, my Solar only buys more than five Excellency dice on a roll in life-or-death situations. Not everyone is so quick to blow their load.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-31T09:59:19-07:00","id":1315717,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think that'd work. Solars would still be the best because their charms are overall stronger, then Lunars, then DBs, but the gap would be smaller.<br /> <br /> You could also remove the Aura mechanic from DBs so they could combo their good charms together, that'd increase their power, but they'd still be a bit behind the other two.<br /> <br /> <br /> Though personally, for mixed play I'd prefer to give the DB players some non-charm mechanical benefits (like more experience, more charms, more starting stats, etc; actually they do have more starting stats, but even more so; obviously this can also be done the other way by giving the Lunar and Solar players less stuff), or non-mechanical benefits (lots of jade artefacts lying around, though unfortunately that doesn't work as well as in 2nd ed since Solars are also resonant with them, or have lots of cultures that like DBs, are a bit meh on Lunars, but hate Solars).<br /> That way you can still use weaker DBs for NPCs.<br /> Ie don't make DBs better relative to the other PCs, make your DBs better relative to the other PCs.<br /> <br /> But that may not work as well for you, or it may just not matter if you don't mind DB NPCs being more dangerous to the PCs.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-31T10:03:35-07:00","id":1315718,"title":"","content":"I would say that a big, <i>big</i> thing in flattening the power curve is going to be either removing Supernal abilities from Solars, or giving everybody else something similar. Have access, right from Essence 1, to Essence 5 effects, makes a pretty huge difference, in my experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-31T10:14:47-07:00","id":1315719,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's a very big deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-31T11:04:22-07:00","id":1315725,"title":"","content":"As other people have mentioned, DB Aura mechanics and Solar Supernal are 2 important things to look at. I'd try the following :<br /> -Treat every DB Charm as having the Balanced Keyword<br /> -Make it so Supernal only makes Charms 1 Essence higher available, not all Charms","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-31T11:13:00-07:00","id":1315726,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1315717#post1315717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that may not work as well for you, or it may just not matter if you don't mind DB NPCs being more dangerous to the PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>A secondary goal of this would be to increase the range of challenging combat enemies for celestial exalted whether that be lower powered Exigents, local gods, or Terrestrials. I want the local magistrate and his praetorian guard to be a meaningful challenge to a new Dawn Caste and a suicidal challenge to storm into without a plan. Solars and Lunars can kill the mortal king that oppressed them as part of their backstory. If they want to unseat an E3 dragon blooded who is established in the region, that should be a story that sees a session or more of gameplay.<br /> <br /> I'm of the mindset that it is entirely okay to have the splats have enormous differences in what they can do, but it is not okay to have those differences ultimately result in as big of a difference as there currently is when the opposed dice pools can hit the table. Having one player that can do things which are fundamentally different from others due to the nature of their character concept is fantastic and to be encouraged. Having a character that can out shine similarly built peers by just flatly having twice as many dice to add to a pool is just... I don't know, it's boring to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1315718#post1315718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that a big, <i>big</i> thing in flattening the power curve is going to be either removing Supernal abilities from Solars, or giving everybody else something similar. Have access, right from Essence 1, to Essence 5 effects, makes a pretty huge difference, in my experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree and I think that Azure Winds was onto something with their charm rewrite when they reduced the prerequisite boost from &quot;Treat your essence as 5&quot; to &quot;Add 2 to your essence.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-31T23:38:51-07:00","id":1315827,"title":"","content":"One minor thing to bear in mind is that DB excellencies are much more essence efficient.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s no replacement for celestial dice caps and it won\u2019t overtake a specialist, but the extra effects are not to be sneezed at, and the downside to celestial caps is that you have to judge carefully how much essence you have left.<br /> <br /> Once you\u2019re tapped it doesn\u2019t matter that you can spend 10 motes to a DBs 6 because you only have have 5-8 to spend, and the DB gets more out of their excellency than you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-01T05:20:46-07:00","id":1315856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1315827#post1315827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-snip-</div> </div> </div> </div>One more reason my Eclipse is so conservative with his Excellency (also that he commits to a lot of Social Charms).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-03T13:56:28-07:00","id":1316301,"title":"","content":"The one place lowering the Solar dice cap might cause a problem is crafting. The dice tricks have smaller returns on smaller pools. So I might also recommend cutting down the necessary successes for different artifacts.<br /> <br /> I'm also toying with adapting the crafting rules from Scion, where questing and acquiring materials counts towards the overall goal, so maybe starting with an epic material gives you a few rolls worth of successes, or journeying to a dangerous/auspicious place to craft with your Circle also counts towards your success total.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-20T20:23:31-07:00","id":1319855,"title":"","content":"What breaks if I allow making disengage actions when not in close distance with Dexterity + Athletics opposed roll? Essentially, if I allow rush actions to allow you keep distance from someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-20T21:15:42-07:00","id":1319860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1319855#post1319855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I allow making disengage actions when not in close distance with Dexterity + Athletics opposed roll? Essentially, if I allow rush actions to allow you keep distance from someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm understanding you correctly, I'm pretty sure nothing. I'm fairly certain being able to make an uncontested Disengage action (A Disengage with no enemies in the same range band to oppose it) is RAW. It would still count as an action so taking an uncontested Disengage and throwing a knife at someone would apply the Flurry penalty to the attack but that's it.<br /> <br /> Update: Just re-read the Disengage rules and it appears I might be wrong about that being how it works RAW, but it IS how I've been running it for 3+ years now and nothing has exploded, so I'm gonna stand by my &quot;nothing breaks&quot; until someone who understands the system way more than me says otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":882,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","user":"SamuraiMujuru","date":". 06-21-2019, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-20T21:53:14-07:00","id":1319866,"title":"","content":"It has to consume the character's movement action for the turn, otherwise infinite kiting becomes possible and combat between range and melee fighters breaks completely. The reason why being far forces you to aim AND aiming forces you not to move on the same turn is so enemies get a chance to catch up. Charms that grant you a second move action on your turn tend to be high Essence and once-per-scene only.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T10:54:53-07:00","id":1319966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1319866#post1319866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has to consume the character's movement action for the turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually my intent was that it works exactly like Rush au rebours: it doesn't consume your move action, but id doesn't actually make you move either. It allows you to automatically keep distance to given enemies if they move by one range band on their turn.<br /> <br /> I knew that &quot;kiting&quot; was the primary source of concern, but as far as understand, RAW there is no option to reliably increase your distance to enemies which want to prevent it (you move, they move and rush. If they fail, yo are still at the same distance). This wouldn't still make kiting an unbeatable tactic, since you have to actually win those Athletics + Dexterity rolls.<br /> <br /> What breaks if I introduce the third option &quot;Mantain Distance&quot; which allows you to reflexively move one range band if a given opponent does but doesn't require you to make a move action yourself? This is supposed to model tactics such as crcling a foe with mounted archers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T12:37:23-07:00","id":1319990,"title":"","content":"To increase your distance you have the following options :<br /> -make the opponent prone<br /> -knock them back 1 range band<br /> -use a Withdraw Action","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T14:40:45-07:00","id":1320006,"title":"","content":"Epitome is right, and the main thing we\u2019re talking about here is that last one, bc a Disengage past Close Range is mechanically the same as Withdrawing, just with a big Initiative price tag.<br /> RAW, moving away from your opponent at that speed is withdrawing, and sacrificing your Initiative in doing so. It\u2019s also not possible for anyone not using charms to actually move and aim. They would have to stop and aim, then flurry withdraw and their attack action. <br /> <br /> That makes it pretty useless for an individual rider, even an Exalted one would have difficulty jumping that hurdle.<br /> A Battle Group would have less difficulty with it, but that also gets into Battle Groups spending Initiative, something I prefer to avoid bc \ud83d\ude29 (it\u2019s RAWcompliant and absolutely legit tho. Even quite close to how horseback archery was used historically. Just dramatically limits how much they can do it)<br /> <br /> Your proposal is basically letting them keep their Initiative. I don\u2019t think that\u2019s game breaking, especially given the number of charms that let you move Range bands without preventing you from moving Away. As I read it, the Initiative is basically the \u2018tax\u2019 for possibly escaping the combat altogether, as evidenced by Go to Ground also enforcing a massive Initiative loss should you later rejoin combat.<br /> <br /> That said, I would perhaps consider making it a Latent ability on the mount itself. Not necessarily meaning Only the Linowan-Fleeing-Lizard can do this, but rather that the capacity to carry and obey a rider who is actively looking backwards is a trick you have to Teach your mount.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T15:25:43-07:00","id":1320015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1319966#post1319966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What breaks if I introduce the third option &quot;Mantain Distance&quot; which allows you to reflexively move one range band if a given opponent does but doesn't require you to make a move action yourself? This is supposed to model tactics such as crcling a foe with mounted archers.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you gaining out of a &quot;Maintain Distance&quot; action?<br /> <br /> I assume it would not be usable in the same round as a normal reflexive move or else you would gain distance. If it is just to enable your reflexive move to occur out of your turn then perhaps just let your players do that instead. If you don't change the rules they could achieve this anyway by delaying their action to act in sequence with their opponent.<br /> <br /> As for the gaining distance there are options if you consider difficult terrain there are potential circumstances that you could enable a miscellaneous action to create difficult terrain behind them.<br /> <br /> Also others have mentioned withdraw - withdraw is nothing like disengage. Disengage is an opposed roll. If you succeed you move a range band when they move towards you.<br /> <br /> Withdraw requires reaching a target number of 10 on an extended roll with difficulty 1 and interval 1 turn to move an additional range band. Unless your burning motes and using charms you would be unlikely to manage the extra move every turn.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T21:02:15-07:00","id":1320048,"title":"","content":"Can I add my own questions here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T21:31:43-07:00","id":1320050,"title":"","content":"that depends what type of question it is, if its for clarifications the questions thread would serve more then enough, if its asking on opinions for rule changes, thats here","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T21:59:30-07:00","id":1320053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1320050#post1320050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that depends what type of question it is, if its for clarifications the questions thread would serve more then enough, if its asking on opinions for rule changes, thats here</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been looking at the rules for mage the ascension, and i noticed something. <br /> <br /> So remember all those rules for infrastructural spells, I.e. 'food from the aerial table' and 'water from stone'? Would it break the rules if you allow bigger effects, in exchange for longer casting times?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T22:26:07-07:00","id":1320056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1320053#post1320053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been looking at the rules for mage the ascension, and i noticed something.<br /> <br /> So remember all those rules for infrastructural spells, I.e. 'food from the aerial table' and 'water from stone'? Would it break the rules if you allow bigger effects, in exchange for longer casting times?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not the Mage the Ascension forum. Its Exalted thus I can't answer you since I have no idea about any of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T22:32:44-07:00","id":1320057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1320056#post1320056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is not the Mage the Ascension forum. Its Exalted thus I can't answer you since I have no idea about any of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Inspired by mage the ascension. <br /> <br /> I mean, that's what i meant. <br /> <br /> About sorcerers. <br /> <br /> Food from the aerial table, and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T23:44:53-07:00","id":1320060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1320057#post1320057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inspired by mage the ascension.<br /> <br /> I mean, that's what i meant.<br /> <br /> About sorcerers.<br /> <br /> Food from the aerial table, and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I don't have MtA so I do't know what those do. Is it just &quot;get food and water from the aether&quot;? manna from heaven? If you have a dedicated survivalist* then it might step on their toes, but otherwise it's just a basic working. There's a Thamaturgy thingy for splitting bread a la Jesus, so just dont invalidate that. <br /> <br /> but for real, when are you hard up for food and water enough that getting it via sorcery is gonna derail your campaign? This is pure fluff by the scope of Exalted. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *<span style=\"font-size:8px\">hahahahahahahahahahaha</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T00:56:45-07:00","id":1322904,"title":"","content":"What breaks if I allow kiais from Silver-Voiced Nightingale style to be used in Close range in conjuction with unarmed martial arts charms?<br /> <br /> I know that this might be difficult to answer, but Silver-Voiced Nightingale doesn't look so balanced around exclusive weapon as, say, Righteous Devil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T06:52:13-07:00","id":1322950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1322904#post1322904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I allow kiais from Silver-Voiced Nightingale style to be used in Close range in conjuction with unarmed martial arts charms?<br /> <br /> I know that this might be difficult to answer, but Silver-Voiced Nightingale doesn't look so balanced around exclusive weapon as, say, Righteous Devil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanically not much. It's more thematically that you may have a hard time explaining how your voice is tearing people apart like a Tiger's Claws, dragging an enemy in short range of you with Serpent Style or ripping their still-beating heart from their body with Black Claw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T14:21:03-07:00","id":1323050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1322904#post1322904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I allow kiais from Silver-Voiced Nightingale style to be used in Close range in conjuction with unarmed martial arts charms?<br /> <br /> I know that this might be difficult to answer, but Silver-Voiced Nightingale doesn't look so balanced around exclusive weapon as, say, Righteous Devil.</div> </div> </div> </div>If a character has mastery, I'd worry about allowing them access to all unarmed styles with an artifact, especially one as convenient as VotNB.<br /> Black claw would gain access to artifact stats at all, outside of Wood Dragon's Claw, and also would gain access to free social influence flurries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T15:11:18-07:00","id":1324053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1322904#post1322904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I allow kiais from Silver-Voiced Nightingale style to be used in Close range in conjuction with unarmed martial arts charms?<br /> <br /> I know that this might be difficult to answer, but Silver-Voiced Nightingale doesn't look so balanced around exclusive weapon as, say, Righteous Devil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without Mastery it's already legal as it has the same stats as an unarmed attack at Close and the rules for wielding two weapons lets you fluff your attacks however you want. Play on.<br /> <br /> With Mastery, you've given an always-on, non-disarmable artifact weapon to every style, even styles which don't allow artifact weapons.<br /> <br /> I would not just give the PCs +1 Accuracy, +3 Damage, +2 Overwhelming for free on all their attacks. You're devaluing enemy soak, PC attack charms and artifact merits, and bypassing weapon limitations on martial arts. This is going to make combats easier, making harder to challenge the PCs, and it's going to increase the power disparity between PCs (although the Martial Artist is four merit points and an ability dot down so maybe it'd actually close the gap, not accouting for Solar XP).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T16:24:59-07:00","id":1330315,"title":"","content":"What breaks if DB Bonfire is changed the following way : If you have an active Aura when you reach Bonfire, you can choose to stay in that Aura and you become locked in that Aura instead of your Aspect's Aura.<br /> <br /> i.e. a Fire Aspect is in Earth Aura and enters bonfire anima. She chooses to remain in Earth Aura, at which point she becomes unable to enter any Aura other than Earth until her anima goes down by a level.<br /> <br /> Thematically, this would be represented by the Bonfire anima being a Fire-Earth Hybrid, like what happens at burning anima.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-12T14:43:35-07:00","id":1330623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1330315#post1330315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if DB Bonfire is changed the following way : If you have an active Aura when you reach Bonfire, you can choose to stay in that Aura and you become locked in that Aura instead of your Aspect's Aura.<br /> <br /> i.e. a Fire Aspect is in Earth Aura and enters bonfire anima. She chooses to remain in Earth Aura, at which point she becomes unable to enter any Aura other than Earth until her anima goes down by a level.<br /> <br /> Thematically, this would be represented by the Bonfire anima being a Fire-Earth Hybrid, like what happens at burning anima.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know who you are, but every post you do I feel like we encounter the same problems in game.<br /> <br /> To answer the question, I think it makes DB simpler and more fun (I really like the hybrid element of your Aspect and your Aura during burning anima, and I think it's a shame you don't see it during Bonfire) , which at the moment I consider to be a good thing. I just believe you should also add a rule where Charms that are meant to have restrictions based around Anima/Aura interaction do not benefit from this houserule (given the way you present the houserule I don't believe such a case might exist, but you never know)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-12T16:40:10-07:00","id":1330647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1330623#post1330623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know who you are, but every post you do I feel like we encounter the same problems in game.<br /> <br /> To answer the question, I think it makes DB simpler and more fun (I really like the hybrid element of your Aspect and your Aura during burning anima, and I think it's a shame you don't see it during Bonfire) , which at the moment I consider to be a good thing. I just believe you should also add a rule where Charms that are meant to have restrictions based around Anima/Aura interaction do not benefit from this houserule (given the way you present the houserule I don't believe such a case might exist, but you never know)</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha good to meet a kindred spirit!<br /> <br /> Good catch, I didn't think about the possibility of Charms forcing specific Aura/Anima interactions. If that happens then I agree it should have precedence over this houserule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T12:22:29-07:00","id":1330782,"title":"","content":"Apologies if this has been asked already.<br /> <br /> What breaks if I detach &quot;initiative&quot; aquired from withering attacks from the initiative as the order of action?<br /> <br /> In other words, what are the problems of using a static order of actions and let every character build up a &quot;momentum&quot; to unleash their decisives?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T12:46:43-07:00","id":1330786,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... tbh, I'm not sure anything much breaks. Possibly stuff relating to (edit: ) Onslaught penalties gets weaker, as you'll always recover your Onslaught penalty by the next time a certain person attacks you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-13-2019, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T12:46:44-07:00","id":1330787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1330782#post1330782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies if this has been asked already.<br /> <br /> What breaks if I detach &quot;initiative&quot; aquired from withering attacks from the initiative as the order of action?<br /> <br /> In other words, what are the problems of using a static order of actions and let every character build up a &quot;momentum&quot; to unleash their decisives?</div> </div> </div> </div>At the least, a dozen or so charms become somewhere between &quot;less useful&quot; to &quot;useless&quot; as their whole thing is adding a set amount of initiative to attempt to get ahead of others. Another dozen or so become weaker or useless because they only trigger (or their stronger effect) triggers by shifting your turn order. But outside of charms, it just removes a lever for players to use which isn't the end of the world. And I can see the appeal of one less <i>thing</i> to track.<br /> <br /> Edit: The Wizard of Oz pointed out another one with Onslaught. That's a fair point as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":368,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","user":"The Unsung Hero","date":". 08-13-2019, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T14:19:47-07:00","id":1330818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1330782#post1330782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies if this has been asked already.<br /> <br /> What breaks if I detach &quot;initiative&quot; aquired from withering attacks from the initiative as the order of action?<br /> <br /> In other words, what are the problems of using a static order of actions and let every character build up a &quot;momentum&quot; to unleash their decisives?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really unsure of how this would go in a Solar game, where a Solar fighter has a lot of tools to act on everyone's round. It can be messy already, so maybe it wouldn't make things worth.<br /> <br /> One of the good point I think is that it would reduce the time of inactivity of a high initiative player doing a decisive attack. At the moment, when you have a lot of initiative and use a decisive and your initiative is then set to 3, you do not play for the remainder of the round (which is normal), and then you do not play for most of the next round because with 3 initiative you are likely to be the last one playing, making it feels like you didn't play for 2 rounds straight.<br /> <br /> The thing is, I believe the system bas been thought around this : When you use a decisive, you advance towards victory by wounding your ennemies and adding penalties to their actions, but you also open up your defense and become vulnerable because you are low initiative and other people will play before you. I don't know how this would work with a system that do not use initiative for action ordering.<br /> <br /> How would you decide action ordering ? At random ? With dice pools ? From stunts ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T14:21:13-07:00","id":1330820,"title":"","content":"Also I believe The Wizard of Oz and Unsung Heroes confused Overwhelming with Onslaught but I'm not sure","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T14:24:37-07:00","id":1330823,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you're right I did. Thanks for pointing that out, I've edited it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T15:08:10-07:00","id":1330833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1330820#post1330820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I believe The Wizard of Oz and Unsung Heroes confused Overwhelming with Onslaught but I'm not sure</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1330823#post1330823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, you're right I did. Thanks for pointing that out, I've edited it.</div> </div> </div> </div>What? I had it right the whole time! You can't prove otherwise... &gt;_&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-14T10:28:41-07:00","id":1330944,"title":"","content":"You also lose out on Clashes. The strategy of timing your Decisive Attacks etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-16T15:42:06-07:00","id":1331246,"title":"","content":"What breaks if you allow Sorcery to affect Exaltations. Like say Solar Allfather binds a Dawn Caste Exaltation of his Son to an Artifact Hammer that can only be lifted by the Worthy, as well as binding the memories of his son to the Exaltation.<br /> <br /> Or a Sorcerer binding their Exaltation to a World they Created so it will reincarnate in a line of Witches. Or Binding a Dawn, Twilight, and Zenith together to reincarnate with each other, and maybe bound to the reincarnations of their hosts souls, as well as binding Three Goddesses to steward the Exaltations themselves?<br /> <br /> Or binding a Solar Exaltation to act as a Sun for a World, or as a mystical Eternal Flame in whose embers rests the souls of Lords.<br /> <br /> Or the biggest Sacred Cow, what about Splitting an Exaltation so maybe diminishing it to create squire Exaltations, or shattering it into a host of weaker Exaltations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-17T18:30:15-07:00","id":1331419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1331246#post1331246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if you allow Sorcery to affect Exaltations. Like say Solar Allfather binds a Dawn Caste Exaltation of his Son to an Artifact Hammer that can only be lifted by the Worthy, as well as binding the memories of his son to the Exaltation.<br /> <br /> Or a Sorcerer binding their Exaltation to a World they Created so it will reincarnate in a line of Witches. Or Binding a Dawn, Twilight, and Zenith together to reincarnate with each other, and maybe bound to the reincarnations of their hosts souls, as well as binding Three Goddesses to steward the Exaltations themselves?<br /> <br /> Or binding a Solar Exaltation to act as a Sun for a World, or as a mystical Eternal Flame in whose embers rests the souls of Lords.<br /> <br /> Or the biggest Sacred Cow, what about Splitting an Exaltation so maybe diminishing it to create squire Exaltations, or shattering it into a host of weaker Exaltations.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mechanically? nothing. Storywise? just chuck the whole system into the bin. <br /> <br /> There are only a few <b>iron-clad</b> rules in Exalted: Death is permanent, Time Travel is forbidden, Exaltations are un-fuckwith-able. The Jade Prison was a <b>MASSIVE </b> endeavor and the best that they could do with it was merely catch the Exaltations of the Solars and hold them in a box. And then the box broke. <br /> <br /> So you start with the Mjolnir thing- ok. thats interesting. it kinda fits the theme of getting power via worth. Then since screwing with exaltations is possible (Jade Prison aside) you move on to the Dawn Twilight Zenith thing, well now you have a destined trio. Ok, not really game breaking, but it means that Exaltations can definitely be bound down to certain rules and laws. Make one into a Sun? Sure. you've already established that they can be tied down by sorcery- if they can be tied to each other, why not to a Sun? you already tied one to a Hammer. Never mind that it makes the idea of solar exaltations totally useless because they've been demoted to Divine Batteries. <br /> <br /> <b><i>Split one?</i></b> turn the setting's single, defining characteristic into a mere commodity to be rationed out? Sure! why not. Nothing matters anymore anyway. They can be split. Mask of Winters, Bishop, Her Redness, every last first age Twilight, Ketchup, Ma-ha-suchi, several Fae Nobles, and the Yozi themselves have all totally not noticed this is possible or they absolutely would have done it <b><i> 5 MILLENIA AGO </i></b> when that would have been <b><i>extremly goddamn useful</i></b>. No problem! Now that the cat is out of the bag, there are probably a handful of &quot;pure&quot; solars left. Because the running theme of Exalted isn't the power, it isnt the daiklaves, the DBs, the Realm, the concept of Exaltations themselves, or anything like that: the Theme of Exalted is <b>Mistakes Can Not Be Undone</b><i>. </i>So you can't put the cat back in the bag, can't unring the bell. Bad guys win, good guys lose. You start up a game of Vampire The Masquerade or whatever because that's where everything devolves into. <br /> <br /> So Everything. Everything Breaks if you let Solar Exaltations be screwed with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-17T18:43:34-07:00","id":1331423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1331419#post1331419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Mechanically? nothing. Storywise? just chuck the whole system into the bin.<br /> <br /> There are only a few <b>iron-clad</b> rules in Exalted: Death is permanent, Time Travel is forbidden, Exaltations are un-fuckwith-able. The Jade Prison was a <b>MASSIVE </b> endeavor and the best that they could do with it was merely catch the Exaltations of the Solars and hold them in a box. And then the box broke.<br /> <br /> So you start with the Mjolnir thing- ok. thats interesting. it kinda fits the theme of getting power via worth. Then since screwing with exaltations is possible (Jade Prison aside) you move on to the Dawn Twilight Zenith thing, well now you have a destined trio. Ok, not really game breaking, but it means that Exaltations can definitely be bound down to certain rules and laws. Make one into a Sun? Sure. you've already established that they can be tied down by sorcery- if they can be tied to each other, why not to a Sun? you already tied one to a Hammer. Never mind that it makes the idea of solar exaltations totally useless because they've been demoted to Divine Batteries.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Split one?</i></b> turn the setting's single, defining characteristic into a mere commodity to be rationed out? Sure! why not. Nothing matters anymore anyway. They can be split. Mask of Winters, Bishop, Her Redness, every last first age Twilight, Ketchup, Ma-ha-suchi, several Fae Nobles, and the Yozi themselves have all totally not noticed this is possible or they absolutely would have done it <b><i> 5 MILLENIA AGO </i></b> when that would have been <b><i>extremly goddamn useful</i></b>. No problem! Now that the cat is out of the bag, there are probably a handful of &quot;pure&quot; solars left. Because the running theme of Exalted isn't the power, it isnt the daiklaves, the DBs, the Realm, the concept of Exaltations themselves, or anything like that: the Theme of Exalted is <b>Mistakes Can Not Be Undone</b><i>. </i>So you can't put the cat back in the bag, can't unring the bell. Bad guys win, good guys lose. You start up a game of Vampire The Masquerade or whatever because that's where everything devolves into.<br /> <br /> So Everything. Everything Breaks if you let Solar Exaltations be screwed with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow methinks I touched a nerve.<br /> Cept you are not putting it in a book you are doing it in one game.<br /> <br /> By your reasoning we shouldn't have Abyssals or Infernals? Especially since it took over 5k years to achieve them so they shouldn't exist?<br /> <br /> And binding Exaltations could be curses or whims of the Exalted themselves. And if say you bound one into a Sun you could still in theory pluck it out.<br /> <br /> Just because you can do something doesn't mean it would be easy, even if you could destroy Exaltations I don't think the Sidereals would have the resources to do it.<br /> <br /> I don't mind even if in the Primordial War a handful of Exalted were permanently lost, either pushed outside the Universe or obliterated with the Deathnell of a Primordials or Primordial Warmachine.<br /> <br /> And the split Idea is basically me just thinking about the Imbued and how the Solars could have been broken because they were too mighty.<br /> <br /> And the fact that you can't undo it is the point... And why would Ma-ha-suchi want to split Exaltations I don't follow you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-17T19:05:32-07:00","id":1331429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1331423#post1331423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow methinks I touched a nerve.<br /> Cept you are not putting it in a book you are doing it in one game.<br /> <br /> By your reasoning we shouldn't have Abyssals or Infernals? Especially since it took over 5k years to achieve them so they shouldn't exist?<br /> <br /> And binding Exaltations could be curses or whims of the Exalted themselves. And if say you bound one into a Sun you could still in theory pluck it out.<br /> <br /> Just because you can do something doesn't mean it would be easy, even if you could destroy Exaltations I don't think the Sidereals would have the resources to do it.<br /> <br /> I don't mind even if in the Primordial War a handful of Exalted were permanently lost, either pushed outside the Universe or obliterated with the Deathnell of a Primordials or Primordial Warmachine.<br /> <br /> And the split Idea is basically me just thinking about the Imbued and how the Solars could have been broken because they were too mighty.<br /> <br /> And the fact that you can't undo it is the point... And why would Ma-ha-suchi want to split Exaltations I don't follow you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because he hates the Solars? <br /> <br /> Because Abyssals and Infernals still have a solar exaltation, only that they're slightly shifted? The Exaltations aren't split or broken. They're re-orientated. Like how you can change the configuration of a program or machine, but you yourself can't damage it. You can use the exaltation as a source of metaphysical and essence power, but you can't change it at its core. That is, Excellence and Perfection conceptualised. <br /> <br /> And you have to ask yourself. The Primordials, at the base, are all-surpassingly, all-consumingly good at anything they turn their minds to. So powerful that multiple exalts, over the generations, each of them a hero that can make entire armies quake in their boots, had to die continuously to even kill several of them. And you want to give them a way to split apart and weaken the powers of their core enemies? Then questions will have to be asked, like 'Why didn't the Makers of the Universe, the ones who invented the concepts of Dance, Distance, Linear time, and Spatial relationships, not do this to the beings that were killing them?' The Answer would nominally be 'Because the Exaltations were indestructible. If the Mouth of Oblivion was to consume all, there would still be 1,000 exaltations, floating around the mouth of the void like a thousand shining stars, waiting for one more hero to grant power to. <br /> <br /> Yes, a handful of Exalted can be permanently lost. Maybe. But it costs a primordial to blow them up. They're not something to be destroyed so cheaply by something like <i>Sorcery</i><br /> <br /> As for how 'not being able to undo it is the point'. Well, that's cause you got your wires crossed. The mistake isn't splitting the Exaltation. Its creating the Exaltation at all.<br /> <br /> The Exaltations are miracles, superweapons capable of binding to a normal human and granting him immense power at a base, Your baseline exalted with excellencies alone can outfight, out talk, and outsmart 90% of everyone he meets. And he gets stronger. Again and again. The Theme of Solars is Excel Beyond all limits. They keep on getting stronger and stronger and stronger. Give him a gun, and he'll soon be sniping with the rest of them, then start evolving to using pistols to blow up tanks and take down satellites. Give him a computer, and he'll take over the world, smashing apart firewalls and backdoors like it was nothing. Give him a scalpel and a booklet on medicine, and he'll be curing cancer with his bare hands. There is no guaranteed way to keep yourself safe from an Exalted. <br /> <br /> The Solars/ Exalted had shaping defenses, Perfect Defenses, and Ghost Eating Technique. They were weapons that were aimed to murder the creators of reality, and they succeeded. After the war, the Unconquered Sun and the Incarna gifted them Creation... because they realized that at this point, the Exalted Host can murder the gods, topple their thrones, and take the Games of Divinity for themselves. Autochthon find himself fucked over, first by being forced to cripple his chosen race, then he fled to another dimension for fear of his life. <br /> <br /> The Primary Theme of Exalted is 'mistakes cannot be undone'. And the Exaltations were one of the biggest mistakes of them all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-17T20:19:17-07:00","id":1331433,"title":"","content":"I feel that saying Exaltations were one of the biggest mistakes of them all, is needlessly trying to subvert expectations, they are what they are. The Primordial War brought peace to humanity but they committed Genocide unseen in Creation even with the Great Contagion Balorian Crusade.<br /> <br /> I didn't say you destroy Exaltations with Sorcery.<br /> <br /> I did say maybe use Sorcerous Workings to tamper with them, or even artifacts as that is what Monstrances are.<br /> <br /> And I do feel it would be poignant if a handful of immortal Exaltations were lost in the War.<br /> <br /> And its silly and lacks gravity if there was no way for Exalted to be beaten and permanently lost. I feel they probably almost lost lost of times, like things where the Primordials almost wiped out humanity a few times with a disease or a dance.<br /> <br /> I just believe it wasn't easy to destroy Exaltations. The immutable rules are no time travel and no resurrection, not Exaltations can not be messed with at all, unless for some reason you want to invert them to be Abyssal or corrupt them to Infernal essence.<br /> <br /> We already had methods to bottle the genie back up, the Jade Prison, and Lytek's Cabinet and other artifacts. They are just expensive and well guarded and flawed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-17T21:26:26-07:00","id":1331438,"title":"","content":"logic dictates if you can either destroy exaltations or alter them permanently with sorcery, then it must mean that the reverse is true too, which can flip the balance of power quite badly. A can of worms best not to get into. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2610-lycaniz","name":"lycaniz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2610_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T04:53:30-07:00","id":1332101,"title":"","content":"What Breaks if you allow players to roll initiative with their fighting abilities instead of Awareness ?<br /> <br /> Here is my analysis : Most players I play with take awareness to be good in fight, and as a bonus they are also good at seeing stuff.<br /> <br /> The problem I have with it is multi-layered :<br /> First, it makes one ability a go-to for everyone. Some characters can afford not to do this way (Stealth Solar, for example). I don't really like the &quot;Everyone got to have exactly this thing to fight good&quot;, and since initiative is extremely important in fight, people take it.<br /> <br /> Second, it makes using stealth and larcin NPC extremely hard, because of the first point. Since everyone takes a lot in awareness, your better-than-average stealth guy never stands a chance because the Dawn + whatever 1 or 2 good fighting guys are here with almost maximum stats in Awareness.<br /> <br /> So I'm wondering if I can propose to players to roll with Wits + Whatever combat ability for Join Battle, as an alternative. My hope is that players who want to go for extremely perceptive characters will still go for Awareness, and they still can roll Awareness + Wits for Join Battle, and other combat oriented characters will stop spending too much points on things they have no interest in, and also improve the opportunities of NPCs (or even PCs, because if you are not a Night Supernal Stealth or Larcin GL hiding stuff from your party when they all throw 16-20 dices to spot things) to do fun shady things.<br /> <br /> Concerning Charms that specifically interact with Join Battle, like Awakening Eye (Exalted 3e core), I'mthinking about making it bridge from other combat abilities at a slightly higher cost in Charm pre-requisite, so fighters who want especially high initiative can do it. This or just tell them to buy Awareness Charms.<br /> <br /> Also I'm aware Awareness (ahah) has double 9, reroll 6 and so on, while most fighting abilities do not. I think mostly it's not a bother to me, except if you find some strange case where it would lead to a 10 initiative difference on average.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T05:23:55-07:00","id":1332103,"title":"","content":"I don't think anything breaks per se, but since Join Battle replacers tend to be Charm effects, I would put that effect in custom Charms to stay consistent. Like you make a custom Charm for each of Archery, Brawl, Melee and Thrown that lets the user Join Battle with that Ability. You could add some bonus effects depending on the Ability, the same way Stealth gets a Stealth attempt (i.e. ranged abilities get a free Aim action or something like that), that way the alternate Join Battle Charms could remain appealing even though Awareness would still have the highest possible number of successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 08-22-2019, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T05:45:32-07:00","id":1332110,"title":"","content":"Tbh, I don't think it'd make a huge difference. It'd just make combat characters a bit more focused. That's not something I want, but others might.<br /> <br /> Personally, I like combatants having to buy more than just Melee. Melee makes attacks and defends. If you've got Melee 5, that's 90% of the rolls you need to make in combat. But you still need Dodge to disengage (as I discovered when my elite swordsman got stuck fighting some mortal guards and couldn't get through to the Dawn he was trying to ambush), Awareness to spot ambushes and get the drop on your enemies, Resistance against poison, Integrity against fear, Athletics or Ride to chase fleeing) enemies (or horse archers and skirmishers), War to coordinate your allies, etc. So you can't just be Sword McSword, Exalt of Swords. You have to bring in other things.<br /> <br /> And let's not forget that Melee and Awareness (and Resistance and Socialise and Bureaucracy and Sail) cost exactly the same; ie the game's designers think they're equally good, and the character system treats them as if they're equal choices. But judging from the number of characters with Melee 5 vs the number of characters with Linguistics 5, I'd say players don't value them equally, they consider Melee and Brawl an incredibly good value choice (Thrown and Archery not so much, since they don't give you Parry or defensive charms. Martial Arts is in the middle, it gives you Parry but it does cost more).<br /> <br /> And by bringing in other abilities to combat, it also means that the characters who've gone for other things can feel like they have a &quot;thing&quot; in combat. Sure, the professional thief with amazing awareness of his surroundings, so he never gets caught, may not have the same offensive capability as the Dawn overall, but at least she's got good Initiative. Similarly to how the Zenith ascetic also doesn't have much in the way of offensive capibility, but if you're fighting an enemy who relies on poison, his enormous Resistance will impress everyone as he shrugs off venoms and toxins like they're nothing.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it can actually also help differentiate the combat characters in more ways than just their Melee or Brawl score.<br /> <br /> We recently did a big fight in my essence 1 Lunars game, and it turned out several of the non-combat characters had appalling initiative. The Full Moon had great initiative. Was that because he had a high combat rating? No, actually the Changing Moon is a skilled archer, the Casteless merchant an excellent swordsman, the Tarzan-expy is amazing at ape-wrestling and slamming enemies with his giant ape fists.<br /> But the Full Moon, as well as having an amazing combat pool, has an amazing Join Battle as well. While the Changing Moon archer was rolling her 2 or 3 dice for Join Battle, he was rolling 13 dice.<br /> <br /> It's really easy to get a combat ability at 5 at character creation. But your Dawns, etc, shine because they've invested in Melee <i>and</i> Awareness <i>and</i> Athletics <i>and</i> Resistance.<br /> (Though if you want to reduce the difference in skill between combat characters and non-combat characters, you may not want that.)<br /> <br /> <br /> I'll point out that there are a few charms that change Join Battle calculations; Solar Stealth lets you roll Dex+Stealth for JB, Lunar Perception lets you roll Per+Awareness. But no charm lets you swap<br /> <br /> As a final point, I'll point out that way surprise attacks work.<br /> <br /> Many people find ambushes in Exalted 3e really weird. They're quite unintuitive. There's no surprise round like in most games. First, you get to the range you want undetected. Then you announce that you're attacking... and make opposed Join Battle. If you win, you make a surprise attack, if you lose, you don't.<br /> <br /> But from the defenders perspective, it does make some sense; if they roll well on Wits+Awareness, they detect the ambush, if they don't, then they don't. If they're rolling Wits+Brawl... well how does Brawl help them detect a sniper?<br /> <br /> <br /> Overall, I don't think it's a great idea... but I don't think it'll break much, tbh.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T06:25:08-07:00","id":1332114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1332110#post1332110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And let's not forget that Melee and Awareness (and Resistance and Socialise and Bureaucracy and Sail) cost exactly the same; ie the game's designers think they're equally good, and the character system treats them as if they're equal choices</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with everything you said except this.<br /> <br /> Holden explicitly said he did not consider all Abilities to be of equal worth and said that a lack of balance was a deliberate design choice. (Think it was here, may have been RPGnet.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T06:47:04-07:00","id":1332117,"title":"","content":"I mostly do not agree with anything you said but the point about ambushes seems like a really valid point. I'll post later to answer your comments in more details","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T07:00:07-07:00","id":1332118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1332114#post1332114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holden explicitly said he did not consider all Abilities to be of equal worth and said that a lack of balance was a deliberate design choice. (Think it was here, may have been RPGnet.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not know that. Can't say I agree with that design choice, but it's a ship that's long since sailed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T07:02:01-07:00","id":1332119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1332117#post1332117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mostly do not agree with anything you said but the point about ambushes seems like a really valid point. I'll post later to answer your comments in more details</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of what I said is subjective; things I think are good for the game. But that obviously depends on the nature of your game, the players, etc, etc.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T07:26:28-07:00","id":1332124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1332110#post1332110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll point out that there are a few charms that change Join Battle calculations; Solar Stealth lets you roll Dex+Stealth for JB, Lunar Perception lets you roll Per+Awareness. But no charm lets you swap<br /> <br /> As a final point, I'll point out that way surprise attacks work.<br /> <br /> Many people find ambushes in Exalted 3e really weird. They're quite unintuitive. There's no surprise round like in most games. First, you get to the range you want undetected. Then you announce that you're attacking... and make opposed Join Battle. If you win, you make a surprise attack, if you lose, you don't.<br /> <br /> But from the defenders perspective, it does make some sense; if they roll well on Wits+Awareness, they detect the ambush, if they don't, then they don't. If they're rolling Wits+Brawl... well how does Brawl help them detect a sniper?<br /> <br /> <br /> Overall, I don't think it's a great idea... but I don't think it'll break much, tbh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically Stealth characters can already &quot;detect ambushes&quot; by rolling Dex + Stealth, so it wouldn't be any wonkier than how things already work.<br /> <br /> My understanding from asking Vance about ambushes is that whenever the combat engine gets revved up, all ambush targets get a cinematic sixth-sense warning that something is wrong - the Join Battle roll is really just checking whether the ambusher can act before the target has time to ready themselves against an unknown threat, downgrading the ambush to an unexpected attack. So it's not necessary for the Join Battle roll to use Abilities that detect ambushes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 08-22-2019, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T07:42:34-07:00","id":1332126,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think it really breaks anything exactly. As wizard points out it does make it easier to become the perfect 5 stat combatant. If the characters just have awareness for combat purposes though you might still get a character to sneak up on them with appropriate penalties to the awareness roll. If it\u2019s nearly pitch black and in proximity to a waterfall or windstorm that\u2019s a pretty hefty penalty to the perception. It won\u2019t hold up in the face of awareness charms but that\u2019s kind of the way that goes.<br /> <br /> Wait, I didn\u2019t see the numbers you were posting at first, are they first throwing a full excellency into their perception checks and then again into join battle? I don\u2019t know if that\u2019s sustainable. After a fight or two like that they\u2019ll be almost empty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 08-22-2019, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T10:25:08-07:00","id":1332147,"title":"","content":"I'll try not to argue too much about Initiative and the way the game works because the thread os not meant for this. I just want to answer people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think anything breaks per se, but since Join Battle replacers tend to be Charm effects, I would put that effect in custom Charms to stay consistent. Like you make a custom Charm for each of Archery, Brawl, Melee and Thrown that lets the user Join Battle with that Ability. You could add some bonus effects depending on the Ability, the same way Stealth gets a Stealth attempt (i.e. ranged abilities get a free Aim action or something like that), that way the alternate Join Battle Charms could remain appealing even though Awareness would still have the highest possible number of successes. </div> </div> </div>I think I overall decrease the complexity of the game more by stating &quot;New general rule is you Join Battle with Wits + Combat Ability or Awareness&quot; rather than &quot;There is now a non written specific Charm for which ability that changes the rules of the game with some bonus I haven't decided&quot;. If I want to somehow houserule stuff, I better have them being as simple as possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tbh, I don't think it'd make a huge difference. It'd just make combat characters a bit more focused. That's not something I want, but others might.<br /> <br /> Personally, I like combatants having to buy more than just Melee. Melee makes attacks and defends. If you've got Melee 5, that's 90% of the rolls you need to make in combat. But you still need Dodge to disengage (as I discovered when my elite swordsman got stuck fighting some mortal guards and couldn't get through to the Dawn he was trying to ambush), Awareness to spot ambushes and get the drop on your enemies, Resistance against poison, Integrity against fear, Athletics or Ride to chase fleeing) enemies (or horse archers and skirmishers), War to coordinate your allies, etc. So you can't just be Sword McSword, Exalt of Swords. You have to bring in other things. </div> </div> </div>From my experience, combat characters are already focused on combat, so giving them opportunity so save a few mandatory points on Awareness to be used in Bureaucracy, Linguistics or whatever would be an improvements in my games. I don't think I have seen a single character with less than 4 in Awareness in the 20 or so chatacters players around me built, and maybe 2 of them decided to take Awareness because they wanted to be good at seeing things, the rest wanted it because it makes them better in fight, and seeing things was an interesting side-effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And by bringing in other abilities to combat, it also means that the characters who've gone for other things can feel like they have a &quot;thing&quot; in combat. Sure, the professional thief with amazing awareness of his surroundings, so he never gets caught, may not have the same offensive capability as the Dawn overall, but at least she's got good Initiative. Similarly to how the Zenith ascetic also doesn't have much in the way of offensive capibility, but if you're fighting an enemy who relies on poison, his enormous Resistance will impress everyone as he shrugs off venoms and toxins like they're nothing. </div> </div> </div>That's literally half of my main argument. Stop having everyone be an Awareness champion lookalike and give them freedom to invest in other Abilities that may shine differently in combat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While the Changing Moon archer was rolling her 2 or 3 dice for Join Battle, he was rolling 13 dice. </div> </div> </div>I do not mean to judge you as an ST or any of your players, but if any of my players stated &quot;I want to play an archer/someone who can fight&quot;, I would warn them at least three times to take a good score in Awareness, because it is just really good, and when one of my player says &quot;I want to be a good fighter&quot; I don't feel like I'm helping them making a good fighter if I don't advice them to take a good score in Awareness.<br /> <br /> As for your point about Ambushes, Epitome eventually gave a good advice on how to deal with it, so I believe I'm going to use that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don\u2019t think it really breaks anything exactly. As wizard points out it does make it easier to become the perfect 5 stat combatant. If the characters just have awareness for combat purposes though you might still get a character to sneak up on them with appropriate penalties to the awareness roll. If it\u2019s nearly pitch black and in proximity to a waterfall or windstorm that\u2019s a pretty hefty penalty to the perception. It won\u2019t hold up in the face of awareness charms but that\u2019s kind of the way that goes. </div> </div> </div>As I said my perfect combattant are already perfect combattant, Awareness or not.<br /> <br /> For your second point, it's true I can to that, but I want also more freedom to explore stealth and larcin without too much restrictions only because every player rolls 16 dice at minimums before penalties.<br /> <br /> Thanks all for your answers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T11:13:47-07:00","id":1332151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1332147#post1332147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I overall decrease the complexity of the game more by stating &quot;New general rule is you Join Battle with Wits + Combat Ability or Awareness&quot; rather than &quot;There is now a non written specific Charm for which ability that changes the rules of the game with some bonus I haven't decided&quot;. If I want to somehow houserule stuff, I better have them being as simple as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh sure, if custom Charms aren't your style then keeping it simple works just as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T12:58:34-07:00","id":1332173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1332147#post1332147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think I have seen a single character with less than 4 in Awareness in the 20 or so chatacters players around me built, and maybe 2 of them decided to take Awareness because they wanted to be good at seeing things, the rest wanted it because it makes them better in fight, and seeing things was an interesting side-effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. If every single character has Awareness 4+, then yeah, I can see why you'd want to do something about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do not mean to judge you as an ST or any of your players, but if any of my players stated &quot;I want to play an archer/someone who can fight&quot;, I would warn them at least three times to take a good score in Awareness, because it is just really good, and when one of my player says &quot;I want to be a good fighter&quot; I don't feel like I'm helping them making a good fighter if I don't advice them to take a good score in Awareness. </div> </div> </div>She was a social character, a Changing Moon. Just one with Dex 4, Archery 3 or 4 (I forget) and a Moonsilver powerbow. My point is that having an artefact weapon and good main stats didn't let her compete with the Full Moon (who also has an artefact weapon), as I don't think it should (since obviously she blows him out of the water in social stats) because he's invested in all of the secondary combat abilities, not just the main one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For your second point, it's true I can to that, but I want also more freedom to explore stealth and larcin without too much restrictions only because every player rolls 16 dice at minimums before penalties. </div> </div> </div>For my group, this isn't the case, but I can definitely see how if it was, I'd want to do the same as you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T19:03:03-07:00","id":1332213,"title":"","content":"My Eclipse has Awareness 3; I was actually going to put it even lower, but since he\u2019s a vigilante detective, I thought it might be weird if he didn\u2019t notice things. <br /> <br /> (He uses Stealth for Join Battle rolls via a Charm.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T10:03:07-07:00","id":1333114,"title":"","content":"What breaks if I make the mounting -1 penalty for ammunition checks a mounting +1 difficulty instead? I\u2019ve never used the ammunition system before, mostly because I didn\u2019t really understand it when I first read through 3e and also thought that it was a dex+archery roll rather than straight archery and pretty pointlessly easy. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m also not sure if successfully scavenging ammunition resets the penalty, if it doesn\u2019t then I think mounting difficulty is definitely too harsh, if it does then it might give the mechanic slightly more bite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T13:30:57-07:00","id":1333159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1333114#post1333114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I make the mounting -1 penalty for ammunition checks a mounting +1 difficulty instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I can tell, nothing - no charms or evocations currently in print that I can find ignore or change penalties for ammunition checks, so there's really no difference mechanically. I suppose a penalty is technically capable of rendering it impossible to roll, whereas increasing difficulty doesn't, but I doubt that's much of a change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve never used the ammunition system before,</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it gets very little use, in my experience. I'm not sure I've <i>ever</i> called for an ammunition check in my own game. 5 rounds is just a bit too long, to be honest - very few fights last that long in Exalted 3e. To make it a bit more relevant, I'd probably say that characters should roll an ammunition check at the <i>start</i> of a fight as well, with penalties if they have had fights before and haven't had a chance to scavenge for ammo or otherwise collect it. If you fail, you only have one shot, while if you succeed, you get turns equal to your successes before you have to roll another check.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">and also thought that it was a dex+archery roll rather than straight archery and pretty pointlessly easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, a straight Archery (or Thrown) roll is pretty weird. I think that might be the only thing in the system that calls for that? If not, it's certainly quite rare. Personally, I'd make that a [Wits + (Archery or Thrown)] roll, since otherwise a Solar archer would be getting less benefit out of their Excellency than a DB would, and a Lunar would technically not be able to use an Excellency <i>at all</i>. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m also not sure if successfully scavenging ammunition resets the penalty, if it doesn\u2019t then I think mounting difficulty is definitely too harsh, if it does then it might give the mechanic slightly more bite.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that scavenging ammo should reset the penalty. The penalty exists to represent the fact that as you fire your store of ammo, you're more and more likely to run out. Once you scavenge some, you've got a stock again. Mind, it's probably reasonable to impose a penalty (or higher difficulty) on future <i>scavenging</i> rolls once you've successfully scavenged some, since that means the battlefield will be a bit more empty when you try it again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T16:04:25-07:00","id":1333173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1333159#post1333159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, a straight Archery (or Thrown) roll is pretty weird. I think that might be the only thing in the system that calls for that? If not, it's certainly quite rare. Personally, I'd make that a [Wits + (Archery or Thrown)] roll, since otherwise a Solar archer would be getting less benefit out of their Excellency than a DB would, and a Lunar would technically not be able to use an Excellency <i>at all</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if you even CAN excellency it since it's such a special roll. I also assumed that the every 5 rounds thing applied to consecutive combats without being able to restock, but again I kind of wonder if there's even any point to it or if it's just RPG busywork at that point. You've got an over 95% chance to roll at least 1 success on 6 dice, and unless something insanely pressing is happening at the end of a battle you can always take an action to scavenge some arrows with an even greater chance of success.<br /> <br /> Maybe one in twenty fights last up to five rounds, and if only one in twenty of those there's a failed roll it probably isn't worth it for the 1 in 400 fights where it will actually matter. Even if it advances the difficulty by one step each time no fight ever lasts 10 rounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T16:16:43-07:00","id":1333175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1333173#post1333173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if you even CAN excellency it since it's such a special roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. I feel that if you're rolling an Ability, that means skill plays a role, and thus the Excellency should apply. And that makes sense in the context, which seems to be assuming that a skilled archer is taking more accurate shots and wasting fewer arrows. So a masterful archer should be able to use their inherent magic to do that, just better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also assumed that the every 5 rounds thing applied to consecutive combats without being able to restock, but again I kind of wonder if there's even any point to it or if it's just RPG busywork at that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see &quot;every 5 rounds total&quot; being reasonable, but on the other hand, I <i>really</i> don't want to track rounds from previous combats, just to tell the ranged combatant &quot;sorry, the last fight lasted three rounds, and now we're at two rounds in this fight, so you need to make an ammunition roll&quot;. <br /> <br /> I think the idea of ammunition is to <i>reduce</i> &quot;RPG busywork&quot;, since it's trying to do away with precise tracking of every arrow or knife you're carrying. But tracking based on every single round of every combat that passes defeats the purpose. That's why, the more I think about it, I prefer the idea of making an ammunition check at the start of the battle to determine how much you have handy, and letting that determine how long before you have to make another check in that fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T16:48:48-07:00","id":1333185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1333175#post1333175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the idea of ammunition is to <i>reduce</i> &quot;RPG busywork&quot;, since it's trying to do away with precise tracking of every arrow or knife you're carrying. But tracking based on every single round of every combat that passes defeats the purpose. That's why, the more I think about it, I prefer the idea of making an ammunition check at the start of the battle to determine how much you have handy, and letting that determine how long before you have to make another check in that fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, maybe. If you can scavenge for arrows at the end of any particular combat I don't know if that would ever really matter. Scavenging is a low difficulty roll that takes one action, if you've got 30 seconds after a fight you can do it 100% of the time, and then you're set for the next one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T20:32:58-07:00","id":1333215,"title":"","content":"Reminder that battle groups exist. Even with Exalted levels of overpenetration that should still be an ammo check at least every two or three rounds instead of five.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T16:15:34-07:00","id":1333445,"title":"","content":"What do you think of Lizard-Tyrant as familiars ?<br /> <br /> We had a good taste today of our Zenith unleashing the terrifying roar in a battle that was basically an unlimited range attack that target ennemies, can easily cause all ennemies to lose 10 initiative or so and a WP or just flee, and has apparently no reset condition so is free to reuse.<br /> <br /> This and all the others insane things lizard-tyrant can do. I know there are certainly &quot;stronger builds&quot; or whatever you want to name it but here it's more about losing the ability to have multiple options at your disposal as a ST because one character have a really polarising effect.<br /> <br /> So I'm asking the question because I'm rather happy for a Survival Zenith to do fun things with a Unicorn, a talking monkey or whatever cool thing you want to have, but lizard-tyrant are really strong. Would it seem fair to you that I don't accept Lizard-tyrant and the like (extremely strong giants dinosaurs basically) as familiars ? I'm not really having fun as a ST when one of my player has one, but I don't want to private them of a legitimate aspect of the game. What do you think ?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T18:13:38-07:00","id":1333463,"title":"","content":"Of course it's reasonable for you-as-ST to say you aren't comfortable with something at your table. <i>You're the ST</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T18:49:13-07:00","id":1333466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1333445#post1333445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think of Lizard-Tyrant as familiars ?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are definitely very, very powerful. Anything with Legendary Size is going to be, and tyrant lizards are pretty much the top end of those. <br /> <br /> You're certainly within your rights as an ST to disallow them if you're just not comfortable with it, though I'd definitely say the player was owed some kind of replacement creature, rather than just having it removed by fiat. However, before you do that, consider a couple of things. <br /> <br /> First, I'm not sure it's as powerful as you're making it out to be. Its Terrifying Dragon Roar ability, for example, counts as a decisive attack, resetting it to base initiative. That means that a) it's basically just used up all the initiative its attacks have gained on doing that rather than actually damaging anybody, and b) at base initiative, it's now more vulnerable to being crashed, or at least reduced to 1 initiative. Also, I would personally say that once you spend WP to resist the effect, you're immune for the rest of the scene. I think that's consistent with how other emotional influence effects are treated in the system.<br /> <br /> Second, remember that walking around with something like a tyrant lizard in tow should have <i>consequences</i>. Basically everybody who meets them has reasonable grounds for instantly developing an intimacy of fear, for example. And cities and other settlements will almost certainly automatically forbid it entry, and probably fight if the character presses the matter. While the PC will probably <i>win</i> those fights, it will still make doing business in any settled area much, much harder. When a tyrant lizard comes to town, everybody who can move out probably does so. And if the player chooses to leave their familiar out in the wilderness in order to avoid these kind of hassles, well, those are times when they won't have it available for a fight. And there are places that a tyrant lizard just <i>can't </i>go, no matter how much the player would like to have them handy. Try taking one into a cave where the human-scale characters have to crawl on hands and knees, for example. <br /> <br /> Basically, a tyrant lizard, as a familiar, exchanges raw potency in a fight for all the other things a familiar can be useful for - spying on people, appealing to people's love of pets, simply being around to help out in most circumstances, and so forth. And it's not unreasonable for enemies to take steps to deal with it either! I wouldn't recommend too much of &quot;while you're off shopping, your tyrant lizard was ambushed and badly injured&quot;, but if people know they're going to be fighting the PC, they can do things like prepare pit traps, set up huge piles of meat to lure it away, and so on, meaning the PC with the familiar will at least have to spend time commanding and controlling it, if not losing it for the fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T01:12:34-07:00","id":1333490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1333445#post1333445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think of Lizard-Tyrant as familiars ?<br /> <br /> I'm not really having fun as a ST when one of my player has one, but I don't want to private them of a legitimate aspect of the game. What do you think ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Exalted wield the powers of the greatest gods in Creation. In play-testing, a starting Dawn killed a Tyrant Lizard without taking a single level of damage. I would say it's perfectly reasonable to not roll the Tyrant Lizard into fights unless using Seasoned Beast-Rider\u2019s Approach. <br /> <br /> If your approach to STing is going to be to ban anything that's powerful then you are not going to have fun running Exalted.<br /> <br /> It is perfectly reasonable to disallow something that doesn't fit with the <i>tone</i> of the game. If you're running a game of politics and intrigue then a Tyrant Lizard is not appropriate.<br /> <br /> It's perfectly reasonable (and your job as ST) to show the concequences of actions. Tyrant Lizards need a warm environment. They need to <s>be fed</s> hunt. They're basically impossible to domesticate (marking the character as Anathema as surely as a giant golden sword). They're enormous -- they're not going to fit through city gates or into sailing ships or ancient tombs. The PCs are going to be easy to track. People are going to react with fear. Imagine trying to walk a pet tiger around your hometown, now multiply that by a thousand in a world where you are guilty until proven innocent.<br /> <br /> Terrifying Dragon Roar is a Latent ability that needs to be unlocked with XP (on top of a three-dot merit). It's resisted by Resolve. A Tyrant Lizard has a Base Initiative of 5 and a 10 dice Intimidation pool -- which is about 8 successes. A normal mortal solider (before Initimacies) has a Resolve of 2 and so is only losing 6i (which the Tyrant Lizard isn't gaining). An Elite Solider with an appropriate Initimacy loses 0i (zero, zilch, nadda, nil, nix, nought, nothing). Essence users with Resolve scores lower than 4 can always spend motes to make up the shortfall. Fearless adversaries also exist: Tiger Warriors, The Dead, Automatons.<br /> <br /> Lastly, whilst it's an Intimidation pool not a Threaten check, I personally would use the rules for retrying Threaten checks on p223. I also agree with Kelly that once WP is spent it should protect you from fleeing for the scene (and even if you don't play it that way, at the low end, Conscripts have 3WP which is giving you three turns of fighting).<br /> <br /> If you really want to ban it then talk to the player and refund the XP so they can buy something else. But Tyrant Lizards are far less powerful than Solar Charms: if you can't balance this you are going to struggle running this game.<br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1333445#post1333445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know there are certainly &quot;stronger builds&quot; or whatever you want to name it but here it's more about losing the ability to have multiple options at your disposal as a ST because one character have a really polarising effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm interested in exploring this thought further with you.<br /> <br /> What options do you feel like you're losing as ST?<br /> What can't you do?<br /> <br /> With my ST hat on, I see very little difference between attacking the PCs with a Wing of mortal infantry and having the Dawn Caste rout them in two turns or having the Zenith's Tyrant Lizard rout them in one. And if that extra turn is so important, then the NPCs spend the single point of Willpower it takes not to run away (or they're Elite Troops, or they've been blessed with fearlessness by a local god or what-have-you).<br /> <br /> (Remember you should be grouping characters &quot;who aren\u2019t especially noteworthy to the story as individuals&quot; into a single battlegroup as per p205. So if the Circle is attacked by six nameless thugs/wild wolves that should be one Size 1 battlegroup, not 6 individual NPCs. Also remember that Essence users have Charms to boost their Resolve or even become immune to fear.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-01-2019, 05:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T03:23:48-07:00","id":1333500,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your answers.<br /> <br /> I'll answer the mechanical answers first and then I'll try to discuss the thematics one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you really want to ban it then talk to the player and refund the XP so they can buy something else. But Tyrant Lizards are far less powerful than Solar Charms: if you can't balance this you are going to struggle running this game. </div> </div> </div>Don't worry I'm not crazy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm not going to remove anything from my players &quot;just because&quot; without any compensation. Usually when I have a problem with something in game, I ask stuff on forum and when I do a new campaign I change the things I had problems with, but in the meantime I let it continue to test it and see how it affects my game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First, I'm not sure it's as powerful as you're making it out to be. Its Terrifying Dragon Roar ability, for example, counts as a decisive attack, resetting it to base initiative. That means that a) it's basically just used up all the initiative its attacks have gained on doing that rather than actually damaging anybody, and b) at base initiative, it's now more vulnerable to being crashed, or at least reduced to 1 initiative. Also, I would personally say that once you spend WP to resist the effect, you're immune for the rest of the scene. I think that's consistent with how other emotional influence effects are treated in the system. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Terrifying Dragon Roar is a Latent ability that needs to be unlocked with XP (on top of a three-dot merit). It's resisted by Resolve. A Tyrant Lizard has a Base Initiative of 5 and a 10 dice Intimidation pool -- which is about 8 successes. A normal mortal solider (before Initimacies) has a Resolve of 2 and so is only losing 6i (which the Tyrant Lizard isn't gaining). An Elite Solider with an appropriate Initimacy loses 0i (zero, zilch, nadda, nil, nix, nought, nothing). Essence users with Resolve scores lower than 4 can always spend motes to make up the shortfall. Fearless adversaries also exist: Tiger Warriors, The Dead, Automatons. </div> </div> </div>I'd agree with you if, as I said, the Familiar wielder wasn't Solar. With Ambush Predator Style and Familiar-honing instructions, a Solar can easily make his familiar roll anything above 17 initiative (on average), for 2 Charms and 1 full Excellency. He's probably one of the first creature to act. Yesterday our game was a huge battle with war stratagems and the like. Against the Solars and their allies was something around 4 battle groups of 100+ ennemies and 4-5 powerful lieutenants. They didn't roll higher initiative (which is normal, even if they were optimized), so the lizard acted first. He rolls 27 dices for Terrifying roar (he can actually do more, but for the sake of the demonstration I'm keeping all baseline stats), which turns into 14 successes. For lieutenants, everyone of them that do not have excellency on Integrity basically loses 10 initiative, the others lose more or less 5. Initiative crash ensues for everyone that is basically not a celestial, and even them are put in a difficult situation. This attack target every enemy, on miles so reasonably all around the battlefield. I don't even know how to handle battle groups in this case, I guess this should be a rout check ? Because this is clearly not meant to function like a regular intimidation attempt so there are no clear answers on how to handle it.<br /> <br /> I didn't even try to optimise the roll of the lizard tyrant, the solar could for example give him mutations, grant him a Familiar honing instructions, or train him and that would easily bring him 10 more successes on the intimidation roll (thus 10 initiative less on everyone involved). So yeah I guess there are certainly optimized characters who might do crazy things, but this is hardly optimized : it's 4 Charms and 3 points of merit. If anything, any normal Martial Arts build cost more investment (but at this point the Solar usually invest more than just 4 Charms on his familiar, so we can discuss subtilities. Still it's not that huge of a cost).<br /> <br /> Anyway, at this point, almost every enemy anywhere on the battlefield lost a ton of initiative on the first round, when they are not immediately crashed, thus granting the Lizard initiative to avoid being put into crash, and he has 15 Soak anyway so he's not so easy to crash. Needless to say, when everyone is crashed the opposition they can make suddenly become less interesting.<br /> <br /> So now, what are the options ?<br /> <br /> a) Make more thing immune to fear, or prevent him from being here at all. Ok but this is not really fun, we all know the story of the Wizard in D&amp;D that optimized to throw fireballs and the ST decided to give fire immunity on every ennemies they encounter. There are situations that are appropriate, but usually it's boring.<br /> <br /> b) Try to ambush or assassinate the Lizard-tyran or the Solar. I can see 1 scenario like that, maybe 2, but any more would become boring and a proof of bad faith. It will obviously fail, but may weaken the Lizard-tyrant. Can be considered.<br /> <br /> c) Antoganize the Lizard-Tyrant so the player has consequences to deal with. Yeah this could be done from time to time, but when the player makes the Lizard tyrant intelligent with sorcery, is a Champion of his people (because he's a Solar who tamed a titanic beast), and the game happens somewhere else that around the Treshold where everyone is not necessarily a nazis against anathemas, this quickly become irrelevant.<br /> <br /> d) Make his Limit Break break things. Yeah I like this one.<br /> <br /> I feel the options are extremely polarizing : It's shut down the lizard or nothing, basically.<br /> <br /> Now onto less mechanical questions :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What options do you feel like you're losing as ST?<br /> What can't you do? </div> </div> </div>I feel like the problem is twofold (I'm not sure this is proper English so correct my use of this one if you may) :<br /> - The encounter becomes boring because when ennemies do not have initiative they usually lose a lot of options that are fun<br /> - The encounter becomes boring because the players know they don't risk much given the circumstances.<br /> <br /> I'm not like &quot;Oh my gawd this Lizard-tyrant is ruining my games this is a catastrophe&quot;. But I'm disappointed because I have had many awesome fights playing Exalted and the Lizard-tyrant used this way basically made them way less exciting if I don't resort to shenanigans to shut him down, and I'm wondering if I did something wrong or if I should get rid of this particular aspect of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T04:55:06-07:00","id":1333509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1333500#post1333500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't worry I'm not crazy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm not going to remove anything from my players &quot;just because&quot; without any compensation. Usually when I have a problem with something in game, I ask stuff on forum and when I do a new campaign I change the things I had problems with, but in the meantime I let it continue to test it and see how it affects my game.<br /> <br /> I'd agree with you if, as I said, the Familiar wielder wasn't Solar. With Ambush Predator Style and Familiar-honing instructions, a Solar can easily make his familiar roll anything above 17 initiative (on average), for 2 Charms and 1 full Excellency.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the small matter of this being the Solar's Supernal: literally the thing they're supposed to be the best in Creation at?<br /> <br /> Otherwise at Essence 1 you can't buy these Charms and at Essence 2 Familiar Honing Instruction is a Simple Charm. <br /> <br /> You're also looking at 17m (4m to order into battle, 13m to roll a full join battle to get to your 17i).<br /> <br /> Terrifying Apparition of Glory is only three Charms into Presence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He's probably one of the first creature to act. </div> </div> </div>Yeah five dots in Wits and 5 dots in your Join Battle Ability and a full Excellency will generally do that. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yesterday our game was a huge battle with war stratagems and the like. Against the Solars and their allies was something around 4 battle groups of 100+ ennemies </div> </div> </div>Sounds like it should have been one Size 5 battlegroup. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and 4-5 powerful lieutenants. They didn't roll higher initiative (which is normal, even if they were optimized), so the lizard acted first. He rolls 27 dices for Terrifying roar (he can actually do more, but for the sake of the demonstration I'm keeping all baseline stats), which turns into 14 successes. For lieutenants, everyone of them that do not have excellency on Integrity basically loses 10 initiative, the others lose more or less 5. </div> </div> </div>Who are these lieutenants who don't have an Integrity Excellency or a relevant Intimacy? <br /> <br /> 4 Resolve, Defining Intimacy boosts that to 8, Excellency to 10. Shikari Join Battle on ~7i so we're not really looking at any Crashes here (unless you push the combo to 27m by Full Excellency-ing Familiar Honing Instruction).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Initiative crash ensues for everyone that is basically not a celestial, </div> </div> </div>Well your Size 5 Battlegroup should probably take (14 success - 2 Resolve - 5 Size) 7 Magnitude damage which isn't even enough to force a Rout check. Terrestrials really should have a good reason (read Defining Intimacy) to be risking their lives, and even without an Integrity Excellency should still be sitting on 1i.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and even them are put in a difficult situation. This attack target every enemy, on miles so reasonably all around the battlefield. I don't even know how to handle battle groups in this case, I guess this should be a rout check ? Because this is clearly not meant to function like a regular intimidation attempt so there are no clear answers on how to handle it.<br /> <br /> I didn't even try to optimise the roll of the lizard tyrant, the solar could for example give him mutations, grant him a Familiar honing instructions, or train him and that would easily bring him 10 more successes on the intimidation roll (thus 10 initiative less on everyone involved). So yeah I guess there are certainly optimized characters who might do crazy things, but this is hardly optimized : it's 4 Charms and 3 points of merit. If anything, any normal Martial Arts build cost more investment (but at this point the Solar usually invest more than just 4 Charms on his familiar, so we can discuss subtilities. Still it's not that huge of a cost). </div> </div> </div>Harmonious Presence Meditation<br /> Majestic Radiant Presence <br /> Terrifying Apparition of Glory<br /> <br /> This is exactly the power level of 4 Charms and a Merit.<br /> <br /> Heck <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1293704#post1293704\">Lunars have a nasty combo for the same sort of mote cost</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway, at this point, almost every enemy anywhere on the battlefield lost a ton of initiative on the first round, when they are not immediately crashed, thus granting the Lizard initiative to avoid being put into crash, </div> </div> </div>Which is why you group trivial threats into as few battlegroups as possible (as per the rules on p205).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and he has 15 Soak anyway so he's not so easy to crash. Needless to say, when everyone is crashed the opposition they can make suddenly become less interesting. </div> </div> </div>How so? What Charms are we talking here? If I hit you for 10i then you lose 10i and I gain 10i whether I'm Crashed or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So now, what are the options ?<br /> <br /> a) Make more thing immune to fear, or prevent him from being here at all. Ok but this is not really fun, we all know the story of the Wizard in D&amp;D that optimized to throw fireballs and the ST decided to give fire immunity on every ennemies they encounter. There are situations that are appropriate, but usually it's boring.<br /> <br /> b) Try to ambush or assassinate the Lizard-tyran or the Solar. I can see 1 scenario like that, maybe 2, but any more would become boring and a proof of bad faith. It will obviously fail, but may weaken the Lizard-tyrant. Can be considered.<br /> <br /> c) Antoganize the Lizard-Tyrant so the player has consequences to deal with. Yeah this could be done from time to time, but when the player makes the Lizard tyrant intelligent with sorcery, is a Champion of his people (because he's a Solar who tamed a titanic beast), and the game happens somewhere else that around the Treshold where everyone is not necessarily a nazis against anathemas, this quickly become irrelevant.<br /> <br /> d) Make his Limit Break break things. Yeah I like this one.<br /> <br /> I feel the options are extremely polarizing : It's shut down the lizard or nothing, basically. </div> </div> </div>Are the PCs supposed to win the fight or not?<br /> How much faster does the Tyrant Lizard Crashing everyone on Turn 1 make the fight?<br /> <br /> If the big fight is over in five rounds instead of seven then I don't see the problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now onto less mechanical questions :<br /> <br /> I feel like the problem is twofold (I'm not sure this is proper English so correct my use of this one if you may) :<br /> - The encounter becomes boring because when ennemies do not have initiative they usually lose a lot of options that are fun<br /> - The encounter becomes boring because the players know they don't risk much given the circumstances.<br /> <br /> I'm not like &quot;Oh my gawd this Lizard-tyrant is ruining my games this is a catastrophe&quot;. But I'm disappointed because I have had many awesome fights playing Exalted and the Lizard-tyrant used this way basically made them way less exciting if I don't resort to shenanigans to shut him down, and I'm wondering if I did something wrong or if I should get rid of this particular aspect of the game. </div> </div> </div>Being Crashed isn't an end state. It cuts you out of charms that cost i and Perilous charms, locks you out of Decisives and shuts down Hardness. It doesn't stop you throwing a Full Excellency Withering attack to get out of Crash. Combat is a seesaw not a slide.<br /> <br /> This is what Solar Exalted do. They smash armies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-01-2019, 08:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T06:06:13-07:00","id":1333514,"title":"","content":"I don't really wish to start a quote war with you because I feel like we don't play the same way. I will look a little bit harsh in my answers, but it is to accentuate the fact we have different analysis of the game rather than &quot;you are wrong I am right&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the small matter of this being the Solar's Supernal: literally the thing they're supposed to be the best in Creation at?<br /> <br /> Otherwise at Essence 1 you can't buy these Charms and at Essence 2 Familiar Honing Instruction is a Simple Charm.<br /> <br /> You're also looking at 17m (4m to order into battle, 13m to roll a full join battle to get to your 17i).<br /> <br /> Terrifying Apparition of Glory is only three Charms into Presence. </div> </div> </div>Not every supernal causes me the same problem.<br /> <br /> 17m is nothing compared to the benefits of what I described, and in range with what any Celestial a bit oritented toward combat will do.<br /> <br /> I don't even begin to fathom how you can compare Terrifying Apparition of Flory with Terrifying Roar. TAfG is 5 initiative to resist, TR is 5 initiative in suboptimal circumstance. TAfG has rules that do not work in anyway the same manner than the houserule you propose below.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah five dots in Wits and 5 dots in your Join Battle Ability and a full Excellency will generally do that. </div> </div> </div>I don't know I have 5 Perception and 5 Awareness and Awakening Eye, and my average initiative is 14-15, which is less. Can you teach me how to roll better or should I just break the laws of probabilities ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sounds like it should have been one Size 5 battlegroup. </div> </div> </div>On this one I really don't know. In context one lieutenant was trying to breach the right side of our fortifications with some forces while the other was trying to embush us passing from the left side (range between the right side and the left side is extreme), plus another one was fighting in the middle of our camp with their troops because they used them as bait. I don't feel like this should be represented as 1 battle group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Who are these lieutenants who don't have an Integrity Excellency or a relevant Intimacy?<br /> <br /> 4 Resolve, Defining Intimacy boosts that to 8, Excellency to 10. Shikari Join Battle on ~7i so we're not really looking at any Crashes here (unless you push the combo to 27m by Full Excellency-ing Familiar Honing Instruction). </div> </div> </div>Yeah why on earth does every NPC is not a litteral exact clone of his neighbor with maximum stats on every attribute and ability ? Crashes come fast with any stunt or mutations or anything that comes at a rather low price.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well your Size 5 Battlegroup should probably take (14 success - 2 Resolve - 5 Size) 7 Magnitude damage which isn't even enough to force a Rout check. Terrestrials really should have a good reason (read Defining Intimacy) to be risking their lives, and even without an Integrity Excellency should still be sitting on 1i. </div> </div> </div>I guess why not it could be a not terrible houserule to handle the fear effects on Battle groups.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Harmonious Presence Meditation<br /> Majestic Radiant Presence<br /> Terrifying Apparition of Glory<br /> <br /> This is exactly the power level of 4 Charms and a Merit. </div> </div> </div>As I said already I can't even fathom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is why you group trivial threats into as few battlegroups as possible as per the rules on p205). </div> </div> </div>Talked about this already. Every lieutenants had good stats and were at least as powerful as a Dragon Blooded, and the player had a bit more stats than the baseline described in my example so he rolled more successes. Or should I just forever consider the Creation is composed of 700 Celestials and everything else are Battle Groups ? Doesn't seem fun to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How so? What Charms are we talking here? If I hit you for 10i then you lose 10i and I gain 10i whether I'm Crashed or not. </div> </div> </div>Like, the basic mechanic of the game is you need initiative to deal damage, and lots of special attacks cost initiative. I guess at this point though it is just a matter of random &quot;This attack cost initiative, this one doesn't&quot;, so I could just ignore it when it bothers me. Also, when your ennemy has lots of Soak, it's harder to recover from crash, because well, he has Soak.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are the PCs supposed to win the fight or not?<br /> How much faster does the Tyrant Lizard Crashing everyone on Turn 1 make the fight?<br /> <br /> If the big fight is over in five rounds instead of seven then I don't see the problem. </div> </div> </div>That's kind of the only point where I agree with you : Reducing the duration of fight with no tension is useful. However, behold my other strategy around this one : I just make players do a skill check and they win it. Even faster. When I want a fight with a bit more tension however, this is a hassle to me hence my questions on the forum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Being Crashed isn't an end state. It cuts you out of charms that cost i and Perilous charms, locks you out of Decisives and shuts down Hardness. It doesn't stop you throwing a Full Excellency Withering attack to get out of Crash. Combat is a seesaw not a slide. </div> </div> </div>I kinda answered this already. No initiative essentially means less tension for the player, so starting every ennemy with 5-10 less initiative bothers me.<br /> <br /> Again I think we shouldn't really argue over this. The fact is the experience I described happened in the game and what could have been a tense fight was not, which bothers me because I know for a fact if the player had a fucking cool Unicorn everyone would have also done awesome stuff with much more tension, but it was not the case. I'm not making up things to complain on the forum, I've got 3 years of experience STing Exalted 3e, I don't just throw 5 thugs at my players and wonder &quot;why the hell does this not work ?&quot;, and I was trying to figure out if someone else had encountered the same issue or if I could safely remove this aspect of the game.<br /> <br /> Thanks for your answers and time, I hope I didn't appear too assertive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T06:23:17-07:00","id":1333520,"title":"","content":"I feel you Chausse, we have a friendly agreement at my table that nobody takes tyrant lizards as familiars. For a Survival Supernal Zenith it\u2019s so much more insane, boosting the rolls with solar excellencies and then things like Deadly Predator Method...it becomes too much for us. Solar Exalted are supposed to be stupid powerful but that doesn\u2019t mean it\u2019s impossible to be so strong that it\u2019s broken. The solar survival tree is meant to be badass enough that you can take a dog or a falcon and turn it into a combatant that can clash with fairie lords, those same charms applied to a tyrant lizard pushes it too far, at least as long as our table is concerned.<br /> <br /> Edit: one thing you could try, maybe, is doing bigger days with more intense scenes, particularly action and combat. If your players start to suspect that there might be 3 big fights in the span of an in game hour they might become hesitant to spend all those motes and willpower on every one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 09-01-2019, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T06:43:12-07:00","id":1333521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1333520#post1333520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel you Chausse, we have a friendly agreement at my table that nobody takes tyrant lizards as familiars. For a Survival Supernal Zenith it\u2019s so much more insane, boosting the rolls with solar excellencies and then things like Deadly Predator Method...it becomes too much for us. Solar Exalted are supposed to be stupid powerful but that doesn\u2019t mean it\u2019s impossible to be so strong that it\u2019s broken. The solar survival tree is meant to be badass enough that you can take a dog or a falcon and turn it into a combatant that can clash with fairie lords, those same charms applied to a tyrant lizard pushes it too far, at least as long as our table is concerned.<br /> <br /> Edit: one thing you could try, maybe, is doing bigger days with more intense scenes, particularly action and combat. If your players start to suspect that there might be 3 big fights in the span of an in game hour they might become hesitant to spend all those motes and willpower on every one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it could be a solution but I believe it applies at large for Exalted : Throw more challenges to exhaust characters <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> This campaign is stopping though since I'm changing town, but I really wish to learn lessons from this campaign for the next one I wish to do on a city-boat roaming the Dreaming Sea.<br /> <br /> I really feel like the Survival Supernal is supposed to have this very thematic of beast, sometimes a bit exotic, that do cool stuff when infused by the power granted by the bond with their masters. But for what I have experienced with different players, Survival is rather used as a fuel for Willpower for their sorcerous masters, not for personal RP about 2 beings sharing something that make the sum greater than its parts.<br /> <br /> I don't blame players though, I believe playing a usually mute NPC who is supposed to be rather bestial consistently to make the relation feel real is hard. Also, when you see that for 1 more dot of merit, you can multiply your power exponentially ... I guess this metagame choice is a sort of metaphor for Solar themselves : You can be stronger at the expanse of the fun of everyone else <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T07:20:41-07:00","id":1333527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1333521#post1333521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess it could be a solution but I believe it applies at large for Exalted : Throw more challenges to exhaust characters <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> This campaign is stopping though since I'm changing town, but I really wish to learn lessons from this campaign for the next one I wish to do on a city-boat roaming the Dreaming Sea.<br /> <br /> I really feel like the Survival Supernal is supposed to have this very thematic of beast, sometimes a bit exotic, that do cool stuff when infused by the power granted by the bond with their masters. But for what I have experienced with different players, Survival is rather used as a fuel for Willpower for their sorcerous masters, not for personal RP about 2 beings sharing something that make the sum greater than its parts.<br /> <br /> I don't blame players though, I believe playing a usually mute NPC who is supposed to be rather bestial consistently to make the relation feel real is hard. Also, when you see that for 1 more dot of merit, you can multiply your power exponentially ... I guess this metagame choice is a sort of metaphor for Solar themselves : You can be stronger at the expanse of the fun of everyone else <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely don\u2019t blame the players, but it is a hard choice for an ST. It takes a ton of wind out of the combat when at the top of round one every enemy on the field gets crashed and the T-Rex resets to like 20 initiative due to the stacking initiative breaks. T-lizards are particularly bad for that though. I don\u2019t know if there\u2019s any fix for it, as an ST it feels bad to have everyone react with fear and hostility all the time, or to have enemies specifically track down and target the lizard. Your player didn\u2019t take the familiar merit to make an enemy of the whole world, not to mention you\u2019re probably going to have way more instances where people want to bend over backwards not to offend the dude with the dragon in town. If anything I imagine most transactions would be wildly easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T07:26:08-07:00","id":1333529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1333527#post1333527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Your player didn\u2019t take the familiar merit to make an enemy of the whole world, not to mention you\u2019re probably going to have way more instances where people want to bend over backwards not to offend the dude with the dragon in town. If anything I imagine most transactions would be wildly easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially when he has appearance 7 and wants to be considered the most awesome dude in all Creation !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T09:37:55-07:00","id":1333539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1333514#post1333514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really wish to start a quote war with you because I feel like we don't play the same way. I will look a little bit harsh in my answers, but it is to accentuate the fact we have different analysis of the game rather than &quot;you are wrong I am right&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's cool. Sorry if I'm coming across as harsh -- it's not intended.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't even begin to fathom how you can compare Terrifying Apparition of Flory with Terrifying Roar. TAfG is 5 initiative to resist, TR is 5 initiative in suboptimal circumstance. TAfG has rules that do not work in anyway the same manner than the houserule you propose below. </div> </div> </div>14 successes against Resolve 4 (plus intimacy plus Excellency) is 4i then resetting to Base. Base+10 is 0i.<br /> <br /> 5i &gt; 4i<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know I have 5 Perception and 5 Awareness and Awakening Eye, and my average initiative is 14-15, which is less. Can you teach me how to roll better or should I just break the laws of probabilities ? </div> </div> </div>The point is that a PC character with a cap-breaker and max initative will go before unoptimized stock NPCs.<br /> <br /> Your complaint that the person who has optimized initative is going before characters who haven't optmized initative is what I was referring to. But yes, cap breakers are powerful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On this one I really don't know. In context </div> </div> </div>That's a hard one. It really is. I'd still model it as one battlegroup. Cut back on rolling. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah why on earth does every NPC is not a litteral exact clone of his neighbor with maximum stats on every attribute and ability ? Crashes come fast with any stunt or mutations or anything that comes at a rather low price. </div> </div> </div>If you're making the NPCs from scratch, make them appropriate for the scenario.<br /> <br /> If you're using the stats from the book... those are the stats I'm quoting. Resolve 4. (Not the max of 6, but 4.)<br /> <br /> It's not egregious that a professional soldier have an Integrity Excellency. I'm not saying E5 Solar Charms -- I'm saying the basic Excellency the NPCs in the book already have. You need a Defining Intimacy to risk your life, I don't see why a significant NPC opposing a Solar Circle wouldn't have such an Initimacy. They don't need to be exact clones: the Intimacies can all be different, they just have to be applicable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I guess why not it could be a not terrible houserule to handle the fear effects on Battle groups. </div> </div> </div>Battlegroups have static Initative, they don't gain or lose it.<br /> <br /> You could push them into negative Initative instead but that doesn't actually do anything so I'd treat it as a Withering attack that causes some troops to break and run (or otherwise become ineffectual from fear). Otherwise it's just spending 1WP and no further effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Talked about this already. Every lieutenants had good stats and were at least as powerful as a Dragon Blooded, and the player had a bit more stats than the baseline described in my example so he rolled more successes. Or should I just forever consider the Creation is composed of 700 Celestials and everything else are Battle Groups ? Doesn't seem fun to me. </div> </div> </div>With greatest respect, you're describing a scenario where the PCs breezed over their opposition without pause and complaining here about how insignificant your NPCs were and how this awarded multiple Crash bonuses to the PCs.<br /> <br /> If they're supposed to be insignificant, my advice is make them a battlegroup.<br /> <br /> If they're not supposed to be trivial, consider giving them better stats. *shrug*<br /> <br /> Your PCs aren't going to get weaker as the game progresses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like, the basic mechanic of the game is you need initiative to deal damage, and lots of special attacks cost initiative. I guess at this point though it is just a matter of random &quot;This attack cost initiative, this one doesn't&quot;, so I could just ignore it when it bothers me. Also, when your ennemy has lots of Soak, it's harder to recover from crash, because well, he has Soak. </div> </div> </div>Sorry, so in this scenario there was only a Soak 15 Tyrant Lizard and no-one else to get Initative from?<br /> <br /> You can still gain Initative when Crashed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's kind of the only point where I agree with you : Reducing the duration of fight with no tension is useful. However, behold my other strategy around this one : I just make players do a skill check and they win it. Even faster. When I want a fight with a bit more tension however, this is a hassle to me hence my questions on the forum. </div> </div> </div>I think we're at cross purposes here.<br /> <br /> Is this was a fight the PCs were supposed to lose? You could have made it harder.<br /> If the PCs were supposed to win... hurrah!<br /> <br /> If the PCs were supposed to win after a drawn out fight with lots of tension, you could have very easily given the enemy Charms protecting them from fear. As you said, this was long, drawn out, strategic warfare. You could put your own Tyrant Lizard on the field. You could have had reinforcements suddenly appear. A god of murder show up. You could have one of the powerful, competent Lieutenants shut down the Tyrant Lizard with a gambit.<br /> <br /> Or played it straight. A Crashed enemy can still make Withering attacks. If these opponents can't get Initative back because of the PCs high soak, then all you've done is made the fight quicker. If these people were a threat at 10i before they got Crashed then they should still be a threat at 0i. If at 10i they had no way of getting over the PCs soak, then it makes no difference if the Tyrant Lizard AOEs or a Unicorn launches Decisive attacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I kinda answered this already. No initiative essentially means less tension for the player, so starting every ennemy with 5-10 less initiative bothers me. </div> </div> </div>Why?<br /> <br /> A battlegroup with 50i fights exactly the same as a battlegroup with -50i.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again I think we shouldn't really argue over this. The fact is the experience I described happened in the game and what could have been a tense fight was not, which bothers me because I know for a fact if the player had a fucking cool Unicorn everyone would have also done awesome stuff with much more tension, but it was not the case. I'm not making up things to complain on the forum, I've got 3 years of experience STing Exalted 3e, I don't just throw 5 thugs at my players and wonder &quot;why the hell does this not work ?&quot;, and I was trying to figure out if someone else had encountered the same issue or if I could safely remove this aspect of the game.<br /> <br /> Thanks for your answers and time, I hope I didn't appear too assertive. </div> </div> </div>Exalted have powerful abilities. You can remove these abilities from the game if you can't manage them. A reasonable player will work with you, they'll take the Unicorn and nothing will break.<br /> <br /> This time.<br /> <br /> But if you shut players down every time a character gets to do what Exalted are supposed to be able to do, then <i>everything</i> breaks.<br /> <br /> Be sure that you can't work around this problem, or I guarentee you'll be back here in a month when one of your players comes up with another powerful combo. Because this strategy is already pretty suboptimal -- as you said &quot;there are certainly &quot;stronger builds&quot;&quot;.<br /> <br /> I don't mean to be abrasive about this. It's your game. I don't mean any offence. I'm not planning on arguing with you -- I've said what I have to say, I'm not going to say anything else.<br /> <br /> You wanted to know if the game will break? It won't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-01-2019, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T10:15:20-07:00","id":1333546,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your honest answer. I don't believe we leverage the system the same way, so discussing mechanics doesn't seem useful.<br /> <br /> I'd like to keep discussing one particular thing which seems to be a point of non-agreement between us though, that is :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With greatest respect, you're describing a scenario where the PCs breezed over their opposition without pause and complaining here about how insignificant your NPCs were and how this awarded multiple Crash bonuses to the PCs.<br /> <br /> If they're supposed to be insignificant, my advice is make them a battlegroup.<br /> <br /> If they're not supposed to be trivial, consider giving them better stats. *shrug* </div> </div> </div>Reading the forum and the book, there was this common theme emerging that is &quot;Everyone can be a hero&quot; (I feel like quoting My Hero Academia but whatever). Problem is, when I read you, it looks more like &quot;If you don't have Integrity 4 with excellency, and are not able to easily pass up the minimum soak 15 of the Tyrant lizard (he actually had 24 with mutations but whatever) you're an insignificant character&quot;, which seems kind of dull to me.<br /> <br /> Strong god-blooded, strange creatures made up from sorcery, giant beasts created by Lunar Elders, there are various things that I wish to be able to explore without giving them 4 in all stats, immunity against fear, flight and a base damage of 30 damage so &quot;it might feel threatening to players in combat&quot;.<br /> <br /> What do you think about it ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T10:52:33-07:00","id":1333554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1333546#post1333546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for your honest answer. I don't believe we leverage the system the same way, so discussing mechanics doesn't seem useful.<br /> <br /> I'd like to keep discussing one particular thing which seems to be a point of non-agreement between us though, that is :<br /> <br /> Reading the forum and the book, there was this common theme emerging that is &quot;Everyone can be a hero&quot; (I feel like quoting My Hero Academia but whatever). Problem is, when I read you, it looks more like &quot;If you don't have Integrity 4 with excellency, and are not able to easily pass up the minimum soak 15 of the Tyrant lizard (he actually had 24 with mutations but whatever) you're an insignificant character&quot;, which seems kind of dull to me.<br /> <br /> Strong god-blooded, strange creatures made up from sorcery, giant beasts created by Lunar Elders, there are various things that I wish to be able to explore without giving them 4 in all stats, immunity against fear, flight and a base damage of 30 damage so &quot;it might feel threatening to players in combat&quot;.<br /> <br /> What do you think about it ?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Bride of Ahlat is NEVER going to be able to beat Ahlat in a fight.<br /> <br /> If your players are building characters that can take down Ahlat, then a Bride is not going to challenge them.<br /> <br /> And that's ok.<br /> <br /> That's what the characters want to be good at, so let them be good at it.<br /> <br /> Not all characters will want to be so good at combat that they can take down Ahlat. Not all characters will want a pet Tyrant Lizard.<br /> <br /> A Solar with a mortal chopping sword, dex 3, melee 2 and an Excellency WILL be challenged in combat by god-blooded, strange creatures made up from sorcery, giant beasts created by Lunar Elders, and various things. A Solar with 5 Attribute + 5 Ability + 3 dot Merit + multiple charms + XP enhancing their Merit is absolutely the top of their class, best in Creation, ultimate ass-kicker. I'm not suggesting you challenge these characters with 5+5+3 matching Solariods, but if you're throwing in opposition with less than 4 in the relevant stat without so much as an Excellency... how do you think that's going to end?<br /> <br /> Your snakeman merchant can still be a dramatic character who challenges the PCs. But if the PCs are <i>optimised for combat</i> then the snakeman won't be able to challenge them <i>in combat</i>.<br /> <br /> Your PC with the pet T-rex that they've meticulously trained to take down armies can still be challenged. But suboptimal troops have got to play it smarter than running directly into the T-rex's mouth covered in BBQ sauce.<br /> <br /> Being able to rout an army doesn't solve a snakeman's riddle. It doesn't help you win the love of a behemoth. It doesn't help you clear god-blooded rats from a sewer.<br /> <br /> It does let a character be good at the thing she's invested a lot of resources in.<br /> <br /> If the troops can't hurt a Tyrant Lizard with 24 soak at 0i, they don't magically be able to hurt it at 10i. Hurt a softer target to build i. Or better yet, don't start a fight you can't win -- use your army to take a hostage or something.<br /> <br /> There's also something to be said for expectations. If you're throwing armies at your PCs they'll build characters that can fight armies. If you only give them easy threats they won't overinvest. But this is a session zero conversation.<br /> <br /> If I turn up with a character built to fight armies, I don't think it's unreasonable that I should be able to defeat armies. If you want to challenge my army killer, you need to provide a suitably tough opposition.<br /> <br /> I'm not suggesting (5+5+1) Resolve 6, 30 damage super-optimised opposition. I'm suggesting 4s and an Excellency: the level p496 suggests for &quot;seasoned fighters, or an Exalt who can carry himself well in battle&quot;. I'm suggesting Gambits, Disease, Poison, Stratagems, tactics, custom Charms, blessings from gods: you don't need 30 damage to challenge the 24 soak Tyrant Lizard if you can incapacitate it in a clever way (lure it away, trap it in a pit, paralyze its throat muscles, fight in tunnels, get a blessing from a god, use a Charm that creates Decisives, use Siege Weapons -- fight intelligently).<br /> <br /> If a PC wants to be good at something, I let them be good at it. What are your thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-01-2019, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-03T12:45:58-07:00","id":1333873,"title":"","content":"Sorry I'm finally answering this even if a little late.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a PC wants to be good at something, I let them be good at it. What are your thoughts? </div> </div> </div>So after a little time to think I realised that for me there was some essentials questions I had to address :<br /> <br /> 1) Am I fine with overspecialised character ?<br /> <br /> 2) What actually bothered me with the lyzard-tyrant ?<br /> <br /> And I found the core aspect of the answer in both is : Fun and game design.<br /> <br /> For 1, I usually hate overspecialised character. To me they are usually a result of the metagame rather than a relatable creature living in the game (ie, the player wants to do a particular shenanigan so he constraints the character to have the requirements for the shenanigan, usually by ignoring other aspects of the character so he has enough points of whatever the system use). It's not the case for everyone but still happens most of the time. But whatever.<br /> <br /> The encounter was kinda boring afterwards because we felt like not much could happen to us, because they had no initiative, but were not dead nonetheless. The thing is, I'm actually quite ok now with Dawn one-shotting things on the first round. It's part of the game, I have some ideas on how to change it if for future campaigns I want to try a different aspect of the game, but mainly it's fine. The thing is at least when the Dawn kills stuff, it forwards the story. What I like about initiative is that it overall moves the game forward. Here everyone just lost initiative, and the only thing it managed to do is kinda make everything slow and tensionless. With the initiative crash he did, the lizard tyrant got back to the initiative he had so nothing changed on him, we had no idea on how to rule beastmen trained by a Lunar plotting for revegenge since millenia in the nearby Shadowlands so the battlegroup stayed because it made no sense either to say they fled since there is no rule explicitly about Battle Groups in this power, and thus the only thing that changed was the Lieutenant lost tons of initiative and it felt really bland.<br /> <br /> Of course there exists the question of &quot;could I ST this thing better so it doesn't happen ?&quot; and the answer is most likely yes, but I could also say &quot;Well from the beginning there was not exceptionnal storytelling with this Lizard-tyrant and the specific mechanics of the lizard-tyrant always made things complicated to balance for interesting encounters so maybe it could be time to ask if I can get rid of it for my next campaigns&quot;.<br /> <br /> So yeah I'm sorry I guess I kinda looked like I was whining (because I was) on my post, but I was looking for people to discuss the matter and help me make up my mind about this stuff, and overall the variety of answers I got here helped me to decide what I want to do as well as to pinpoint where may have been my fault as a ST.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T11:53:04-07:00","id":1333999,"title":"","content":"What breaks if my solar players are allowed to home brew mastery effects (Okayed by the ST of course) if the M.A charm itself doesn't have one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14713-chronos12","name":"Chronos12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14713_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T12:53:24-07:00","id":1334006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chronos12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1333999#post1333999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if my solar players are allowed to home brew mastery effects (Okayed by the ST of course) if the M.A charm itself doesn't have one?</div> </div> </div> </div>If your players either stick to a single MA on their characters or they use MAs which aren't compatible with each other then there isn't much to worry about.<br /> <br /> The problem with tinkering with Martial Arts Charms is that they have to be balanced against every single Martial Arts they are compatible with to be sure you're not creating a broken combination, which tends to be a headache.<br /> <br /> A way to stay 100% safe would be to say that those custom-made Masteries do not activate when the Charm is used in combination with other Martial Arts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 09-04-2019, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T12:59:08-07:00","id":1334008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chronos12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1333999#post1333999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if my solar players are allowed to home brew mastery effects (Okayed by the ST of course) if the M.A charm itself doesn't have one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Martial Arts becomes more powerful.<br /> <br /> On its own, probably fine. But you're going to have to pay close attention to how different Charms interact with each other: an effect which is balanced on its own might tip a different, delicately balanced Charm over the edge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T13:01:26-07:00","id":1334009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chronos12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1333999#post1333999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if my solar players are allowed to home brew mastery effects (Okayed by the ST of course) if the M.A charm itself doesn't have one?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Without knowing the exact effects being proposed, it's hard to say specifically if anything breaks. Since you're talking about &quot;with ST approval&quot;, my advice will thus center around what the ST should be looking for.<br /> <br /> First, I'd be cautious about allowing <i>every</i> charm in a martial art to have Mastery effects. The charms in an MA are designed holistically, around the idea that they all work together in a certain way. Adding extra powers, particularly to every single charm, may make them overpowered. Be careful that the Mastery-level MA charms aren't overall more powerful than the &quot;native&quot; Solar charmset. The route to being an amazing sword fighter shouldn't always be through Steel Devil Style, just plain Solar Melee has to remain competitive.<br /> <br /> Second, even assuming that adding Mastery effects to an MA's charms doesn't break things game-balance-wise, you also need to be cautious about how adding Mastery effects changes the style's <i>feel</i>. The placement of Mastery effects in the charm progression can affect how the experience of learning and using the style comes off. If a style is supposed to be an easy route to fast power, for instance, it will have more Mastery and fewer Terrestrial keywords early in the tree, for example, while one that's supposed to be a slow journey towards being a master will put them further back. Also, styles like the Five Immaculate Dragon Styles deliberately have <i>no</i> Mastery keywords, because they were designed, in-setting, to be harmonious with Dragon-Blooded Essence, something the DBs could unlock the potential of just as well as a Solar. Adding Mastery powers to them would break that feeling.<br /> <br /> Third, I'd consider whether these new Mastery effects are something that, in setting, have always existed as part of the martial art, or if the Solars learning them are innovating them for the first time. If it's the latter, any Sidereals in the game might feel a bit slighted, since they are technically capable of accessing Mastery effects as well, and are supposed to be &quot;peerless martial artists&quot;. Finding out that, oh yeah, Solar martial artists are capable of just suddenly busting out an extra level of power on all the martial arts that Sidereals have studied and tried to perfect for millennia could rankle. If the effects have existed forever, and you're just retconning their existence, I would at least limit it to martial arts charms that any Sidereals in the group haven't already learned, because finding out that there was a way to do this but apparently <i>they</i> never got to use it before now is also going to be aggravating. Adding retconned Mastery effects to charms they haven't learned at least lets the Sidereals say &quot;Oh, yeah, my old Snake Style sifu could do that too. I never progressed far enough in my training to learn that trick, but she could do a number on you.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T13:21:37-07:00","id":1334012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1334009#post1334009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Without knowing the exact effects being proposed, it's hard to say specifically if anything breaks. Since you're talking about &quot;with ST approval&quot;, my advice will thus center around what the ST should be looking for.<br /> <br /> First, I'd be cautious about allowing <i>every</i> charm in a martial art to have Mastery effects. The charms in an MA are designed holistically, around the idea that they all work together in a certain way. Adding extra powers, particularly to every single charm, may make them overpowered. Be careful that the Mastery-level MA charms aren't overall more powerful than the &quot;native&quot; Solar charmset. The route to being an amazing sword fighter shouldn't always be through Steel Devil Style, just plain Solar Melee has to remain competitive.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is reasonable advice, and I agree with everything posted here. I only thought of this ideal due to how some styles feel less useful then others based on the fact that they have less mastery effects then other styles and often due to that are often seen as not worth getting over native charms. The goal would be for solars to take martial arts and have every charm be as worth getting as native charms. I do not want them to be better then native charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1334009#post1334009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, styles like the Five Immaculate Dragon Styles deliberately have <i>no</i> Mastery keywords, because they were designed, in-setting, to be harmonious with Dragon-Blooded Essence, something the DBs could unlock the potential of just as well as a Solar. Adding Mastery powers to them would break that feeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I apologies, but I forgot to mention that detail yes. I'm fine with IMAs not getting mastery effects for the sake of setting narrative. Even if I feel that just mean no solars will ever have the charms save if they're deliberatively gimping themselves for role-playing reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1334009#post1334009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third, I'd consider whether these new Mastery effects are something that, in setting, have always existed as part of the martial art, or if the Solars learning them are innovating them for the first time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think it would be in the &quot;always existed&quot; category myself. Again this is all for mostly mechanical reasons I think this rule should be here not narrative reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14713-chronos12","name":"Chronos12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14713_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T13:41:33-07:00","id":1334017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chronos12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1334012#post1334012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I only thought of this ideal due to how some styles feel less useful then others based on the fact that they have less mastery effects then other styles and often due to that are often seen as not worth getting over native charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bear in mind that &quot;fewer Mastery effects&quot; doesn't necessarily equal &quot;overall weaker&quot; either. A style could well be designed that was at the top-end of existing martial arts in power, and just have very few Mastery effects. It would just mean that not only Solars, Sidereals, and their peers could access the power, but rather it would be more equally available. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T15:28:02-07:00","id":1334030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chronos12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1334012#post1334012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I apologies, but I forgot to mention that detail yes. I'm fine with IMAs not getting mastery effects for the sake of setting narrative. Even if I feel that just mean no solars will ever have the charms save if they're deliberatively gimping themselves for role-playing reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not entirely true :<br /> <br /> -some IMA uniquely combine with regular MAs, i.e. if a Steel Devil stylist wants to expand beyond their main style, Fire Dragon is the only other MA that focuses on dual wielded swords.<br /> <br /> -some styles are simply a strong fit as a secondary, i.e. Air Dragon is a better fit than most for an Ebon Shadow stylist since it helps with Stealth.<br /> <br /> -some effects are unique to IMAs, i.e. only Wood Style will give you combat healing and let you kill any enemy instantly regardless of their health, including Legendary Size enemies.<br /> <br /> -only IMAs go above Essence 3, which means a Martial Arts Supernal can start the game with powerful Essence 4-5 Martial Arts Charms if she focuses on an IMA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T23:27:50-07:00","id":1334766,"title":"","content":"What breaks if I make a charm, Essence and Medicine 4/5, which cuts down on the costs of Essence 1/2 charms like Instant treatment methodology and Wound Mending care technique. I'm trying to write about a medicine supernal, and having her be hamstrung because she spends 5 motes several times on wound mending care technique several times seems to be a downer. <br /> <br /> And another thing. What about high level charms like on Essence 4/5, that can be comboed with other charms such that the Solar heals not just individual people but heals Magnitude's worth of people. For use on mass battlefields and plague-stricken cities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T03:12:58-07:00","id":1334789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1334766#post1334766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I make a charm, Essence and Medicine 4/5, which cuts down on the costs of Essence 1/2 charms like Instant treatment methodology and Wound Mending care technique. I'm trying to write about a medicine supernal, and having her be hamstrung because she spends 5 motes several times on wound mending care technique several times seems to be a downer.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a number of Charms which have the only function of making other Charms cheaper. Healing Trance Meditation and Life-Exchanging Prana immediately jump to mind. Medicine 5 Essence 4 and a Willpower cost for a decent length (a day, say) sounds fine to me if it uses those Charms as a prereq. (And only effects the low level Charms so you still have reason to use the pre-reqs.)<br /> <br /> Or committed motes that give a discount like Harmonious Presence Meditation would probably be ok for a weaker effect: I'd be ok with a M2 E1 Charm that worked exactly like Harmonious Presence Meditation but for Medicine.<br /> <br /> If you don't balance it, then Charms like Benison of Celestial Healing become worthless. Nothing overly much breaks narratively. Solars are meant to be the ultimate healers of legend. Mechanically, I'd be wary of buffing Feit of Imparted Nature, but otherwise you can't heal wounds which don't exist so I don't think it messes with the mechanical or narrative balance too much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And another thing. What about high level charms like on Essence 4/5, that can be comboed with other charms such that the Solar heals not just individual people but heals Magnitude's worth of people. For use on mass battlefields and plague-stricken cities. </div> </div> </div>I feel like THAT breaks the setting. If you can instantly heal everyone on the battlefield with magic that's way beyond what Solar medicine thematically is about and is mega broken mechanically. <br /> <br /> You actually have to doctor these people.<br /> <br /> Maybe a 1/Story Charm that requires expending 3a that let you impart a single -0 level (that didn't stack with Feit of Imparted Nature) and Exalted-level Disease/Poison resistence to 1 Magnitude for every Aggravated health level you take as you rip yourself in every direction to stabilize hundreds of dying folks would be ok. Not healing as such, but staunching wounds, slowing plague and imparting a new surge of life long enough for the Solar and her allies to heal these folks conventionally.<br /> <br /> If the Solar doctor doesn't have to use her skill but can just cast Mass Heal then this flies counter to Solar themes and removes difficult moral and tactical choices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-10-2019, 06:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T03:41:52-07:00","id":1334792,"title":"","content":"Even a miraculously good doctor has limits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T03:43:45-07:00","id":1334793,"title":"","content":"Just saying this, are you saying that solar medicine charms should always work on a case by case basis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T03:52:24-07:00","id":1334796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1334789#post1334789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Solar doctor doesn't have to use her skill but can just cast Mass Heal then this flies counter to Solar themes and removes difficult moral and tactical choices.</div> </div> </div> </div>But doesn't this apply to, well, everything a Solar does? <br /> <br /> I mean, where do you draw the line? Solars can make healing occur in the span of minutes. Solars can do in several seconds what would take doctors hours of surgery and treatment. Solars can make sure they can always make the right diagnosis. <br /> <br /> <br /> What's the difference between 'cast detect disease' and the solar using the charm that lets her never make a misdiagnosis. What's the difference between 'Heal!' and 'I am so good at doctoring, that my patients recover from near-death in minutes'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T04:06:24-07:00","id":1334802,"title":"","content":"Alright. Fine. What about a mass stabilization event? You have an entire battlefield of bleeding and dying soldiers, and this charm lets you staunch their bleeding and give you one day to solve their problems, whether poison, bleeding, or disease.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T04:10:21-07:00","id":1334804,"title":"","content":"I think it's in-theme for an Essence 5 charm but it's going to have to be something extremely Obvious, like a giant healing saint-like glow. Maybe requiring 3 anima levels to be burnt, or it automatically makes you flare iconically, or something like that. Not just wave your hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T04:26:37-07:00","id":1334810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1334802#post1334802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright. Fine. What about a mass stabilization event? You have an entire battlefield of bleeding and dying soldiers, and this charm lets you staunch their bleeding and give you one day to solve their problems, whether poison, bleeding, or disease.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be fine (even if it's Indefinite).<br /> <br /> Solar Medicine works by you treating the patient. You can cure plague by treating the patient with drinking water and a rag, but you still have to treat the patient.<br /> <br /> A Charm that &quot;just heals people&quot; is outside of Solar scope. A Charm that gives you <i>time</i> to heal people is thematically fine just like a Charm that lets you heal folks quickly or without medicines.<br /> <br /> A Solar should absolutely be able to turn up to a freeway pile-up, roll up her sleeves and blaze totemic with a &quot;nobody dies today!&quot; and make it true by the sweat on her brow as she moves from car-to-car, pulling limbs straight as bones knit together, performing CPR by striking the heart chakra once and stitching wounds by passing her hand over them, all the while the dying people just... don't die, lingering at death's door until she can reach them. (Maybe she even has moma bear moments where she rips cars apart with her bare-hands to free trapped patients (Shattering Grasp).) But even if just spending a few seconds with each patient, you still need to treat each patient.<br /> <br /> You can't just treat &quot;a city&quot; or &quot;an army&quot; as one big organism. (An Infernal might be able to.) And you can't just gesture at a pile-up and magically heal everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-10-2019, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T04:27:00-07:00","id":1334811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1334804#post1334804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's in-theme for an Essence 5 charm but it's going to have to be something extremely Obvious, like a giant healing saint-like glow. Maybe requiring 3 anima levels to be burnt, or it automatically makes you flare iconically, or something like that. Not just wave your hands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't you the guy that replied to me about the 'lone supernatural in the modern world'? <br /> <br /> Remember the car pileup idea? Yes, of course its Obvious. Its Essence 5. Its a thing of legend, where the sun shines in the darkness and, for a moment, death is pushed on a grand scale. A pillar of light, rising into the heavens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T04:28:39-07:00","id":1334812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1334810#post1334810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That'd be fine (even if it's Indefinite).<br /> <br /> Solar Medicine works by you treating the patient. You can cure plague by treating the patient with drinking water and a rag, but you still have to treat the patient.<br /> <br /> A Charm that &quot;just heals people&quot; is outside of Solar scope. A Charm that gives you <i>time</i> to heal people is thematically fine just like a Charm that lets you heal folks quickly or without medicines.<br /> <br /> A Solar should absolutely be able to turn up to a freeway pile-up, roll up her sleeves and blaze totemic with a &quot;nobody dies today!&quot; and make it true by the sweat on her brow as she moves from car to car, pulling limbs straight as bones knit together, performing CPR by striking the heart chakra once and stitching wounds by passing her hand over them, all the while the dying people just... don't die, lingering at deaths door until she can reach them. But even if just spending a few seconds with each patient, you still need to treat each patient.<br /> <br /> You can't just treat &quot;a city&quot; or &quot;an army&quot; as one big organism. (An Infernal might be able to.) And you can't just gesture at a pile-up and magically heal everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I have it so that she flares massively bonfire, and where the light touches, wounds stop bleeding and those patients with illness or poison seem to relax, as their symptoms abate for just a day?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T04:57:32-07:00","id":1334820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1334812#post1334812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I have it so that she flares massively bonfire, and where the light touches, wounds stop bleeding and those patients with illness or poison seem to relax, as their symptoms abate for just a day?</div> </div> </div> </div>You &quot;can&quot; do whatever you want. I am a random nobody, my opinion isn't worth anymore than yours.<br /> <br /> I like the concept. I would probably do things slightly differently but I don't think it breaks anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T05:06:49-07:00","id":1334822,"title":"","content":"It's not that I don't think your opinion matters. It's that it doesnt jive with what I see. I mean, look at craftsman needs no tools. The materials just assemble themselves into it either by hand, breathe, or voice.<br /> <br /> If a solar can become so good a craftsman that he can work materials without touching it, a solar can become so good a doctor he can heal people without touching the patient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T14:30:56-07:00","id":1334979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1334822#post1334822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not that I don't think your opinion matters. It's that it doesnt jive with what I see. I mean, look at craftsman needs no tools. The materials just assemble themselves into it either by hand, breathe, or voice.<br /> <br /> If a solar can become so good a craftsman that he can work materials without touching it, a solar can become so good a doctor he can heal people without touching the patient.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah but the Solar still has to work the materials. They don't assemble themselves whilst she sits and does a crossword. You need to use your action. You need project slots. You need to concentrate on what you're doing. It's still based on your ability to craft.<br /> <br /> If you wanted a Charm where you sing people to good health, I could see that (Deebs have one). I could see a Solar doctor who literally gives their patients the breath of life, or who kisses broken bones better. I even don't have a problem with a Solar using homeopathy that actually works. But at the end of the day, it's grounded in the Solar acting -- using her medical skill to heal the patient.<br /> <br /> The Medicine Charms in the corebook are &quot;at the peak of their power&quot;: they can treat a patient in seconds and with just touches, but &quot;Her efforts still must be efficacious and logical&quot;, and the Charms still hinge on the Solar using her effort (turn) and skill (ability roll). The one Charm in Miracles is also worth a look.<br /> <br /> (And, to be clear, I only objected to mass heal. Mass stabilisation is fine -- very in-theme.)<br /> <br /> But we're straying from the idea of &quot;what breaks if&quot; now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-10-2019, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T13:00:34-07:00","id":1338858,"title":"","content":"What breaks if I make the following change to combat rules :<br /> <br /> Every combatant on the same side in a battle add and subtract from a single shared initiative pool for the team. Everything else is still resolved normally, you attack team members individually and try to overcome their parry and soak as usual, but the target's initiative is the combined initiative of every member of her team.<br /> <br /> <u>example :</u> 3 DBs fight 2 blood apes<br /> <br /> 1) the 3 DBs roll Join Battle and get 8, 9 &amp; 5 ini, for a shared pool of 22. The 2 Blood apes roll 6 &amp; 8 for a total of 14.<br /> 2) the DBs go first in whatever order they prefer.<br /> 3) DB1 Withers blood ape 1 for 8 ini, DB 2 Withers blood ape 2 for 6 ini, crashing the blood apes at 0 ini.<br /> 4) DB 3 launches a 43 ini Decisive against blood ape 1, demolishing them and resetting the DB team's ini to 3<br /> 5) blood ape 2 Withers DB 3 for 8 ini, crashing the DBs down to -5 and getting an initiative shift, then they decisive DB 1 with 13 ini and unleash 2 more Withering attacks with Principle of Motion<br /> 6) etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T13:38:11-07:00","id":1338861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1338858#post1338858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I make the following change to combat rules :<br /> <br /> Every combatant on the same side in a battle add and subtract from a single shared initiative pool for the team.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're going to have to try it and tell us.<br /> <br /> I forsee a lot of wonk: every time a PC launches a Decisive, basically the entire party gets Crashed, loses their Perilous Charms and no-one else can launch a Decisive. Which if you invested in Heavy Armor to tank is going to be frustrating. Outnumbering your foes becomes slightly less valuable (a sword which cuts both ways) unless the numbers difference changes the Initative order.<br /> <br /> I'd probably make characters act in their Join Battle order (like Battlegroups).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T15:22:01-07:00","id":1338879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1338858#post1338858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I make the following change to combat rules :<br /> <br /> Every combatant on the same side in a battle add and subtract from a single shared initiative pool for the team. Everything else is still resolved normally, you attack team members individually and try to overcome their parry and soak as usual, but the target's initiative is the combined initiative of every member of her team.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it's certainly going to change things. I say give it a shot, but I have to be honest that's coming from my own curiosity than anything. My initial thought is that it's going to make turn one, especially with multi-target decisive attacks bonkerz. Like if you had a full circle of Solars you could easily get 40 initiative and then the Dawn just activates Invincible Fury of the Dawn and Thunderbolt Attack Prana and kills the entire enemy side before they even got to act.<br /> <br /> Distract gambits also become kind of useless.<br /> <br /> I dunno it might work though, as long as your party doesn't decide to try and abuse it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T15:33:32-07:00","id":1338880,"title":"","content":"Also a lot of abilities need you to lower a foe below your own initiative, in a group setting that can be more powerful (Teamwork!) or frustrating (no teamwork)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T17:16:52-07:00","id":1338896,"title":"","content":"After fiddling with it a bit, I think it might be an interesting way to model a team effort in an epic battle, i.e. when it's Circle vs Circle or Circle vs Kaiju. But I don't think it would work as a general rule for every battle, because any fight where the offensive capabilities of one side aren't matched by the defensive capabilities of the other will turn into a mess of alpha strikes pretty quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T06:37:26-07:00","id":1340404,"title":"","content":"What breaks if I make Thunderbolt Attack Prana into a simple charm that keeps all the text is has now, except it lets you make an attack with any other close ranged ability, rather than supplementing an existing one.<br /> <br /> It mostly comes from my problem that most other effects seem pretty balanced from the standpoint of big epic effect costs big epic motes and willpower, and even then you approach a limit, but especially when supplementing Simple type charms like Heaven Sword Flash or Invincible Fury of the Dawn I find it just pushes it too far, especially for the relatively low cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T06:59:22-07:00","id":1340406,"title":"","content":"I think it's fine, but what is your problem with it exactly ?<br /> <br /> The personnal problem I have is that almost any fighter I have at my table take TAP because it's just so strong. If you think it allows for too much shenanigans or whatnot with multi attack then there should be no &quot;breaking&quot; by making it a simple Charm : It's already a cool Charm with a cool effect that works in itself.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T07:40:12-07:00","id":1340413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1340406#post1340406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's fine, but what is your problem with it exactly ?<br /> <br /> The personnal problem I have is that almost any fighter I have at my table take TAP because it's just so strong. If you think it allows for too much shenanigans or whatnot with multi attack then there should be no &amp;quot;breaking&amp;quot; by making it a simple Charm : It's already a cool Charm with a cool effect that works in itself.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I was mostly thinking of things like if you\u2019re surrounded by powerful beastmen, and you go really hard, like use Fire and Stones Strike, full excellency, Excellent Strike and Rising Sun Slash to ensure you hit with 3 overflow, and maybe one other decisive damage adder, and combo it with Heaven Sword Flash you can actually just take out every single beastman in Close range. It\u2019s very expensive to do, but also awesome. If you add TAP in there you can do that with Lunar Exalted, and that I\u2019m less of a fan of. <br /> <br /> The same goes for Invincible Fury of the Dawn, although that one\u2019s much better against a single target. It not only doubles the base damage, but also the damage boosters, which are themselves multiplied by the number of attacks you make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T09:06:52-07:00","id":1340422,"title":"","content":"Yeah I never really had a strong melee character at my table (most prefer brawl or MA, I don't know why) but I see where you are going. I honestly think it's fine to make it a Simple Charm. You can still enhance it with supplemental and have good things out of it.<br /> <br /> I'm personnaly considering making a bit further in the Athletics tree (or essence 2 or something) because I'm bored of people auto buying it. I'll see with my next game","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T09:53:55-07:00","id":1340431,"title":"","content":"Yeah the internal balance is also a bit wonky. Compared to the Essence 3 Hungry Tiger Technique which can only be used on crashed targets, only gives you bonus damage equal to your overflow successes, and only stacks linearly with other forms of decisive damage adders, you could probably even put it at Essence 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T10:11:55-07:00","id":1340434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1340431#post1340431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah the internal balance is also a bit wonky. Compared to the Essence 3 Hungry Tiger Technique which can only be used on crashed targets, only gives you bonus damage equal to your overflow successes, and only stacks linearly with other forms of decisive damage adders, you could probably even put it at Essence 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking Essence 3 is a lot because it's at the same Essence that Dragon Blooded got their Brawl signature Charm that has basically the same effect, and logically Solars access effects at a lower Essence level that Solars, but I'm not sure my reasoning makes sense","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T10:17:14-07:00","id":1340436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1340434#post1340434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking Essence 3 is a lot because it's at the same Essence that Dragon Blooded got their Brawl signature Charm that has basically the same effect, and logically Solars access effects at a lower Essence level that Solars, but I'm not sure my reasoning makes sense</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, which signature charm does that? I might be missing something here...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T11:00:17-07:00","id":1340444,"title":"","content":"Oh wait, you might mean the water melee signature Roaring River Slash, where you roll damage twice and add the result together? It\u2019s a very similar effect but the charm itself as well as it\u2019s context in the charmset, is very different. For one it\u2019s a simple charm, and another it expends water aura, which mean together the only melee charms that can supplement it are the excellency and the one that ignores a few points of hardness, so there just isn\u2019t that same potential to explode. Which is good, Solars are about combining ten different effects to blow up.<br /> <br /> Sometimes Solars and DBs get effects at the same Essence, like true flight, but they\u2019re not always so easy to compare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T12:48:04-07:00","id":1340467,"title":"","content":"It's also unusable by Air/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T12:50:19-07:00","id":1340468,"title":"","content":"It's also unusable by Air/Earth/Fire/Wood aspects in bonfire, due to the Aura requirement. Even for Water aspects, being in Aura when using melee (mostly Fire-aspected) is awkward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T15:59:35-07:00","id":1340512,"title":"","content":"True, for a water swordsman being able to straight up double decisive damage is their special awesome power to punch above their limits, but for Solars, at least with TAP as written, it\u2019s more the sauce to go on a lethal combo that can already kill almost anything, and ensure that it does 80% of the time or more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T23:55:44-07:00","id":1340568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1340444#post1340444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh wait, you might mean the water melee signature Roaring River Slash, where you roll damage twice and add the result together? It\u2019s a very similar effect but the charm itself as well as it\u2019s context in the charmset, is very different. For one it\u2019s a simple charm, and another it expends water aura, which mean together the only melee charms that can supplement it are the excellency and the one that ignores a few points of hardness, so there just isn\u2019t that same potential to explode. Which is good, Solars are about combining ten different effects to blow up.<br /> <br /> Sometimes Solars and DBs get effects at the same Essence, like true flight, but they\u2019re not always so easy to compare.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah sorry I read it a long time ago and kept the idea of double damage but without context or details. Maybe putting TAP Essence 3 might be good for me then if my next table goes for it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T05:45:29-07:00","id":1340599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1340568#post1340568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah sorry I read it a long time ago and kept the idea of double damage but without context or details. Maybe putting TAP Essence 3 might be good for me then if my next table goes for it</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and if your group isn\u2019t currently having a problem with it, like they\u2019re not way overdoing it Essence 2 might just be fine anyway, I just think that even at 3 it\u2019s balanced. Plus that was an athletics Supernal can do some really powerful combat thing right off the bat that sets him apart, while making the combat Supernal still better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T08:26:32-07:00","id":1340621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1340404#post1340404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I make Thunderbolt Attack Prana into a simple charm that keeps all the text is has now, except it lets you make an attack with any other close ranged ability, rather than supplementing an existing one.<br /> <br /> It mostly comes from my problem that most other effects seem pretty balanced from the standpoint of big epic effect costs big epic motes and willpower, and even then you approach a limit, but especially when supplementing Simple type charms like Heaven Sword Flash or Invincible Fury of the Dawn I find it just pushes it too far, especially for the relatively low cost.</div> </div> </div> </div><s>Could you use Supplemental Charms from the Combat Ability used to make the attack?</s><br /> <br /> Just read the text. Yeah, looks fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T11:05:00-07:00","id":1340806,"title":"","content":"...I ditch Solar XP split and just give a flat ~8 xp per session?<br /> <br /> <br /> ...I ditch XP altogether and grant Bonus Points instead? Say ~2 per session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T11:40:57-07:00","id":1340813,"title":"","content":"Solar exp exists to incentivize players to buy other things than Charms. Charms are such an incredibly superior investment that the devs literally had to create a separate exp that allows everything except Charms to get players to spend their exp on other things.<br /> <br /> So the worst case is your players will no longer buy anything but Charms.<br /> <br /> Using BP instead of exp should work fine, I think several people here do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T14:37:41-07:00","id":1340844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1340806#post1340806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I ditch Solar XP split and just give a flat ~8 xp per session?<br /> <br /> <br /> ...I ditch XP altogether and grant Bonus Points instead? Say ~2 per session.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar XP is a really good incentive to round out your basic stats instead of buying more &quot;kill things&quot; Charms. The expression bonuses encourage roleplay and interesting group dynamics. I'd be more inclined to award Solar XP to the whole party than ace it entirely. What are you trying to achieve?<br /> <br /> I've awarded BP instead of XP on a 1-to-1 basis for years. Works great. Halving the rate should work fine too -- reasonably balanced characters should grow at roughly the same rate as if you were using XP. The reason I go 1:1 is because Charms are grotesquely overcosted in BP, meaning PCs who go heavy into Charms will lag in development compared to if they were earning XP. And also it fixes fractional problems with abilities that cost XP and don't have a BP cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T14:50:29-07:00","id":1340847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1340844#post1340844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are you trying to achieve?</div> </div> </div> </div>Simplicity, mostly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T01:47:33-07:00","id":1340920,"title":"","content":"I got a headcanon. But...<br /> <br /> What breaks if I make it so that Old Realm can be understood instinctively by anyone who hears or reads it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T02:26:02-07:00","id":1340921,"title":"","content":"If they can understand it, why can't they speak it? If they can speak it, why other languages? Tower of Babel problem. Not an insolvable question - perhaps it is taboo avoidance, other languages are preferred for ethnic marking etc. but a question nonetheless. Compounded if we go for take a sort of Saphir-Whorf esque stance that Old Realm is a particularly special vehicle of communication that would be preferred (which I can't remember if the text ever did!). <br /> <br /> On another game and setting tack, what happens to all the ancient texts with lost knowledge which only savants knowledgable in the Old Realm can read? Are those replaced with codes / ciphers / constructed languages to keep the setting function of making texts opaque?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T08:02:33-07:00","id":1344190,"title":"","content":"... You partially ignore charm prerequisites? Allowing, say, &quot;any X charms in the same ability&quot; to replace a specific charm prereq, with X equal to twice the charm's Essence requirement? That should hopefully simplify charm selection and let you skip past ones you don't care for without letting you jump straight to high-tier charms...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T08:14:41-07:00","id":1344191,"title":"","content":"Well, the first thing you need to do is find a way to actually get the starting charms in a tree. No charm has a pre-req if zero so you need to at least have the first two be available in some way. It also affects different exalted in wildly different ways. For a Solar with Supernal in their abilities it\u2019s going to be crazy good. You can just go down one branch of their massive combat trees and then pick up the capstone charms from each of the other branches in one swoop. You also might run into problems where some charms are just upgrades of their previous charm, so you need to specify if those can be taken and just automatically grant what they\u2019re upgrading, or if they still have charm prerequisites. I don\u2019t know if it\u2019s broken exactly, but it will let Solars get a lot more with a lot less investment.<br /> <br /> For Dragonblooded it\u2019s going to be awful, and I mean absolutely wretched. There\u2019s some elemental sections of charm trees that you really just kinda want to take that element, and to get the big badass Essence 5 capstone for that element you\u2019d hate having to take a bunch of charms that you\u2019re barely ever going to use just to get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T08:18:21-07:00","id":1344193,"title":"","content":"(For clarity, it would be an optional substitution-- you could do the normal prereq, OR the &quot;any X charms&quot; thing. So you could always take no-requirement charms normally. And if there's a high-essence charm you really want, you can always zip straight down the tree to it. A charm that upgrades the prerequisite would do nothing if you don't have said charm to upgrade)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12314,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","user":"Grod_the_giant","date":". 10-28-2019, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T08:54:10-07:00","id":1344199,"title":"","content":"A generalized system is bound to run into potential abuses and strange edge cases like DrLoveMonkey has pointed out. If the players can be trusted to play fair it shouldn't cause too much trouble.<br /> <br /> Personally if a player wanted 1 or 2 Charms in the middle of a tree but did not want either the Charms before or the Charms after, I'd simply come up with alternate pre-requisites for those Charms specifically for that character. A change in the Charm trees that is balanced for 1 character might be broken for another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T09:23:30-07:00","id":1344205,"title":"","content":"Moreover, it can create a strange dissonance as regards Charm progression. There\u2019s a reason they\u2019re in the order that they\u2019re in, and getting the battle-rage tree of Resistance as your prerequisites for Adamant Skin Technique but <i>no</i> soak enhancers is a tad strange.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T13:54:17-07:00","id":1344745,"title":"","content":"If I apply the Double 10s rule on Decisive damage and Gambit rolls, move all Double #s charms down a #, and give everyone a free Ox-Body that doesn't count against their (Stamina) max? <br /> <br /> I ask this because my players steadfastly refuse to remember that Double 10s is on everything except Decisive damage and Gambits, so I'd like to just rip that exception straight out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T14:15:41-07:00","id":1344747,"title":"","content":"I guess it's not an awesome fix from a design perspective because it interacts strangely with pre existing Charms and it isn't well balanced statistically, but if your players have difficulty remembering I guess augmenting baseline HP isn't too problematic","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T16:40:00-07:00","id":1344773,"title":"","content":"The overall difference is minor, the real thing the no double 10s rule does is remove extreme variance from attacks that can kill.<br /> <br /> So by allowing double 10s, what happens is you create the possibility for a lucky enemy with 6 initiative to one-shot one of your players, creating a feeling that you can randomly die at any moment similar to critical hits in D&amp;D/Pathfinder.<br /> <br /> If that's something you and your players can live with then all is good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T16:51:10-07:00","id":1344774,"title":"","content":"It also normalizes bad rolls just a touch, like now rolling 15 dice and getting three 10s and a 7 is better. The difference won\u2019t come up that often though and I don\u2019t think it breaks anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T04:13:42-08:00","id":1346120,"title":"","content":"Potentially a solution in search of a problem, but here goes, a Q for the mechanically savvy out there\u2026<br /> <br /> How badly would the game break if at bonfire, rather than being locked out of non-balanced and non-native-aspect charms, DBs count as having the aura of both their native aspect AND the aura relevant to their most recent charm use simultaneously?<br /> <br /> E.g. a water-aspected melee-ist uses Stoking Bonfire Style and Crimson Fang Bite, hitting bonfire. He enters water aura \u2018naturally\u2019 and elects to simultaneously enter fire aura (cue cool mixed anima of a raging waterfall dotted with oil slick-type fires or the like).<br /> <br /> Essentially, never liked the locking you out of your charms mechanic and how hard certain DB/non-native-aspect combat abilities seem to be to play \u2013 air-aspected swordsman, AKA Tepet Arada, I\u2019m looking at you \u2013 as a result (although appreciate that balanced charms mitigate that, certain aspects just don\u2019t lend themselves to certain abilities easily and that DBs need a cap on charm combos to keep in-setting relative power levels working etc).<br /> <br /> Reasoning behind the suggestion is (a) it still emphasises the native aspect of the DB a la the lock-out mechanisim (i.e. your native charms are still the things you find easiest when you go all out), (b) makes you less leery of choosing a combat ability that\u2019s out of aspect as all of the non-basic toys aren\u2019t locked away, while still not handing you carte blanche to use every charm going, (c) <a href=\"https://youtu.be/VNT866uM6dU?t=55\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.<br /> <br /> Too much added (not always popular) aura bookkeeping? Makes a DB fight too predictable? Everyone would race to get into bonfire. Would also mean that, for example, an earth aspect at bonfire would always be able to use Impervious Skin of Stone after an attack while merrily swinging away with fire melee charms, which might unbalance things between the aspects\u2026<br /> <br /> [Edited for bad initial charm example...]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 11-05-2019, 07:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T18:46:32-08:00","id":1346328,"title":"","content":"Having 2 auras at once should be a noticeable power up, although I'm not mechanics savvy enough to go into just how much.<br /> <br /> One way you could avoid most balance issues is, instead of being in the 2 auras at once, when you hit bonfire you pick which one you want to be locked into (either your current Aura or your aspect Aura). While this won't solve getting locked out at bonfire, it should solve the problem that some aspects are worse at an ability than others, while still making your aspect aura easier to access than the others, and still allowing a hybrid aura imagery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T02:04:08-08:00","id":1346402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1346328#post1346328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One way you could avoid most balance issues is, instead of being in the 2 auras at once, when you hit bonfire you pick which one you want to be locked into (either your current Aura or your aspect Aura). While this won't solve getting locked out at bonfire, it should solve the problem that some aspects are worse at an ability than others, while still making your aspect aura easier to access than the others, and still allowing a hybrid aura imagery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice! More elegant and streamlined than my suggestion...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T02:26:19-08:00","id":1346404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1346328#post1346328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having 2 auras at once should be a noticeable power up, although I'm not mechanics savvy enough to go into just how much.<br /> <br /> One way you could avoid most balance issues is, instead of being in the 2 auras at once, when you hit bonfire you pick which one you want to be locked into (either your current Aura or your aspect Aura). While this won't solve getting locked out at bonfire, it should solve the problem that some aspects are worse at an ability than others, while still making your aspect aura easier to access than the others, and still allowing a hybrid aura imagery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I think Epitome's idea is quite fine I'd allow it if I found DB elemental auras were too restrictive on this point","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T11:09:54-08:00","id":1347965,"title":"","content":"How much does it break balance if I change Terrestrial MA's in the following way :<br /> <br /> -At Essence 2, a Terrestrial Martial Artist may repurchase Essence 1 Martial Arts Charms they know to remove the Terrestrial Keyword<br /> -At Essence 4 they may do the same with Essence 2 Martial Arts Charms<br /> -Essence 3+ Martial Arts Charms cannot be upgraded in this way and can only ever lose their Terrestrial Keyword with the effect of Immaculate Martial Arts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T11:38:01-08:00","id":1347975,"title":"","content":"From a balance perspective I don't know. What I can say from a design perspective is I find Charm repurchases (especially those in the Solar Core Book, I haven't look too much into the other splats) very boring, because you invest so much in what usually feels so little from a growth perspective for your character. <br /> <br /> If I may do a suggestion : A player can negotiate with the ST that, if he successfully use the MA Charm or a chain of MA Charm (for those that are interdependent) in a scene where he achieves specific objectives tied to the Martial Art, he loses the Terrestrial Keyword ? For example, for Armor-Penetrating Fang Strike (Exalted Core p.428), if your Dragon-Blooded was a Wyld Hunt shikari totally devoted to hunting the Solar Anathema, successfully crashing a Solar/Abyssal in Heavy Artefact armor using this Charm in a fight scene would unlock the Terrestrial keyword for him on this Charm ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T12:12:27-08:00","id":1347981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1347975#post1347975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a balance perspective I don't know. What I can say from a design perspective is I find Charm repurchases (especially those in the Solar Core Book, I haven't look too much into the other splats) very boring, because you invest so much in what usually feels so little from a growth perspective for your character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that wouldn't be too problematic for Martial Arts Charms, as removing the Terrestrial Keyword is a dramatic upgrade stronger than most Upgrade Charms, let alone most Charm Repurchases.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1347975#post1347975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I may do a suggestion : A player can negotiate with the ST that, if he successfully use the MA Charm or a chain of MA Charm (for those that are interdependent) in a scene where he achieves specific objectives tied to the Martial Art, he loses the Terrestrial Keyword ? For example, for Armor-Penetrating Fang Strike (Exalted Core p.428), if your Dragon-Blooded was a Wyld Hunt shikari totally devoted to hunting the Solar Anathema, successfully crashing a Solar/Abyssal in Heavy Artefact armor using this Charm in a fight scene would unlock the Terrestrial keyword for him on this Charm ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an interesting idea and probably the most sensible solution, but I still want to figure out a more general solution that doesn't rely on ST fiat if I can.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T12:58:26-08:00","id":1347988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1347981#post1347981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that wouldn't be too problematic for Martial Arts Charms, as removing the Terrestrial Keyword is a dramatic upgrade stronger than most Upgrade Charms, let alone most Charm Repurchases.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's an interesting idea and probably the most sensible solution, but I still want to figure out a more general solution that doesn't rely on ST fiat if I can.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess sour solution is fine then. I'm not an expert on MA, the one I saw on Armor-Penetrating Fang Strike really didn't seem worth a rebuy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T10:46:38-08:00","id":1348298,"title":"","content":"What breaks if you lose some initiative when you try to decisive attack a target you have not attacked the prior round? Trying to mitigate decisive target switching without managing a concept of &quot;target&quot;, but also not making it more difficult to alternatingly wither multiple targets to manage initiative.<br /> <br /> Would there need to be a &quot;round 1&quot; clause so that alpha strikes can still happen, or could they stand to have a little less edge?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":1542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","user":"MoroseMorgan","date":". 11-13-2019, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T15:39:50-08:00","id":1348345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1348298#post1348298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if you lose some initiative when you try to decisive attack a target you have not attacked the prior round? Trying to mitigate decisive target switching without managing a concept of &quot;target&quot;, but also not making it more difficult to alternatingly wither multiple targets to manage initiative.<br /> <br /> Would there need to be a &quot;round 1&quot; clause so that alpha strikes can still happen, or could they stand to have a little less edge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, ambushes are going to be defanged and anytime somebody's 'target' is killed by someone else/flees/surrenders/etc that guy is going to lose initiative for something totally out of their control. <br /> It also sets up some cheesy things involving two attackers shuffling who's at close. Alice hits Bob with a withering, so Bob disengages while Carl steps forward and attacks. Alice can't decisive her 'target' unless she wins the roll-off. <br /> <br /> But more importantly, I can't speak to what will happen in your game without knowing the problem you're encountering. What circumstances are people engaging in decisive target switching in, and what problems is it causing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T15:07:36-08:00","id":1348561,"title":"","content":"What breaks if...<br /> <br /> Crashed targets do not award initiative from withering attacks? So, they can be driven further into crash by repeated withering attacks, but each only awards the +1 initiative for a successful attack?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T15:20:47-08:00","id":1348563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elkovash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1348561#post1348561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if...<br /> <br /> Crashed targets do not award initiative from withering attacks? So, they can be driven further into crash by repeated withering attacks, but each only awards the +1 initiative for a successful attack?</div> </div> </div> </div>Overall it causes initiative to drain from the system faster than it accumulates, so the longer a fight drags on the less ini there will be to go around.<br /> <br /> On defense, it limits comebacks. Suppose you initiative shift an enemy, sending you from -5 to 7 while the enemy goes from 5 to -2. Well now you're stuck at 7 for your extra free attack, and for 3 more turns after that.<br /> <br /> On the attacking side, since using a Decisive on someone doesn't put them out of Crash, it means you get stuck at 3 ini for 2-3 turns before you can gain ini again, so Decisives become much more punishing and the chance you'll get initiative shifted rises dramatically. This encourages degenerate gameplay where you drive the enemy further into crash while gaining no ini yourself for 2 turns so that you can always Decisive on the last turn of an enemy's Crash.<br /> <br /> <i>Edit:</i><br /> For something like that to work I'd recommend a few more tweaks :<br /> <br /> -successfully using a Decisive takes someone out of Crash immediately<br /> <br /> -adding ways to increase the total initiative in the system (such as in the Momentum Exalted combat rework where stunts award initiative)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 11-14-2019, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T15:45:45-08:00","id":1348568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elkovash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1348561#post1348561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if...<br /> <br /> Crashed targets do not award initiative from withering attacks? So, they can be driven further into crash by repeated withering attacks, but each only awards the +1 initiative for a successful attack?</div> </div> </div> </div>Decisive defenses usable in Crash become a lot stronger. The Twilight Anima power won't be that big of a deal, but Adamant Skin Technique becomes absolutely insane if the only way to get much more initiative off you is to wait until you reset from Crash.<br /> Defend Other becomes <i>really really irritating</i> when the defender is Crashed. I can imagine a Suicide War Lion build that throws up Fivefold and then face-tanks every withering attack directed at his team. Couple with AST and I think you could seriously break the combat engine.<br /> <br /> But barring AST and chicanery, I think the only big issues Epitome didn't cover would be that a barely-crashed enemy becomes a dilemma and that it promotes a bunch of target-switching if you're aiming for a 1HK.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T16:20:00-08:00","id":1348571,"title":"","content":"Ta. <br /> <br /> I had initially thought that shifting might give the INT injection the system needs to keep running but I hadn\u2019t crunched any hard numbers just yet. <br /> <br /> Or to promote more low-initiative decisives.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll think more on it and come back. <br /> <br /> Thanks again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T03:01:04-08:00","id":1348632,"title":"","content":"What breaks if Invulnerable Skin of Bronze gives you -0 health levels that do not interact with the effects of Charms instead of Soak ?<br /> <br /> Basically I don't like permanent Soak cumulable very much, but I'm fine with the other effects of the spell. If the -0 provided by the spell are depleted, it acts the same than Virtuous Guardian of Flame : Dissipates for the day and the spell cannot be relaunched for the remaining duration. What amount of health you think would be acceptable ? I'm hesitating between 3 (to make it an Ox Body technique with side effect) or more ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T12:29:44-08:00","id":1348702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1348632#post1348632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if Invulnerable Skin of Bronze gives you -0 health levels that do not interact with the effects of Charms instead of Soak ?<br /> <br /> Basically I don't like permanent Soak cumulable very much, but I'm fine with the other effects of the spell. If the -0 provided by the spell are depleted, it acts the same than Virtuous Guardian of Flame : Dissipates for the day and the spell cannot be relaunched for the remaining duration. What amount of health you think would be acceptable ? I'm hesitating between 3 (to make it an Ox Body technique with side effect) or more ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Shouldn't break anything unless you've got a character using it to compensate for awful Soak. Or a Soak-Monster who's prone to whining. <br /> Having it provide health will make Invincible God-Metal Flash a lot lamer, though. <br /> Having the health be entirely -0s means the spell will end very quickly, generally in the first Decisive the user takes damage from. Your call as to if that's desirable. <br /> <br /> Your problem is ISoB stacking on top of Stamina, armor, and Charms to create absurd Soak pools, correct? As an alternate solution, why not make ISoB's Soak replace the Soak you gain from Stamina? That should leave it still beneficial to cast but impede the stacking. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T16:56:19-08:00","id":1348753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1348702#post1348702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shouldn't break anything unless you've got a character using it to compensate for awful Soak. Or a Soak-Monster who's prone to whining.<br /> Having it provide health will make Invincible God-Metal Flash a lot lamer, though.<br /> Having the health be entirely -0s means the spell will end very quickly, generally in the first Decisive the user takes damage from. Your call as to if that's desirable.<br /> <br /> Your problem is ISoB stacking on top of Stamina, armor, and Charms to create absurd Soak pools, correct? As an alternate solution, why not make ISoB's Soak replace the Soak you gain from Stamina? That should leave it still beneficial to cast but impede the stacking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fine with awful soak and whiners.<br /> Why would Invincible God-Metal Flash get lamer ?<br /> I think you are right and won't &quot;dissipates the spell&quot; once the -0 health levels are depleted. They are just gone and can't regenerate, but the sorcerer can still benefit from every other bonuses for the day. The spell is just gone. The only way to lose all benefits is to use God Metal Flash, or lose some to distortion. <br /> <br /> Your assumption is correct. I really hesitated between both solutions. The problem I have with your solution (I like it more personally) is that through talk with other players they feel it as a nerf of the spell, and god people don't like nerfed things. Meanwhile more health points doesn't seem to bother them, it's just another alternative, even one that seems better than a Solar Charm so why not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T02:18:04-08:00","id":1348816,"title":"","content":"<s>ISoB provides Natural Soak but counts as Medium Armor. It doesn't stack with armor (outside of the Control Spell benefit).</s><br /> <br /> Apparently this is wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-16-2019, 08:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T03:35:24-08:00","id":1348826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1348816#post1348816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ISoB provides Natural Soak but counts as Medium Armor. It doesn't stack with armor (outside of the Control Spell benefit).</div> </div> </div> </div>Really ? I'm pretty sure I read aconvo somewhere where it was said it stacked with armor. If that's not the case I have no need for fix then. Thx !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T05:33:50-08:00","id":1348834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1348826#post1348826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really ? I'm pretty sure I read aconvo somewhere where it was said it stacked with armor. If that's not the case I have no need for fix then. Thx !</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure it stacks with armor. <span style=\"color:#000000\"> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">&quot;The Invulnerable Skin of Bronze </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">gives the sorcerer +6 natural soak and Hardness 6&quot; gives natural soak, nothing about not stacking with armor.<br /> The only mention of armor is &quot;</span><span style=\"font-family:-webkit-standard\">s</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">he is considered to be wearing medium armor,</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">which might deny her the use of certain Martial Arts</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">styles or other e</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">ffects.&quot; One could argue that armor is an effect that is denied while wearing other armor, but that seems like a fairly twisty interpretation to me.<br /> <br /> &quot;</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">A sorcerer who knows Invulnerable Skin of Bronze as her </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">control spell may add her Essence to the soak and Hardness bonus she receives as long as she is unarmored. Even without the spell, her skin takes on a faint bronze tint. She may also </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">add her Essence to her soak when the spell is not in e</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">ff</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">ect.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't think this clause makes any sense if it's impossible to be both armored and using the spell, or if using the spell makes you count as armored.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> </span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T05:43:24-08:00","id":1348835,"title":"","content":"To clear any confusion, Devs have stated it stacks.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1072762#post1072762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It stacks with armor. The &quot;counts as medium armor&quot; is for purposes of things that aren't compatible with armor, like Diamond-Body Prana.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T07:37:42-08:00","id":1348857,"title":"","content":"Yeah ok I'll go with the bonus hp as discussed then. Thanks for help ! Btw any suggestion as to how many -0 health level would be good given what I intend to do ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T08:08:44-08:00","id":1348860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1348753#post1348753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would Invincible God-Metal Flash get lamer ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Say the spell gives 3 -0 HL. Activating God-Metal Flash now makes you lose 3HL in order to get (Essence +5) damage reduction, meaning God-Metal Flash now provides 3 less DR total.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1348857#post1348857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah ok I'll go with the bonus hp as discussed then. Thanks for help ! Btw any suggestion as to how many -0 health level would be good given what I intend to do ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Health levels is a very different benefit from Soak and Hardness, there's not really a 1:1 conversion you can make, but I figure 3 would be a safe bet.<br /> <br /> Another idea to change the spell could be to make the soak not stack with Stamina as prncss suggested, and in return make the 6 soak/hardness of ISOB ignore effects that bypass soak/hardness, so it doesn't just replace natural soak but actually makes it better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T09:07:18-08:00","id":1348871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1348860#post1348860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say the spell gives 3 -0 HL. Activating God-Metal Flash now makes you lose 3HL in order to get (Essence +5) damage reduction, meaning God-Metal Flash now provides 3 less DR total.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Health levels is a very different benefit from Soak and Hardness, there's not really a 1:1 conversion you can make, but I figure 3 would be a safe bet.<br /> <br /> Another idea to change the spell could be to make the soak not stack with Stamina as prncss suggested, and in return make the 6 soak/hardness of ISOB ignore effects that bypass soak/hardness, so it doesn't just replace natural soak but actually makes it better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll try the soak version, but if I feel my players uncomfortable with the &quot;nerf&quot; I'll sitch to the health version.<br /> <br /> Yeah ok I get it for God Metal Flash, I'll think of a solution that makes sense. Thanks for the common sense","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T10:18:27-08:00","id":1349111,"title":"","content":"... If you applied half your soak to successes on Withering damage rolls, instead of reducing the number of dice before rolling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T10:23:01-08:00","id":1349112,"title":"","content":"Certain Charms add or reduce damage after soak, so those would need to be adjusted bare minimum.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T10:38:30-08:00","id":1349119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1349111#post1349111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... If you applied half your soak to successes on Withering damage rolls, instead of reducing the number of dice before rolling?</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming this gets rid of overwhelming, high soak becomes incredibly powerful.<br /> <br /> Things that trigger off of taking no damage get either a boost or a penalty, depending on specifics.<br /> <br /> The probability curve of damage gets a lot wider, since more dice are being rolled","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T11:38:58-08:00","id":1349132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1349111#post1349111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... If you applied half your soak to successes on Withering damage rolls, instead of reducing the number of dice before rolling?</div> </div> </div> </div>autXautY's analysis is spot on, but here's a thing that will let you play with numbers to see exactly what the difference would be. <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://anydice.com/program/189d0\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://anydice.com/anydice-banner.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://anydice.com/program/189d0\" target=\"_blank\"> AnyDice </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://anydice.com/program/189d0\" target=\"_blank\"> https://anydice.com/program/189d0 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> AnyDice is an advanced dice probability calculator, available online. It is created with roleplaying games in mind. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T04:44:26-08:00","id":1351842,"title":"","content":"What breaks if... You downgrade the Deathlords to powerful ghosts who have Underworld domains and replace the incursions into Creation by the Abyssals under the direct command of the Neverborn?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800080\">I express my opinions, but YSMV; Your Stories May Vary.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Formerly known as wyrmpuff</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12288-mal-akh","name":"Mal'akh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12288_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T05:02:53-08:00","id":1351845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal'akh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1351842#post1351842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if... You downgrade the Deathlords to powerful ghosts who have Underworld domains and replace the incursions into Creation by the Abyssals under the direct command of the Neverborn?</div> </div> </div> </div>The deathlords things where they've got every single charm? <br /> <br /> Really frickin' stupid. <br /> <br /> Now, Neverborn giving commands? What are they like? Remember, these are huge titan things, dreaming and dying, yet living on at the same time, filled to the brim with insanity-destroying nightmares.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T05:54:13-08:00","id":1351849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal'akh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1351842#post1351842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if... You downgrade the Deathlords to powerful ghosts who have Underworld domains and replace the incursions into Creation by the Abyssals under the direct command of the Neverborn?</div> </div> </div> </div>Must say I'm not against the idea. When I discovered Exalted 3e (So I had 0 knowledge of Exalted lore) and read the chapter about the Dead and Underworld, i didn't understand a single thing about who was in charge and that left me very confused. Apparently the dead huge guys succesfully stole the soul of the guy that killed them and made them into overlord that can now create sub-overlord guyz that are supposed to oppose the Solar guys that killed their master in the first place ?<br /> <br /> I really prefer your idea. There are neverborn, which are dead titans, and Abyssal descends directly from the neverborn. Deathlords obeys the neverborn (or not), but are just powerful ghost ennemies. Much clearer to me.<br /> <br /> As a note : I still don't know exactly what is the relationship between Neverborn, Deathlords and Abyssals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T05:59:31-08:00","id":1351850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1351849#post1351849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a note : I still don't know exactly what is the relationship between Neverborn, Deathlords and Abyssals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Urm... do you want me to explain it? Its a bit long and convoluted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T06:37:37-08:00","id":1351853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1351850#post1351850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its a bit long and convoluted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hardly.<br /> <br /> The <b>Neverborn</b> are the dead titans; they can\u2019t really do much, as dead gods experiencing constant agony.<br /> <br /> The<b> Deathlords </b>are the restless ghosts of Exalted killed around the Usurpation, peerless necromancers who rule patches of the Underworld. They are more powerful than bog standard ghosts, even the ghosts of Exalts, but how exactly they came to that power hasn\u2019t been rigorously explained in this edition (nor do I think it should be).<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">In previous editions, they were <i>given</i> power by the Neverborn in exchange for serving the Neverborn\u2019s desire to destroy Creation, but this time around it could very well be that they stole said power with unknown rituals, or were imbued with it with no conditions by desperate dead titans, or maybe traded strange and terrible things for their unusual potency. Maybe different ones seized their power in different ways; maybe there\u2019s still some to be seized yet, for one who would seek it.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Deathlords corrupted some of the divine fire that fills the Sun\u2019s Chosen, giving rise to the <b>Abyssal Exalted</b>, to whom the Deathlords serve as mentors, vassals, and benefactors.<br /> <br /> Let me provide an example from what I played in 2e that I feel will need only minimal adjustment for Ex3: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I once played an Abyssal called <b>Son-of-Void Dragon</b>. He was once a mortal prince and a warlord whose enemies received aid from beyond the grave, allowing them to capture him and sentence him to a death by beheading.<br /> <br /> As the headman\u2019s blade descended, the prince defiantly raised his eyes to meet the gaze of each of his enemies, when he saw a figure among them that hadn\u2019t been there a moment ago, a ghostly giant wearing a mask of ice. Time itself seemed to freeze as <b>the Mask of Winters</b> judged him. The prince felt a splinter of cold on the back of his neck - was it the bite of steel, or the ghost-king\u2019s touch?<br /> <br /> \u201cI can grant you the power to take glorious, terrible vengeance on your betrayers, if you will serve me after.\u201d<br /> <br /> The prince said no word, but his decision was made. The blade sliced cleanly through his neck, but the parted flesh had come together again, cleanly, leaving no scar.<br /> <br /> The headman tried to yank his blade free, but the prisoner had seized the sword in his teeth! Surging with power, he bit down, and shattered it to pieces, bits of steel tumbling from his new fangs.<br /> <br /> Standing, he snapped his bindings as though they were forged of paper, and turned on his enemies, tearing men and spirits alike to pieces with his bare hands, until only he and the Deathlord remained. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-30-2019, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T06:57:18-08:00","id":1351854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1351845#post1351845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, Neverborn giving commands? What are they like? Remember, these are huge titan things, dreaming and dying, yet living on at the same time, filled to the brim with insanity-destroying nightmares.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whispers Background. In the scenario I presented each Abyssal will get one free dot in the Whispers Background (whether they want it or not).<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1351849#post1351849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really prefer your idea. There are neverborn, which are dead titans, and Abyssal descends directly from the neverborn. Deathlords obeys the neverborn (or not), but are just powerful ghost ennemies. Much clearer to me..</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. The whole &quot;Deathlords are titanic entities of the Underworld&quot; idea has felt always felt contrived to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800080\">I express my opinions, but YSMV; Your Stories May Vary.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Formerly known as wyrmpuff</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12288-mal-akh","name":"Mal'akh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12288_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T07:07:07-08:00","id":1351855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal'akh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1351842#post1351842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if... You downgrade the Deathlords to powerful ghosts who have Underworld domains and replace the incursions into Creation by the Abyssals under the direct command of the Neverborn?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing <i>breaks</i>, but it <i>does</i> force more of the game\u2019s spotlight into the hands of titans defeated before the dawn of history, which is a little less interesting to me than other alternatives. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s the same reason I prefer to see new demons over seeing new Yozis, and the reason I was disappointed that Rick Riordan\u2019s books kept ushering in titanomachies, instead of actually exploring a world like ours with demigods and monsters running around behind the scenes.<br /> <br /> (Especially since there\u2019s very little character-wise for the Neverborn as-written.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-30-2019, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T07:45:52-08:00","id":1351860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1351855#post1351855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing <i>breaks</i>, but it <i>does</i> force more of the game\u2019s spotlight into the hands of titans defeated before the dawn of history, which is a little less interesting to me than other alternatives.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s the same reason I prefer to see new demons over seeing new Yozis, and the reason I was disappointed that Rick Riordan\u2019s books kept ushering in titanomachies, instead of actually exploring a world like ours with demigods and monsters running around behind the scenes.<br /> <br /> (Especially since there\u2019s very little character-wise for the Neverborn as-written.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'm not a fan of the Deathlord corrupting the Souls of the Solar Exalted, because it makes me feel like a very active agent that holds the power of Exaltation is not a theme I find anywhere else in the books. If the Neverborn are the direct creators of the Abyssals I'm rather fine : Very mysterious and dead whispering guys give Exaltation to edgy people. If Mast of Winters is giving Exaltations, I'm feeling uncomfortable with the idea : The guy has armies, lands, direct temporal power, a calendar of invasion, and he can chose Exalted. It doesn't feel the same at all than Luna (that goes to her Chosen but does not act herself on Creation, from what I understood) or Exigents (That are begging for Exaltation).<br /> <br /> Maybe it's on purpose, but without clearer explanation of the theme that is conveyed here I feel this makes for a demystification of Exaltation (Again, the only thing I read is the part about Mask of Winter and underworld in the core book and it got me confused maybe I'm all wrong).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T08:16:54-08:00","id":1351867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal'akh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1351842#post1351842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if... You downgrade the Deathlords to powerful ghosts who have Underworld domains and replace the incursions into Creation by the Abyssals under the direct command of the Neverborn?</div> </div> </div> </div>Running the Neverborn as the main antagonists can have a significant impact on the tone of a chronicle. Without further lore changes, they're not really an enemy you can really defeat only desperately push back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T08:21:54-08:00","id":1351868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1351867#post1351867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Running the Neverborn as the main antagonists can have a significant impact on the tone of a chronicle. Without further lore changes, they're not really an enemy you can really defeat only desperately push back.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think my point (and also of Mal'Akh, but I can't speak for him) is that we should use the Abyssals as the main antagonists, and they draw strength and untold powers from the whispers of the Neverborn. At least, that's how I did it in my first campaign (There was a big imprisoned and dead Neverborn, and the players were countering the plans of the abyssals that tried to free him), and that felt much more natural to me than to have the intermediary Deathlord whom (Is that how I should use &quot;whom&quot; ?) I don't really understand the place in the dynamic of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T08:45:07-08:00","id":1351873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1351868#post1351868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Is that how I should use &quot;whom&quot; ?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Protip: If you replace the word with &quot;him&quot; and it still reads the right way, you're using &quot;whom&quot; correctly. If it'd sound better as &quot;he,&quot; then this becomes a job for &quot;who.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T09:05:02-08:00","id":1351877,"title":"","content":"Guess I misused it then <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T16:30:01-08:00","id":1351932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Running the Neverborn as the main antagonists can have a significant impact on the tone of a chronicle. Without further lore changes, they're not really an enemy you can really defeat only desperately push back.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think my point (and also of Mal'Akh, but I can't speak for him) is that we should use the Abyssals as the main antagonists,...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's as Chausse said, replace the Deathlords with the Abyssals. The Deathlords as powerful ghosts could still have ignited the Great Contagion and the Balorian Crusade and replacing the Mask of Winters with a circle of Abyssals is a straightforward exchange.<br /> <br /> Yes, it would have a significant impact on the tone of a chronicle as PCs would be confronted with active and powerful foes that are stronger than the Bull of the North.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800080\">I express my opinions, but YSMV; Your Stories May Vary.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Formerly known as wyrmpuff</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12288-mal-akh","name":"Mal'akh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12288_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T01:14:26-08:00","id":1351979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal'akh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1351932#post1351932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> It's as Chausse said, replace the Deathlords with the Abyssals. The Deathlords as powerful ghosts could still have ignited the Great Contagion and the Balorian Crusade and replacing the Mask of Winters with a circle of Abyssals is a straightforward exchange.<br /> <br /> Yes, it would have a significant impact on the tone of a chronicle as PCs would be confronted with active and powerful foes that are stronger than the Bull of the North.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I like with this version is I can still see a use for the Deathlords as sort of Avatars of the Neverborn, beings in deep slumber or something like that where the objective of a campaign is to stop their awakening for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T03:25:19-08:00","id":1351988,"title":"","content":"So... nothing breaks? Just some juggling around? Because I have another 'What breaks if...'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800080\">I express my opinions, but YSMV; Your Stories May Vary.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Formerly known as wyrmpuff</i></span>","edited":{"userid":12288,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12288-mal-akh","user":"Mal'akh","date":". 12-01-2019, 06:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12288-mal-akh","name":"Mal'akh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12288_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T06:04:41-08:00","id":1352001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal'akh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1351988#post1351988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... nothing breaks? Just some juggling around? Because I have another 'What breaks if...'</div> </div> </div> </div>Personnally I think it's fine but I'm not a psychic maybe there are some future materials that will come pose problem with this interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T06:05:15-08:00","id":1352002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1351877#post1351877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guess I misused it then <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No that's correct. I don't think the him/he substitution is a great rule of thumb (I see why it's suggested but you have to reconstruct the sentence to &quot;I don't understand [him/he]&quot; -- you'd use &quot;him&quot; thus &quot;whom&quot; is correct. But if you reconstruct the sentence you could end up changing the voice &quot;[Him/he] is not understood by me&quot;, and that could be misleasing). Who acts upon whom? You don't understand whom. Who doesn't understand you.<br /> <br /> I prefer the Neverborn dead not sleeping, but it'd be a cool twist that doesn't really break the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-01-2019, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T06:10:56-08:00","id":1352004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1352002#post1352002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No that's correct. I don't think the him/he substitution is a great rule of thumb (I see why it's suggested but you have to reconstruct the sentence to &quot;I don't understand [him/he]&quot; -- you'd use &quot;him&quot; thus &quot;whom&quot; is correct).<br /> <br /> I prefer the Neverborn dead not sleeping, but it'd be a cool twist that doesn't really break the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh okay thanks yeah reconstructing the sentence backwards make sense.<br /> <br /> I think the Neverborn are dead but the thing is usually in WW settings and the kind of fantasy setting Exalted is, &quot;dead&quot; doesn't mean &quot;it's dead and you can't interact with it&quot;, but more like &quot;it's dead but it still does stuff just in some sort of twisted dead manner&quot;. At least that's how I interpret the fact that the Neverborn gave power to the Deathlords and so on ...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T08:15:42-08:00","id":1352012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal'akh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1351988#post1351988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... nothing breaks? Just some juggling around? Because I have another 'What breaks if...'</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably won't hurt.<br /> I'd advise caution that circles vs. circles tend to favour the player characters for the simple fact that they each have one character sheet to keep track of while you have several. What's a challenging encounter on paper might not work in practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T08:56:37-08:00","id":1352015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1352004#post1352004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Neverborn are dead but the thing is usually in WW settings and the kind of fantasy setting Exalted is, &quot;dead&quot; doesn't mean &quot;it's dead and you can't interact with it&quot;, but more like &quot;it's dead but it still does stuff just in some sort of twisted dead manner&quot;. At least that's how I interpret the fact that the Neverborn gave power to the Deathlords and so on ...</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;In his house at R'lyeh dead Cthulhu waits, dreaming.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T22:10:50-08:00","id":1352104,"title":"","content":"What breaks if... The Yozis had nothing to do with the release and corruption of the Solars? Instead the whole project was dreamed up by the Neverborn with the help of the Deathlords. No Green Sun Princes at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800080\">I express my opinions, but YSMV; Your Stories May Vary.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Formerly known as wyrmpuff</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12288-mal-akh","name":"Mal'akh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12288_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T23:27:41-08:00","id":1352108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal'akh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1352104#post1352104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if... The Yozis had nothing to do with the release and corruption of the Solars? Instead the whole project was dreamed up by the Neverborn with the help of the Deathlords. No Green Sun Princes at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well obviously you'd be dealing with no Infernals, or you'd need another explanation on where they came from if you did include them later. But, that's an obvious one and pretty easy and seems one you're aiming for.<br /> <br /> The big alterations would be the potential for a higher count of Abyssals and Solars. If the Yozi weren't involved then the Neverborn and their champions would be allowed to keep whatever the heck they got out of breaking the prison, so if we went with the 2e counts then there's anywhere between 0-50 more abyssals in the setting with the remainder becoming Solars. Which only impacts the game if you feel the need to map out how many of those factions are in play at any given time.<br /> <br /> Really the biggest thing would be needing to explain how the Neverborn and Deathlords managed to find the Jade Prison, since in 2e Ebby contributed the location and some information on how it worked. In your iteration all of this would have been done using the forces of the Underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T00:45:46-08:00","id":1352117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really the biggest thing would be needing to explain how the Neverborn and Deathlords managed to find the Jade Prison, since in 2e Ebby contributed the location and some information on how it worked. In your iteration all of this would have been done using the forces of the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's easy. Sidereals die, even those who were part of the planning committee for the Jade Prison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800080\">I express my opinions, but YSMV; Your Stories May Vary.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Formerly known as wyrmpuff</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12288-mal-akh","name":"Mal'akh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12288_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T04:56:39-08:00","id":1352141,"title":"","content":"Is there even a Jade Prison in 3e ? I think I read that somewhere but I can't remember where.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T08:18:34-08:00","id":1352168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1352141#post1352141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there even a Jade Prison in 3e ? I think I read that somewhere but I can't remember where.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s mentioned in the ex3 corebook but there\u2019s also implication that other things have changed as well, the unconquered sun is now paying more attention to Creation again, Exigents are on the rise, stuff like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T08:40:16-08:00","id":1352169,"title":"","content":"Ok I see thanks for your light","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T12:43:13-08:00","id":1352201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal'akh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1352117#post1352117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's easy. Sidereals die, even those who were part of the planning committee for the Jade Prison.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, you'd potentially need to come up with the explanations for how it was found and analyzed for breaking and capture and that's pretty much it. There's some indication that the Jade Prison has changed from how it functioned in 2e, but nothing concrete has been stated on it. Of course most of the time this isn't going to matter beyond an explanation for more Abyssals and Solars and answering the how's at the beginning of the chronicle when you go, &quot;Right, there aren't going to be any Infernals in this chronicle. They don't exist, Neverborne and the Deathlords managed to do all the work this time,&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T16:25:02-08:00","id":1352467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly, you'd potentially need to come up with the explanations for how it was found and analyzed for breaking and capture and that's pretty much it. There's some indication that the Jade Prison has changed from how it functioned in 2e, but nothing concrete has been stated on it. Of course most of the time this isn't going to matter beyond an explanation for more Abyssals and Solars and answering the how's at the beginning of the chronicle when you go, &quot;Right, there aren't going to be any Infernals in this chronicle. They don't exist, Neverborne and the Deathlords managed to do all the work this time,&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You just need the rationale for internal (read: Storyteller) continuity. You don't even have to tell the players any of it aside from 'There are no Infernals in this game.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800080\">I express my opinions, but YSMV; Your Stories May Vary.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Formerly known as wyrmpuff</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12288-mal-akh","name":"Mal'akh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12288_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T20:21:27-08:00","id":1353230,"title":"","content":"Okay, the last two ones I posted seems to not break anything. This one has, in my opinion, a much bigger impact and has a significant chance of breakage.<br /> <br /> <b>What breaks if... The Loom of Fate only regulates causality and not destiny?</b><br /> <br /> The Five Maidens and their Chosen are there to ensure the proper flow of causality; water flows down and not up, all that are born die, etc. Large Essence expenditure and actions of creatures outside Fate causes the fabric of Creation to form creases, snarls and tears. These are what the Sidereals are meant to troubleshoot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800080\">I express my opinions, but YSMV; Your Stories May Vary.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Formerly known as wyrmpuff</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12288-mal-akh","name":"Mal'akh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12288_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T22:19:00-08:00","id":1353251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal'akh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1353230#post1353230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, the last two ones I posted seems to not break anything. This one has, in my opinion, a much bigger impact and has a significant chance of breakage.<br /> <br /> <b>What breaks if... The Loom of Fate only regulates causality and not destiny?</b><br /> <br /> The Five Maidens and their Chosen are there to ensure the proper flow of causality; water flows down and not up, all that are born die, etc. Large Essence expenditure and actions of creatures outside Fate causes the fabric of Creation to form creases, snarls and tears. These are what the Sidereals are meant to troubleshoot.</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire theme of Astrology, which permeates all things Sidereal, breaks. Why are a bunch of planet Incarnae in charge of physics? Why do Sids have stars in their eyes? What happens to all the Sid Charms based on Destiny and Astrology? Why do Getimians even exist?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T01:26:50-08:00","id":1353282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The entire theme of Astrology, which permeates all things Sidereal, breaks. Why are a bunch of planet Incarnae in charge of physics? Why do Sids have stars in their eyes? What happens to all the Sid Charms based on Destiny and Astrology? Why do Getimians even exist?</div> </div> </div> </div><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Astrology would be the tools that Sidereals are equipped with to smooth out what has disrupted the fabric of Creation by moving &quot;threads&quot; around and reinforcing the damaged areas.</li> <li>Aside from the fact that Creation does not have physics as we know the term. the Five Maidens were needed because the <i>Primordials</i> were outside Fate.</li> <li>They are still Chosen of the Maidens</li> <li>The Destiny Charms will probably become a casualty while Astrology Charms will stay the same.</li> <li>Getimians won't exist in my game in any case.</li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800080\">I express my opinions, but YSMV; Your Stories May Vary.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Formerly known as wyrmpuff</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12288-mal-akh","name":"Mal'akh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12288_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T04:22:12-08:00","id":1353313,"title":"","content":"I feel like this has been asked, but... what breaks if you don't re-order actions every round, and stick to (say) going clockwise around the table? ie, Joey goes third regardless if he has Ini 20 or 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T05:25:35-08:00","id":1353320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1353313#post1353313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this has been asked, but... what breaks if you don't re-order actions every round, and stick to (say) going clockwise around the table? ie, Joey goes third regardless if he has Ini 20 or 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Decisive attacks are a bit safer, since you don't fall back in the initiative order, and in general you don't get the extremes when someone rises or falls in initiative and then goes very soon/very late.<br /> Turn-Order-Manipulation charms have to be reworked.<br /> Clashes don't happen naturally.<br /> Turn order becomes consistent in a fight, which might make things like using a charm that does something to the next attack against a target more predictable, or make a certain character always the one in a position to take advantage of an enemy's onslaught penalty. When generals go relative to their army can matter, and here it will be unchanging within a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T16:34:34-08:00","id":1354939,"title":"","content":"... If a successful attack against a battle group grants initiative equal to its size?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T16:37:16-08:00","id":1354940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1354939#post1354939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... If a successful attack against a battle group grants initiative equal to its size?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only withering or all attacks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T17:21:23-08:00","id":1354943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1354939#post1354939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... If a successful attack against a battle group grants initiative equal to its size?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fighting a large battlegroup becomes easier, since you're regaining initiative faster, and initiative determines how long it takes to kill you.<br /> <br /> When fighting a battlegroup alongside exalted or similarly powerful entities, it becomes more initiative-profitable to attack the battlegroup. Given that battlegroups don't generally have defensive excellencies and charms (or any excellencies and charms), this risks making the battlegroup too easily the focus of attention, especially since a battlegroup's attacks are generally stronger than its defense (orders and multi-target attacks don't really have a defensive equivalent)<br /> <br /> Enfolded in the Dragon's Wings becomes a bit stronger, since it's potentially denying your enemies more initiative.<br /> <br /> If this includes successful decisive attacks, then it becomes harder to take advantage of the reset to crash someone, and more often the case that a decisive increases your initiative, which is weird. (This can happen in normal cases, but only if you make 1 or 2 initiative decisives)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T22:43:25-08:00","id":1359653,"title":"","content":"What breaks if I tie combat more regen to anima levels? Like say at the end of each round an exalt regains a number of motes equal to their current anima level? Or maybe anima+1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T23:10:07-08:00","id":1359656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1359653#post1359653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I tie combat more regen to anima levels? Like say at the end of each round an exalt regains a number of motes equal to their current anima level? Or maybe anima+1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Players are going to lean towards all-in win now maneuvers like TAP-HSF because it's near impossible to sustain a fight without flaring. <br /> You also set up a really nasty trap where if somebody ends a fight low on motes but has time to work off their anima, they might enter the next fight low on motes and unable to spend enough to unlock better mote regen in time. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T23:10:14-08:00","id":1359657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1359653#post1359653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I tie combat more regen to anima levels? Like say at the end of each round an exalt regains a number of motes equal to their current anima level? Or maybe anima+1.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only unexpected side effect I can think of is that it might punish builds that rely on expending anima levels, such as the sort of shenanigans DBs do to avoid getting locked in their Aspect Aura.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T10:20:02-08:00","id":1360156,"title":"","content":"In regards to the ongoing discussion on the topic E10 Solar Charm (PEACH), I have a question : What breaks if Solars do not have a Supernal ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T10:40:08-08:00","id":1360159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1360156#post1360156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to the ongoing discussion on the topic E10 Solar Charm (PEACH), I have a question : What breaks if Solars do not have a Supernal ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think anything <i>breaks</i>, per se. The Solars will definitely look less hyper-competent right out of the gate, but the antagonists in the core book will largely still be defeatable by a prepared group, I think. A hypothetical Third Circle demon or equivalently powerful being might be out of reach of Essence 1 or 2 Solars, though. That might be the most significant &quot;breakage&quot;, actually - it probably will no longer be plausible that the Exalted were able to defeat the primordials right out of the gate, and instead would have had to cultivate their Essence for a while before becoming powerful enough to take them on. Whether you find that scenario plausible or not depends on a lot of factors.<br /> <br /> Personally, if you're dissatisfied with how much Supernal allows Solars to &quot;cap break&quot;, rather than removing it entirely, I'd suggest that it allows them to take charms 2 Essence levels higher than they otherwise could. That means that they could get Essence 3 charms at character creation, just not Essence 5. Essence 2 and 3 Solar charms are generally focuses on specific tricks and tactics, so Essence +2 would allow those without getting into the &quot;feats of incredible power&quot; that Essence 4-5 charms tend to represent. And allowing <i>some</i> cap-breaking means that Solars will get to experience the heights of their charmset in a bit less time, compared to having to wait until their Essence develops all the way to 5 just based on XP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T11:00:23-08:00","id":1360163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1360156#post1360156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to the ongoing discussion on the topic E10 Solar Charm (PEACH), I have a question : What breaks if Solars do not have a Supernal ?</div> </div> </div> </div>As I wrote in that thread, we houseruled supernal to allow you only to choose charms one Essence higher than normally. We are 14 sessions into the campaign and it works fine. This means that you reach Essence 3, where the most juicy charms are, after 10 sessions. This was an extremely satisfying moment.<br /> <br /> Possibly, it's not the best idea if you are realistically planning only a short campaign. My current group is extremely commited, but typically it's hard for me to have even a five-session campaign. Then I would think twice whether I want to get rid of the supernal, since that can mean that we won't ever see half of the charms used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T11:13:58-08:00","id":1360168,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't discard it completely, if only because there are a lot of shticks that really only kick in at Essence 2. A variant I've considered is &quot;your Essence is treated as 1-2 higher for ALL purposes,&quot; so that it's more of a trade-off. (And more relevant at higher Essence levels)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T11:16:06-08:00","id":1360169,"title":"","content":"Thank you both, I like your suggestions.<br /> <br /> I think I prefer the idea to allow to take Charm at Essence+1 rather than Essence+2, because I rarely see people taking Essence 4 Charms at creation anyway, people usually stop at Essence 3. I was also thinking that in a game with very few players (1 or 2) it would encourage them to broaden their capabilities and offer more diverse experience from each character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T16:22:16-08:00","id":1360222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1360159#post1360159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it probably will no longer be plausible that the Exalted were able to defeat the primordials right out of the gate...</div> </div> </div> </div>1) I don't think the Exalted <i>did</i> defeat the Primordials &quot;right out of the gate,&quot; so their ability to do so is probably moot. My understanding is that the conflict took years or decades, and spanned across Creation in its size and scope.<br /> <br /> \u200b2) Even if that weren't true, the Exalted host is made up of far more than just Solars.<br /> <br /> 3) Even if that weren't true, Ghost-Eating Technique is an Essence 1 Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T16:55:53-08:00","id":1360227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1360156#post1360156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to the ongoing discussion on the topic E10 Solar Charm (PEACH), I have a question : What breaks if Solars do not have a Supernal ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've asked a similar question on discord chat myself, but I think the more interesting question would become. &quot;What replaces the Supernal ability?&quot;<br /> <br /> Because Supernal is a pretty big part of their tool kit in 3rd addition, it'd be like taking out Lunars transformation rules. So I think something then should replace it.<br /> <br /> Perhaps a few (two) options.<br /> <br /> -A free excellency and different excellency for each essence level, like essence one would be the normal excellency, but essence 2 would by the 'can apply successes to a completed roll for two motes per success, with either essence 4 or 5 being the spend a willpower for a full excellency.<br /> <br /> -Greatly enhance the anima powers of the caste abilities or add other powerful abilities?<br /> <br /> - Something else that I can't think of at the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":14713,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14713-chronos12","user":"Chronos12","date":". 01-10-2020, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14713-chronos12","name":"Chronos12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14713_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T07:27:08-08:00","id":1361457,"title":"","content":"What breaks if I allow decisive attacks to be made I using less than full Initiative, as opposed to always go all-in, as per the current rules? This one bit of rules always strikes me as rather odd. I understand that we lose some of the usual cinematic feel of current decisive, but it sees to me to automatically increase tactical depth of the combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T07:45:38-08:00","id":1361465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1361457#post1361457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I allow decisive attacks to be made I using less than full Initiative, as opposed to always go all-in, as per the current rules? This one bit of rules always strikes me as rather odd. I understand that we lose some of the usual cinematic feel of current decisive, but it sees to me to automatically increase tactical depth of the combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes combat less dangerous for characters with good withering attacks. Normally they have to make themselves vulnerable to being crashed after a decisive, but if they could just use 15 of their 30 initiative that doesn\u2019t put them in that position. <br /> <br /> The only thing it kind of breaks is the Initiative Shift balancing farming initiative off one target and using it on another. Normally that\u2019s an incredibly dangerous thing to do because if you crash enemy A and decisive enemy B then enemy A has a great opportunity to shift on you. What you want to do is crash A and then kill A.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not really broken but it makes the combats a lot more safe with less ability to swing back one way or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T08:00:14-08:00","id":1361469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1361457#post1361457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks if I allow decisive attacks to be made I using less than full Initiative, as opposed to always go all-in, as per the current rules? This one bit of rules always strikes me as rather odd. I understand that we lose some of the usual cinematic feel of current decisive, but it sees to me to automatically increase tactical depth of the combat.</div> </div> </div> </div> Why would you <i>want </i>to roll less than full Initiative worth of damage?<br /> <br /> Or rather, how do you plan on handling &quot;Reset to Base Value&quot; step, where after a successful attack, the attacker's initiative is simply <b>reset to 3</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T08:21:39-08:00","id":1361474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1361469#post1361469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Why would you <i>want </i>to roll less than full Initiative worth of damage?<br /> <br /> Or rather, how do you plan on handling &quot;Reset to Base Value&quot; step, where after a successful attack, the attacker's initiative is simply <b>reset to 3</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I probably wasn't clear enough. I meant that upon successful attack, you would loose only the Initiative you actually used (say, +1, to stay coherent with the rules for Gambits). Under the current rules, you essentially have to &quot;pay&quot; with your full Initiative in order to attack, which gets refunded if the attack happens to fail.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a> I mean, the intent was for a high Initiative advantage to be in more stable position. Currently, high Initiative opponents don't quite feel to me as if they has upper hand, but rather like a ticking bomb. But that's a good point that this forces you to pay your attention to all opponents.<br /> <br /> Let's muse with the idea a bit more. How about making &quot;cautious attacks&quot; more punitive. Say, you loose the invested initiative no matter the outcome of the attack unless you go &quot;all-in&quot; as per current rules? This would give some incentive to actually not play in an overly cautious way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T09:03:35-08:00","id":1361487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1360156#post1360156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to the ongoing discussion on the topic E10 Solar Charm (PEACH), I have a question : What breaks if Solars do not have a Supernal ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Potentially returning to the problems that Dawn Castes had in previous editions, where if their player wasn't a combat monkey it was easy to be overshadowed by concepts such as Night Caste assassins and Zenith Caste warrior priests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T09:43:44-08:00","id":1361504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic;n1361474[USER=&amp;quot;1121&amp;quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">DrLoveMonkey[/USER] I mean, the intent was for a high Initiative advantage to be in more stable position. Currently, high Initiative opponents don't quite feel to me as if they has upper hand, but rather like a ticking bomb. But that's a good point that this forces you to pay your attention to all opponents.<br /> <br /> Let's muse with the idea a bit more. How about making &amp;quot;cautious attacks&amp;quot; more punitive. Say, you loose the invested initiative no matter the outcome of the attack unless you go &amp;quot;all-in&amp;quot; as per current rules? This would give some incentive to actually not play in an overly cautious way.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could be better. You\u2019ll also have to watch because some powerful enemies already have mechanics in place to mitigate their risk of resetting to base, or allowing them to get around it and that might cause some odd interactions.<br /> <br /> Fakharu, for example, can decisive attack 3 times before he resets to base and a big AoE poison effect that deals lethal damage. Octavian can make a decisive attack and then follow up immediately with a withering to get back to safe initiative, and has a simple charm that deals decisive damage but doesn\u2019t cost initiative or reset him to base. Alhat has a charm that based on the damage roll adds bonus initiative to his reset. Mahicara has a big AoE charm that deals 6L/round and doesn\u2019t reset to base.<br /> <br /> Not all of those would interact too badly with cautious attacks, but some like Fakharu or Octavian could skew things a bit, although I don\u2019t think to the point of breaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T11:18:52-08:00","id":1361528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1361487#post1361487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Potentially returning to the problems that Dawn Castes had in previous editions, where if their player wasn't a combat monkey it was easy to be overshadowed by concepts such as Night Caste assassins and Zenith Caste warrior priests.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it really though ? With the Caste Abilities I think any Dawn can be as interesting as any other Caste character without being a fighting minimaxer.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T12:20:45-08:00","id":1361539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1361528#post1361528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does it really though ? With the Caste Abilities I think any Dawn can be as interesting as any other Caste character without being a fighting minimaxer.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's more that if someone else minmaxes well then the Dawn Caste's fighting ability can feel like an informed attribute. If the Night is an equally talented sword fighter but they can also ninja vanish and backstab people then the Dawn player might feel that their character sucks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T12:46:39-08:00","id":1361544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1361528#post1361528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does it really though ? With the Caste Abilities I think any Dawn can be as interesting as any other Caste character without being a fighting minimaxer.</div> </div> </div> </div>It absolutely does. Note that &quot;overshadowed&quot; and &quot;not interesting&quot; are completely different things. <br /> Even something as simple as the Dawn taking not-Melee while the Night takes Melee at a bit higher investment is all you need for the Dawn to be second-string in their own field of expertise. <br /> One big problem is that the quantity of Caste Abilities and Favored Abilities are equal, so you can have two completely identical Ability/Charm listings. There's absolutely no niche protection aside from Supernal. And combat is something many characters invest into, making it very prone to nichebumping. <br /> Or if you meant Anima Banner abilities, those vary wildly. In a campaign about fighting CoDs and strongarming people, the Zenith outfights the Dawn and the Dawn outsocials the Zenith!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T13:22:23-08:00","id":1361551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1361544#post1361544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It absolutely does. Note that &quot;overshadowed&quot; and &quot;not interesting&quot; are completely different things.<br /> Even something as simple as the Dawn taking not-Melee while the Night takes Melee at a bit higher investment is all you need for the Dawn to be second-string in their own field of expertise.<br /> One big problem is that the quantity of Caste Abilities and Favored Abilities are equal, so you can have two completely identical Ability/Charm listings. There's absolutely no niche protection aside from Supernal. And combat is something many characters invest into, making it very prone to nichebumping.<br /> Or if you meant Anima Banner abilities, those vary wildly. In a campaign about fighting CoDs and strongarming people, the Zenith outfights the Dawn and the Dawn outsocials the Zenith!</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it really, though? Ditching the Supernal-Caste association breaks the stereotypical roles even more than Favored Abilities do, but that's not necessarily a bad thing-- it just means that you're good at the things you want to be good at.<br /> <br /> (Though you might have to be careful of Anima Banner abilities, as you note)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T13:44:36-08:00","id":1361556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1361539#post1361539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's more that if someone else minmaxes well then the Dawn Caste's fighting ability can feel like an informed attribute. If the Night is an equally talented sword fighter but they can also ninja vanish and backstab people then the Dawn player might feel that their character sucks.</div> </div> </div> </div>As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12314_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12314\" data-vbnamecard=\"12314\">Grod_the_giant</a> noted, when Supernals are gone, the Dawn can go on the field of other Castes and do stuff, because they are only Solar 1 Excellent at these things.<br /> <br /> The only specific Caste ability that seem so overwhelming to me that nothing can replace it from another Caste point of view and be core to a character concept would be the Night Caste ability to not flare when spending motes. The rest, while cool, never happened to be &quot;indispensable&quot; to a character concept. They happened to be cool, but never indispensable.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25764\" data-vbnamecard=\"25764\">vwllss trnt prncss</a> I guess the repartition of Caste abilities plays a little bit against the Dawn, but I find Exalted characters are more easily overshadowed by other characters because other characters are more ambitious (and their players are more say &quot;expensive&quot;) than their direct &quot;set of skills&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T14:04:27-08:00","id":1361565,"title":"","content":"Fine if everyone's equally aware of what the Solar charmset can do, I used the Night Caste as an example because Blinding Battle Feint is a formidable join battle charm in the Steath tree.<br /> <br /> Yes, the Dawn Caste could get it if they really want it but that's where the expectation on the player to make their character &quot;properly&quot; increases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T14:18:56-08:00","id":1361569,"title":"","content":"It kinda feels like a crutch though if you have to keep a splat-wide effect to fix a Caste-specific issue. As an alternative, Dawns could simply have a Caste Power that considers them 1 Essence higher when buying Charms from the 5 Combat abilities (Archery, Brawl, Martial Arts, Melee, Thrown), that would be sufficient to solve the &quot;Dawns aren't the most fighty&quot; issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T15:02:58-08:00","id":1361578,"title":"","content":"If supernals are gone then Dawn are even worse because Twilights have snap on Instant Armor. It cripples Dawn to not control the fighting part of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T15:03:39-08:00","id":1361579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1361556#post1361556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12314_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12314\" data-vbnamecard=\"12314\">Grod_the_giant</a> noted, when Supernals are gone, the Dawn can go on the field of other Castes and do stuff, because they are only Solar 1 Excellent at these things.<br /> <br /> The only specific Caste ability that seem so overwhelming to me that nothing can replace it from another Caste point of view and be core to a character concept would be the Night Caste ability to not flare when spending motes. The rest, while cool, never happened to be &quot;indispensable&quot; to a character concept. They happened to be cool, but never indispensable.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25764\" data-vbnamecard=\"25764\">vwllss trnt prncss</a> I guess the repartition of Caste abilities plays a little bit against the Dawn, but I find Exalted characters are more easily overshadowed by other characters because other characters are more ambitious (and their players are more say &quot;expensive&quot;) than their direct &quot;set of skills&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To me, definitely the most powerful (and flavourful) are Eclipse abilities..Diplomatic immunity and sanctifying oaths seem both examples of something that could be high-Essence charms. They are applicable in so many circumstances and guarantee that you essentially always get a chance to try getting things done in a diplomatic way.<br /> <br /> I donl't think there is particular risk of overshadowing Dawns in 3rd edition to be honest. Their caste abilities are solid and, contrary to the second edition, there is no particular reason <i>not </i> to choose Dawn if you want to focus on martial prowess. If you remove Supernal, it is not an overwhelming advantage, but they are still the best in fighting. So whoever wants to focus on combat, will probably choose Dawn anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 01-17-2020, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T15:15:37-08:00","id":1361580,"title":"","content":"Honestly the issue I have with the ideal so far is as I've mentioned before it is a pretty massive hit to their power and there doesn't seem to be any replacing major power for the solar's for it's loss save for some. There is a reason I compared it to Lunar's losing their shape shifting powers. Considering it's easy flight,water-breathing, disguises, and even combat, it's pretty comparable in the 'destroys early stories.<br /> <br /> Grod has suggested one replacement that isn't too bad, and I think it would mostly work as either &quot;Essence is treated as two higher for the supernal ability in every way.&quot; or at least &quot;All Caste abilities are treated as one essence higher.<br /> <br /> The other reason I'm against the ideal is that Supernal is a very FUN mechanic for Solar's since it gives players the ability to go into the very interesting and fun charms. They may go for overwhelming ability or they may like me want to grab an early utility charm that expresses the character's desires. I find that the disappointment that the other splats didn't also get supernal rather telling when WFHW came out rather telling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14713-chronos12","name":"Chronos12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14713_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T16:02:03-08:00","id":1361594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1361551#post1361551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it really, though? Ditching the Supernal-Caste association breaks the stereotypical roles even more than Favored Abilities do, but that's not necessarily a bad thing-- it just means that you're good at the things you want to be good at.<br /> <br /> (Though you might have to be careful of Anima Banner abilities, as you note)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it <b>absolutely does</b>. <br /> It is very easy for differences in Charm choice to de-Dawn the Dawn. And when you take away Supernal, all that's really diversifying characters is Charm choice. <br /> Danny Dawn throws 6 picks into combat and diversifies into other people's niches, Nancy Night goes all-in assassin with 9 combat Charms. Whoops, Nancy's deadlier than Danny. Or whoops, Nancy picked good charms while Danny didn't. Or whoops, Danny picked a diverse spread of combat charms while Nancy went for a focused set of combat charms. <br /> I'm not even theorycrafting here, that last one happened in my game despite the Dawn being Melee Supernal. Both the Zenith and the Night were better fighters than the Dawn because the Dawn's 14 combat Charms had near-zero synergy. This wasn't a problem in my game solely because the Dawn's player has uh, zero mechanical awareness to put it tactfully, and didn't ever realize that his character was underperforming. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T17:18:54-08:00","id":1361612,"title":"","content":"I'm kinda bothered by this discussion because when I wanted to propose this houserule for my future games it was really not oriented towards the Dawn that go full fight (in my games there are fights but most players don't care to have 25 insta kill Charms shenanigans so they don't go there) but rather to avoid the 10 starting bureaucracy/craft/performance/presence/whatever Charms of the usual Zenith/Twilight/Eclipse that usually put them way ahead of the Dawn in the story (and also make the campaign kinda monomaniac, &quot;when all you have is a hammer everything looks like a nail&quot;), yet everyone keeps talking about the &quot;poor Dawn&quot; while I never had any issue with a Dawn that was behind in any fight.<br /> <br /> I'm just looking for more versatile character and was wondering if removing (or reducing) supernal was a good alternative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":". 01-17-2020, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T17:27:43-08:00","id":1361614,"title":"","content":"There's nothing in the Solar Charmset that relies on an expectation that characters will have a Supernal. So no, removing Supernal doesn't break anything mechanically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T18:47:21-08:00","id":1361636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1361612#post1361612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just looking for more versatile character and was wondering if removing (or reducing) supernal was a good alternative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernal allows starting characters to have a &quot;niche&quot; ability so even if mechanically it breaks nothing it brings back the 2e spectre of imbalanced castes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800080\">I express my opinions, but YSMV; Your Stories May Vary.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Formerly known as wyrmpuff</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12288-mal-akh","name":"Mal'akh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12288_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T18:49:09-08:00","id":1361637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1361612#post1361612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kinda bothered by this discussion because when I wanted to propose this houserule for my future games it was really not oriented towards the Dawn that go full fight (in my games there are fights but most players don't care to have 25 insta kill Charms shenanigans so they don't go there) but rather to avoid the 10 starting bureaucracy/craft/performance/presence/whatever Charms of the usual Zenith/Twilight/Eclipse that usually put them way ahead of the Dawn in the story (and also make the campaign kinda monomaniac, &quot;when all you have is a hammer everything looks like a nail&quot;), yet everyone keeps talking about the &quot;poor Dawn&quot; while I never had any issue with a Dawn that was behind in any fight.<br /> <br /> I'm just looking for more versatile character and was wondering if removing (or reducing) supernal was a good alternative.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dawn is just a good example, since it really stands out when fighty-man is less fighty than sneaky-man or talky-man. The general point is pretty universally applicable to any Ability or theater of conflict. Danny Dawn buying 6 Presence charms and leveraging their Anima scary-di[c]e can cause the same issue if Zoey Zenith went for Double-9s with all the social Abilities. <br /> <i><b>If</b></i> everyone in your group knows what they're doing and communicates well during chargen to make sure no niches are infringed upon (or nobody cares about niche protection), not having Supernal should work fine. Heck, better than baseline from a GM perspective since you don't have to plan around E3-5 Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T01:59:58-08:00","id":1361689,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24291_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24291\" data-vbnamecard=\"24291\">Chausse</a> What I will write is borderline trivial, but keep in mind that what is a reasonable rule in rpg game is extremely group-dependent. I would houserule things one way or another depending on who I'm playing with (even before taking into considerations whether group is ok with the houserules).<br /> <br /> So, speaking from practical experience: in my group, nerfing supernal went just fine. We are very happy with the houserule, it was a good decision, and getting access to Essence 3 charms was an extremely satisfying moment for players. So this nerf is not broken in the sense that the game has perfect chance to remain absolutely functional and it did in my case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T03:32:59-08:00","id":1361702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1361612#post1361612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kinda bothered by this discussion because when I wanted to propose this houserule for my future games it was really not oriented towards the Dawn that go full fight (in my games there are fights but most players don't care to have 25 insta kill Charms shenanigans so they don't go there) but rather to avoid the 10 starting bureaucracy/craft/performance/presence/whatever Charms of the usual Zenith/Twilight/Eclipse that usually put them way ahead of the Dawn in the story (and also make the campaign kinda monomaniac, &quot;when all you have is a hammer everything looks like a nail&quot;), yet everyone keeps talking about the &quot;poor Dawn&quot; while I never had any issue with a Dawn that was behind in any fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry you feel that way. We're only capable of speaking in general terms and saying what could go wrong or drawing from our experiences of game groups that could be very different to yours.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, you know your group better than we know your group.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T04:39:28-08:00","id":1361706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1361594#post1361594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, it <b>absolutely does</b>.<br /> It is very easy for differences in Charm choice to de-Dawn the Dawn. And when you take away Supernal, all that's really diversifying characters is Charm choice.<br /> Danny Dawn throws 6 picks into combat and diversifies into other people's niches, Nancy Night goes all-in assassin with 9 combat Charms. Whoops, Nancy's deadlier than Danny. Or whoops, Nancy picked good charms while Danny didn't. Or whoops, Danny picked a diverse spread of combat charms while Nancy went for a focused set of combat charms.<br /> I'm not even theorycrafting here, that last one happened in my game despite the Dawn being Melee Supernal. Both the Zenith and the Night were better fighters than the Dawn because the Dawn's 14 combat Charms had near-zero synergy. This wasn't a problem in my game solely because the Dawn's player has uh, zero mechanical awareness to put it tactfully, and didn't ever realize that his character was underperforming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it means that the Dawn isn't the best fighter, the guy who took the most combat Charms is. It demotes Caste from being a vague analogue for classes to more of a minor role, from being a reflection of in-universe role (Dawns are fighters, Nights are thieves, etc) to more of a personality based thing (Dawns are direct and in-your-face, Nights are about subtlety, etc). I don't think that's a bad thing.<br /> <br /> (And saying &quot;all that's really diversifying characters is Charm choice&quot; is like saying &quot;all that's diversifying D&amp;D characters is class choice.&quot; Of course Charm choice is what diversifies characters; it's the mechanical meat and potatoes <i>of </i>your character)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12314,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","user":"Grod_the_giant","date":". 01-18-2020, 07:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T06:31:11-08:00","id":1361723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1361702#post1361702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry you feel that way. We're only capable of speaking in general terms and saying what could go wrong or drawing from our experiences of game groups that could be very different to yours.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, you know your group better than we know your group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry I din't mean to be rude or prevent your discussion, it just wasn't really answering my point, and going actually very far from my experiences at a table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T13:53:20-08:00","id":1361787,"title":"","content":"No offence taken. Good luck with whatever you decide to go for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T01:00:58-08:00","id":1361867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1361579#post1361579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> To me, definitely the most powerful (and flavourful) are Eclipse abilities..Diplomatic immunity and sanctifying oaths seem both examples of something that could be high-Essence charms. They are applicable in so many circumstances and guarantee that you essentially always get a chance to try getting things done in a diplomatic way.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I meant by my post is that the night power to not flare anima is very core to the &quot;I'm a shadow unseen&quot;, because it allows you to act discreetly where no other Caste could, literally because of their anima and the cost of Charms.<br /> <br /> Other powers, like the Twilight ones, are totally awesome, but not mandatory to play a diplomat. You can still try to convince ennemies to enforce their pacts and to not attack you with your Charms, excellencies, RP and merits. A non-Night Solar literally cannot use many abilities if he is on a stealth mission because his stealth will break. That's what I meant by &quot;The power is totally core to the concept&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T09:24:57-08:00","id":1361912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1361706#post1361706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it means that the Dawn isn't the best fighter, the guy who took the most combat Charms is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats untrue, the best fighter is the guy whose combat charms support each other. The different abilities do not support each other equally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T10:15:33-08:00","id":1361927,"title":"","content":"Best fighter doesn't necessarily make sense ? What do you mesure it with ? The ability to 1v1 ? To 1vBattle Group ? To 1vMore people ? Damage output per round ? Highest burst on first turns ? Defensive power ? I think it's better to think of Exalted characters as complementary in fights, even though some people will try to build characters that are the best in every situations","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":". 01-19-2020, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T11:05:50-08:00","id":1361933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1361867#post1361867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I meant by my post is that the night power to not flare anima is very core to the &quot;I'm a shadow unseen&quot;, because it allows you to act discreetly where no other Caste could, literally because of their anima and the cost of Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many of the Charms available are Mute, though - you can absolutely play a sneaky Zenith. Hell, I'm playing a sneaky Eclipse right now; I don't think Knight Raiton's anima has ever flared in a scene where he didn't want it to.<br /> <br /> Also, Sun-Swallowing Practice is a thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1361867#post1361867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other powers, like the Twilight ones, are totally awesome, but not mandatory to play a diplomat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming you mean Eclipse here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1361867#post1361867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can still try to convince ennemies to enforce their pacts and to not attack you with your Charms, excellencies, RP and merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds a lot like Special Pleading to me.<br /> <br /> Why can I not &quot;still try to remain unseen through my Charms, Excellencies, clever stunts, and Merits?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1361867#post1361867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A non-Night Solar literally cannot use many abilities if he is on a stealth mission because his stealth will break.</div> </div> </div> </div>And again, my Eclipse has done fine with stealth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-19-2020, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T11:56:23-08:00","id":1361940,"title":"","content":"I started typing an answer and then realized I was wrong, so mea culpa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T14:03:33-08:00","id":1361976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1361927#post1361927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Best fighter doesn't necessarily make sense ? What do you mesure it with ? The ability to 1v1 ? To 1vBattle Group ? To 1vMore people ? Damage output per round ? Highest burst on first turns ? Defensive power ? I think it's better to think of Exalted characters as complementary in fights, even though some people will try to build characters that are the best in every situations</div> </div> </div> </div>For the purpose of my answer any of those work, charms supporting each other to achieve an outcome is kinda system bedrock.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T15:39:12-08:00","id":1362005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1361912#post1361912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thats untrue, the best fighter is the guy whose combat charms support each other. The different abilities do not support each other equally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, yes, technically the &quot;best X&quot; will be the character who invested most heavily <i>and</i> most intelligently in Charms, Merits, Abilities, Attributes, Specialties, and Artifacts related to thing X, such that all parts of the build work together in support of accomplishing thing X. Better?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T09:05:03-08:00","id":1363094,"title":"","content":"I kinda want to come back to the idea of separating soak and the damage roll, because I'm trying to speed up combat and I feel like the current system is a both a source of confusion for my players and a cumbersome bit of mental math (base damage + threshold successes - soak is a bunch to keep track of when the numbers are constantly changing). &quot;I get 6 successes,&quot; &quot;okay, that's +2 damage from threshold, -8 from soak,&quot; &quot;so base damage -6&quot; is just a constant sticking point. I'm willing to trade a bit of exact balance for something easier for my group to wrap their heads around*.<br /> <br /> My current thought is &quot;the attacker rolls their total damage pool, the defender rolls dice equal to their soak, and threshold successes become damage,&quot; with your weapon's Overwhelming rating being the minimum amount of withering damage it can deal (Ie, if I hit you with a daiklave and you soak the entire thing, you still take 4 damage). <br /> <br /> <i>Previous Responses</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1349111#post1349111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... If you applied half your soak to successes on Withering damage rolls, instead of reducing the number of dice before rolling?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1349112#post1349112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certain Charms add or reduce damage after soak, so those would need to be adjusted bare minimum.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1349119#post1349119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Assuming this gets rid of overwhelming, high soak becomes incredibly powerful.<br /> <br /> Things that trigger off of taking no damage get either a boost or a penalty, depending on specifics.<br /> <br /> The probability curve of damage gets a lot wider, since more dice are being rolled</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> *I tried to get a group with just people I know are mechanically savvy. Social dynamics meant it didn't stay that way for long :/<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T09:25:34-08:00","id":1363098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1363094#post1363094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm willing to trade a bit of exact balance for something easier for my group to wrap their heads around*.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve had a lot of trouble with it in the past. The only way I kind of figured out how to do it easily without mental fatigue is to do it really procedurally and never try to shortcut it. I was always going \u201cwell my base damae is 12 and his soak is 8 so that\u2019s 4 damage, but I got 4 threshold successes so that\u2019s 8.\u201d Or \u201cokay so I rolled 4 successes that makes his soak effectively 4 so I take that away from 12 and get 8.\u201d And other stuff like that. I have to make a conscious effort to say \u201cmy base damage is 12, I got 4 threshold successes that\u2019s 16, the subtract soak of 8 and I\u2019m left with 8.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T10:47:51-08:00","id":1363120,"title":"","content":"Base + Threshold - Soak = Withering Damage [Minimum of Overwhelming] is how we do it, and it is procedurally easy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T04:57:08-08:00","id":1364732,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering about Double 9s and Double 8s in every ability for Solars (and why not other Exalted actually), and what consequences it could have. And your next line will be &quot;But it will break combat and social abilities !&quot; (Stares in Jojo). But I'd actually say there are already so much Charms which give other kind of dice tricks in these same abilities (reroll 1s, non Charm dices, etc ...) while the defense side usually get limited in the same way by the Dice Charm limitation with no tricks to go over it (maybe specifically in Dodge, I believe) so waddayathinkabout ?<br /> <br /> Basically my goal is remove most dice tricks Charms and replace them with a core simple dice trick Charm for every ability that always work the same way (I've spoken about in another thread)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T07:00:07-08:00","id":1364747,"title":"","content":"I mean... all rolls will be about 20% higher?<br /> <br /> I toyed with something similar a little while back... my thought was to add dice tricks to Excellencies as you bought Charms in that Ability. 5 War Charms? Get double 9s when you use an Excellence. 10 Charms? Double 9s and reroll 6s. And so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T08:00:51-08:00","id":1364755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1364732#post1364732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering about Double 9s and Double 8s in every ability for Solars (and why not other Exalted actually), and what consequences it could have. And your next line will be &amp;quot;But it will break combat and social abilities !&amp;quot; (Stares in Jojo). But I'd actually say there are already so much Charms which give other kind of dice tricks in these same abilities (reroll 1s, non Charm dices, etc ...) while the defense side usually get limited in the same way by the Dice Charm limitation with no tricks to go over it (maybe specifically in Dodge, I believe) so waddayathinkabout ?<br /> <br /> Basically my goal is remove most dice tricks Charms and replace them with a core simple dice trick Charm for every ability that always work the same way (I've spoken about in another thread)</div> </div> </div> </div>So do you mean like get rid of Excellent Strike, and Rising Sun Slash from Solar Melee and just replace them with two charms that give double 9s and double 8s?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T08:41:13-08:00","id":1364762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1364755#post1364755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So do you mean like get rid of Excellent Strike, and Rising Sun Slash from Solar Melee and just replace them with two charms that give double 9s and double 8s?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be the core idea I guess. Excellent Strike for sure, Rising Sun Strike I could consider keeping it because it is fun on paper ... but in practice, when we are 2 hours in a 4-5 hours session, I don't think this keeps the same fun.<br /> <br /> It could be a little different that just buying Charms (I like Grod's idea to unlock simple Charm Dice tricks effects when you have X Charms in an ability for example), but yeah the purpose would be to get rid of most Charms that are too focused on dice tricks. After few years of Solar's campaign, I don't think they are that healthy for my Exalted playstyle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T11:15:26-08:00","id":1364790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1364762#post1364762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be the core idea I guess. Excellent Strike for sure, Rising Sun Strike I could consider keeping it because it is fun on paper ... but in practice, when we are 2 hours in a 4-5 hours session, I don't think this keeps the same fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might not actually end up simplifying much, depending on the charm tree. The only Melee charm out of the 48 that's a dice trick is Excellent Strike, Brawl has 2 for excellency-able rolls and 2 for damage, Socialize has 4 I think, Presence has 2-3. It will be simpler overall most of the time, except maybe for some trees like Melee, but I don't think it's going to drastically simplify things. Also if you go down to double 8s you're going to really boost the power of some trees by a lot.<br /> <br /> It's not really broken, exactly, the game's still going to run, but Solars are just going to be that much more powerful than they currently are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T11:50:52-08:00","id":1364798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1364732#post1364732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering about Double 9s and Double 8s in every ability for Solars (and why not other Exalted actually), and what consequences it could have. And your next line will be &quot;But it will break combat and social abilities !&quot; (Stares in Jojo). But I'd actually say there are already so much Charms which give other kind of dice tricks in these same abilities (reroll 1s, non Charm dices, etc ...) while the defense side usually get limited in the same way by the Dice Charm limitation with no tricks to go over it (maybe specifically in Dodge, I believe) so waddayathinkabout ?<br /> <br /> Basically my goal is remove most dice tricks Charms and replace them with a core simple dice trick Charm for every ability that always work the same way (I've spoken about in another thread)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you'd be better served looking at why certain trees are full of bizarre dice tricks *COUGHCRAFTCOUGH* and what can be done to rework systems so those dice tricks aren't necessary *COUGHCRAFTCOUGH* instead of fiddling with the math. Because as DrLoveMonkey points out, a bunch of trees don't really have many dice tricks. <br /> <br /> Craft, just to introduce an example, is full of dice tricks so that Essence and Exalt type can be used to gate various Artifact dot levels. Can you rework the tree to remove dice tricks without touching the subsystem it interacts with? What about changing the subsystem so the dice tricks aren't needed? (Hint: The answers are no and yes.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T12:05:57-08:00","id":1364805,"title":"","content":"Yeah I guess there are many that include dice tricks in them, but only few are literal only dice-tricks for combat, so I might as well leave them be. I'll keep my plan for social and other Abilities I guess, it's just when I pass over some of them I wish they didn't exactly as they are because they are really more about the combat mini-game than the cinematic of combat and fun combat options, so I was trying to think of ideas to clear them up. I guess it's not easily doable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T12:08:31-08:00","id":1364806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1364798#post1364798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you'd be better served looking at why certain trees are full of bizarre dice tricks *COUGHCRAFTCOUGH* and what can be done to rework systems so those dice tricks aren't necessary *COUGHCRAFTCOUGH* instead of fiddling with the math. Because as DrLoveMonkey points out, a bunch of trees don't really have many dice tricks.<br /> <br /> Craft, just to introduce an example, is full of dice tricks so that Essence and Exalt type can be used to gate various Artifact dot levels. Can you rework the tree to remove dice tricks without touching the subsystem it interacts with? What about changing the subsystem so the dice tricks aren't needed? (Hint: The answers are no and yes.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you see I'm doing a Thesis in Mathematics and even I am not crazy enough to try to play with this thing that is the Craft system <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T12:22:46-08:00","id":1364813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1364805#post1364805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I guess there are many that include dice tricks in them, but only few are literal only dice-tricks for combat, so I might as well leave them be. I'll keep my plan for social and other Abilities I guess, it's just when I pass over some of them I wish they didn't exactly as they are because they are really more about the combat mini-game than the cinematic of combat and fun combat options, so I was trying to think of ideas to clear them up. I guess it's not easily doable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, part of the reason there's SO many dice trick charms is just because there's 25 abilities and like 20 martial arts trees. Even if every tree only has 2 dice trick charms that's still over 80 in the game, which is a big number.<br /> <br /> There's also just a bunch of charms that aren't dice tricks but are maybe kind of fiddly anyway. Like Protection of Celestial Bliss, which gives you this other pool of initiative to draw on for the purposes of Heavenly Guardian Defense and has a bunch of extra rules and motes and stuff attached to it.<br /> <br /> Exalted Essence might be more what you're looking for what that comes out in a year or so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T12:34:24-08:00","id":1364818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1364806#post1364806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well you see I'm doing a Thesis in Mathematics and even I am not crazy enough to try to play with this thing that is the Craft system <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I can't blame you! To be totally honest, my rework started by taking a step to the side and starting fresh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T12:36:08-08:00","id":1364819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1364813#post1364813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, part of the reason there's SO many dice trick charms is just because there's 25 abilities and like 20 martial arts trees. Even if every tree only has 2 dice trick charms that's still over 80 in the game, which is a big number.<br /> <br /> There's also just a bunch of charms that aren't dice tricks but are maybe kind of fiddly anyway. Like Protection of Celestial Bliss, which gives you this other pool of initiative to draw on for the purposes of Heavenly Guardian Defense and has a bunch of extra rules and motes and stuff attached to it.<br /> <br /> Exalted Essence might be more what you're looking for what that comes out in a year or so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that coming so soon ? I recalled in Wizard of Oz it was in its early days.<br /> <br /> Yeah and also there are lots of Charms that are not directly classical dice tricks but contains them : For example, Melee has Excellent Strike, Bulwark Stance, Rising Sun Slash, Agile Dragonfly Blade, Hail-Shattering Practice (only went up to Essence 2, and I didn't even include those that increase damage) And I think Melee is one with the lowest count, compared to Brawl. They are not bad per-se, but I think they focus way too much on the combat mini-game and not on the options of combat that seems much more interesting to me (for a simple example that has good design to me : War Lion Stance).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":". 02-02-2020, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T14:04:05-08:00","id":1364839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1364819#post1364819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah and also there are lots of Charms that are not directly classical dice tricks but contains them : For example, Melee has Excellent Strike, Bulwark Stance, Rising Sun Slash, Agile Dragonfly Blade, Hail-Shattering Practice (only went up to Essence 2, and I didn't even include those that increase damage) And I think Melee is one with the lowest count, compared to Brawl. They are not bad per-se, but I think they focus way too much on the combat mini-game and not on the options of combat that seems much more interesting to me (for a simple example that has good design to me : War Lion Stance).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's certainly true. You could probably prune every tree by about half and still have a tremendously rich spread of abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T14:29:54-08:00","id":1364845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1364839#post1364839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's certainly true. You could probably prune every tree by about half and still have a tremendously rich spread of abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah if you just want to ditch the dice trick charms all together and not replace them with anything I think it still mostly works. Maybe have a defensive equivalent of the double 9s charm just to keep the balance a bit if you\u2019re ditching Bulwer Stance and Hail Shattering and stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T02:56:34-08:00","id":1364976,"title":"","content":"I don't see simple tricks to augment Defense that are statistically equivalent to Double 9s for the defender to use. Static Defense increase ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T06:00:30-08:00","id":1364992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1364976#post1364976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see simple tricks to augment Defense that are statistically equivalent to Double 9s for the defender to use. Static Defense increase ?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could just counter the doubles, make the enemy lose double 10s for example.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not exactly going to be one-to-one anyway. Bulwark Stance reduces damage with its dice trick rather than make you harder to hit, so it\u2019s going to be pretty generalized no matter what.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 02-03-2020, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T06:33:58-08:00","id":1364997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1364992#post1364992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could just counter the doubles, make the enemy lose double 10s for example.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not exactly going to be one-to-one anyway. Bulwark Stance reduces damage with its dice trick rather than make you harder to hit, so it\u2019s going to be pretty generalized no matter what.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, that's definitely annoying.<br /> <br /> Also, oh my god, I just happened to reread a little of Awareness, and are you sure guys we got enough Charms about detecting hidden characters ? I believe we clearly don't have enough of them Charms detecting hidden characters. Maybe we should do more Charms about detecting hidden characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T07:01:19-08:00","id":1365002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1364997#post1364997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, that's definitely annoying.<br /> <br /> Also, oh my god, I just happened to reread a little of Awareness, and are you sure guys we got enough Charms about detecting hidden characters ? I believe we clearly don't have enough of them Charms detecting hidden characters. Maybe we should do more Charms about detecting hidden characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find DB Awareness and Lunar Perception be better in that regard... on the other hand you\u2019re not sneaking up on an awareness Solar I guess?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T07:44:53-08:00","id":1365007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1365002#post1365002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find DB Awareness and Lunar Perception be better in that regard... on the other hand you\u2019re not sneaking up on an awareness Solar I guess?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but at that point just make a Charm that says &quot;You see people&quot;. I mean, I get the idea, they want to be some sort of contest between the Solar awareness and the Solar stealthy guy in the Circle when they disagree or whatnot, but here having like 5 Charms that circumstantials bonuses and dice tricks to see hidden characters ... What bothers me is meanwhile we don't get more cool Charms like the one that allows you to make an olfactive library, or a Charm that allows you to hear your interlocutor's thoughts because your hearing is so perfect (maybe he is in Socialize though), or one that allows you to see in perpendicular directions because you master the reflection of the light on thin air (ok maybe this one is useless I don't know), etc ... like real cool effects that says something about the narration going on in the game.<br /> <br /> Anyway enough ranting I think I got some good ideas thanks to this discussion. I think the safest play for the moment is to not touch combat abilities, and I'll see after a little practice in other abilities if I can apply my ideas to the fighting mechanics. I think for the moment they have too many things going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T16:38:29-08:00","id":1365133,"title":"","content":"There's an Awareness charm that increases your hearing so well that you can hear ants walking outside of your house\u2026 but its the charm after that that gives you bonus dice to hear a character moving in stealth. Ants are louder than thieves I guess. <br /> <br /> Larceny has charms that just straight up say &quot;No&quot;: If you don't have magic that boosts your vision its just impossible to notice the slight of hand. I wish Stealth and Awareness had more of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T17:12:32-08:00","id":1365144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1365133#post1365133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's an Awareness charm that increases your hearing so well that you can hear ants walking outside of your house\u2026 but its the charm after that that gives you bonus dice to hear a character moving in stealth. Ants are louder than thieves I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I read the Keen Hearing and Touch flavour text to mean that it somewhat expands what the ST might be willing to allow a roll for, but mostly it\u2019s the autosuccesses and difficulty manipulation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T01:22:38-08:00","id":1365190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1365144#post1365144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I read the Keen Hearing and Touch flavour text to mean that it somewhat expands what the ST might be willing to allow a roll for, but mostly it\u2019s the autosuccesses and difficulty manipulation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm usually open to accept the core ideas of the Keen sense techniques, like counting fast big groups, see at 100 yards, feel things through the earth vibration, etc ... without a roll, when basically someone is not trying to contest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Larceny has charms that just straight up say &quot;No&quot;: If you don't have magic that boosts your vision its just impossible to notice the slight of hand. I wish Stealth and Awareness had more of that. </div> </div> </div>Thank you that was exactly the kind of thing I was talking about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T01:23:03-08:00","id":1365191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1365144#post1365144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I read the Keen Hearing and Touch flavour text to mean that it somewhat expands what the ST might be willing to allow a roll for, but mostly it\u2019s the autosuccesses and difficulty manipulation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <i><b>&quot;These benefits do not apply to detecting opponents in stealth&quot;</b></i><br /> <br /> It's just such a mood whiplash to go from being Daredevil to it not working on stealth because Game Balance. It's completely a conceit of the mechanics. You can hear animals burrowing underground, conversations through stone walls, ants on a branch, and things below human auditory spectrum, but it gives you no bonus at all on hearing a maid sneak up to your door with a knife in hand, something orders of magnitude louder than hearing a mouse underground. <br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I LOVE the spirit of the Awareness line and I'm taking them on my character, but there are some real brick walls in that tree. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T04:20:25-08:00","id":1365217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1365191#post1365191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <i><b>&quot;These benefits do not apply to detecting opponents in stealth&quot;</b></i><br /> <br /> It's just such a mood whiplash to go from being Daredevil to it not working on stealth because Game Balance. It's completely a conceit of the mechanics. You can hear animals burrowing underground, conversations through stone walls, ants on a branch, and things below human auditory spectrum, but it gives you no bonus at all on hearing a maid sneak up to your door with a knife in hand, something orders of magnitude louder than hearing a mouse underground.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I LOVE the spirit of the Awareness line and I'm taking them on my character, but there are some real brick walls in that tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually fine with the mechanics sometimes confronting the narrative power, but I think Awareness missed some good ideas by going too far with &quot;dice tricks to stealthing character&quot; thing. Whatever I guess just invent some Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T04:35:08-08:00","id":1365222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1365217#post1365217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm actually fine with the mechanics sometimes confronting the narrative power, but I think Awareness missed some good ideas by going too far with &amp;quot;dice tricks to stealthing character&amp;quot; thing. Whatever I guess just invent some Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>The other issue with that is who cares? Are there any antagonists in the game aside from other Solars who specialize in stealth that can even remotely require those kind of insane awareness rolls? A really awesome sneaky enemy might have 11 dice and double 9s to their sneak, and most just have 7-8. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s the same problem with Sail. A Solar sailor takes like 4 charms and can absolutely roll any opposition, then has 20 charms that don\u2019t really help because they always win anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T05:21:26-08:00","id":1365228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1365222#post1365222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The other issue with that is who cares? Are there any antagonists in the game aside from other Solars who specialize in stealth that can even remotely require those kind of insane awareness rolls? A really awesome sneaky enemy might have 11 dice and double 9s to their sneak, and most just have 7-8.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s the same problem with Sail. A Solar sailor takes like 4 charms and can absolutely roll any opposition, then has 20 charms that don\u2019t really help because they always win anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I guess this was my intent behind &quot;Take every Dice tricks Charms and fuse them into one, keep the other fun Charms that allows for real new ways of playing&quot;.<br /> <br /> For the moment, my current version is this one :<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Solar mastery </span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence : 1 (Repurchase at 2 and 3). Abilities : Basically all that makes sense</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost : 3m</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You gain Double 9 on the roll. (Permanent) You get one free Full Excellency once per scene.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Repurchase (Essence 2) : You gain (Essence) non-Charm dices on the roll. (Permanent) You can double 8s once per scene.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Repurchase (Essence 3) : (Permanent) This Charm is now free of motes</span></span><br /> <br /> I believe it to be simple enough and express the power of the Solars in a simple way. My only problem is that that there is no &quot;reroll 1s&quot; or &quot;cascading 10s&quot; that seem rather core to the Solar powers in the existing Charms, but I find them too annoying from an ergonomic point of view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T05:58:32-08:00","id":1365233,"title":"","content":"Assuming you could prune enough charms from the tree I think that would be okay. You\u2019re going to flatten out a lot of the power that Solars have in particular, but I don\u2019t think it would break much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T06:25:20-08:00","id":1365238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1365233#post1365233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming you could prune enough charms from the tree I think that would be okay. You\u2019re going to flatten out a lot of the power that Solars have in particular, but I don\u2019t think it would break much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I think the real complexity comes when deciding how to handle Charms where the narrative effect comes with a dice trick. I'll see case by case I guess","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-10T15:02:26-08:00","id":1435108,"title":"","content":"What breaks if I remove the ability to stunt static values, and reduce the stunt bonuses to 1-2-3 dice?<br /> <br /> I sometimes find it a bit tedious to say &quot;Okay this is the stunted attack, how are you stunting your defense *listens to defensive stunt* okay that's a level one stunt, now what defensive charms/willpower are you spending?&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd much rather &quot;The bladebeak sweeps at you high overhead, feathers shimmering in the noonday sun, what's your defense?&quot; &quot;I'll boost it by 3 with 6 motes, that makes 10&quot;<br /> <br /> I feel it should also help ever so slightly at making lower difficulty rolls more challenging if the stunt bonus is halved. Like a difficulty 3 lock is not quite as easily picked by somebody with 2 Dex and no larceny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-10T21:02:24-08:00","id":1435149,"title":"","content":"IMO it breaks the narrative and imagery of the fight which defense stunts are a deceptively key connective tissue for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-10T21:58:43-08:00","id":1435155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1435149#post1435149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMO it breaks the narrative and imagery of the fight which defense stunts are a deceptively key connective tissue for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay I think I see what you mean, what if it goes like this though. I stunt the attack, and just roll as I'm stunting, they give me their defense, I tell them if it hits, and then they get to describe the result.<br /> <br /> That even gives them more leeway because you get to describe an action knowing you succeeded at it &quot;I reach up and catch the mighty hammer blow with my bare hands, turning it aside and cracking the pavement with its redirected force.&quot; Which I guess you could still do with a stunted defense, but it's a lot more awkward to word and if you get hit anyway it's kind of a wasted stunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T00:42:19-08:00","id":1435160,"title":"","content":"I think you'd have to give the applicabilty of stunts to the static values: i.e. even though you're not giving a stunt bonus, and they're not describing the stunt until after the dice are rolled, you can still block lethal attacks with your Brawl based parry and Lunars still get to boost their Defense with a second attribute.<br /> <br /> One idea I'm toying with is to use Essence's system of Stunts being a flat yes/no. Then you could just perma-bump static values by 1 so long as you trust your players to describe their stunts after the roll. (This is basically what my homebrewed RPG system does, but I'm not sure how applicable it is to Exalted.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T06:00:02-08:00","id":1435180,"title":"","content":"Ah true I forgot about Lunars and lethal blocks I had a nagging feeling something keyed off a stunted defence. None of my players are Lunars right now, but that might just be something I\u2019d have to do later. Should work if I just trust my players to stunt it post roll.<br /> <br /> I think changing to a binary stunt system would be better, but players might feel like they\u2019re being robbed of the chance to regain willpower from a level two stunt and stuff. It would be a lot easier if I didn\u2019t have to decide what constituted various stunt levels though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T07:48:56-08:00","id":1435195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1435108#post1435108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sometimes find it a bit tedious to say &amp;quot;Okay this is the stunted attack, how are you stunting your defense *listens to defensive stunt* okay that's a level one stunt, now what defensive charms/willpower are you spending?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This sort of thing is exactly why I've switched over to a &quot;players roll all the dice&quot; variant--it makes this kind of exchange way smoother, and makes defensive stunts more natural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T10:06:20-08:00","id":1435213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1435195#post1435195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sort of thing is exactly why I've switched over to a &amp;quot;players roll all the dice&amp;quot; variant--it makes this kind of exchange way smoother, and makes defensive stunts more natural.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn\u2019t that just mean you stunt the NPCs attack to raise the difficulty, then the PC stunts their defence to get bonus dice and you still have to go through that step?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T10:51:11-08:00","id":1435223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/849576-what-breaks-if?p=1435213#post1435213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn\u2019t that just mean you stunt the NPCs attack to raise the difficulty, then the PC stunts their defence to get bonus dice and you still have to go through that step?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of? It doesn't do all that much to speed up resolution, but in my experience it's more intuitive to add stunts and charms to an active roll than a passive value.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}